/* Student's Book va Workbook audiolari: audio/a2/student, audio/a2/workbook.
   Dars: { id, u, book, title, dur (soniya), audio, lines: [[kim, inglizcha, oʻzbekcha, soniya], ...], q (ixtiyoriy): [{ t, o, a, why }] }
   Matnlar audiodan avtomatik chiqarilgan (xato boʻlishi mumkin). Savollar (q) va oʻzbekcha tarjima hozircha 1–6-unitlarda bor;
   qolganlarida q yoʻq — sahifa ularni savolsiz koʻrsatadi. q qoʻshilsa, sahifa oʻzi savollarni chiqaradi. */
var AUDIO_LESSONS = [
{"id":"sb-01","u":1,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Daily Routines and Habits","dur":131,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-01.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Good morning. I'm doing a survey about people's daily routines. Could I ask you a few questions?","Xayrli tong. Men odamlarning kundalik tartibi boʻyicha soʻrovnoma oʻtkazyapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",5.4],["Sophie","Sure.","Albatta.",11.5],["Interviewer","Great. First, can I have your name?","Zoʻr. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",13.3],["Sophie","Yes, it's Sophie Carter.","Ha, men Sophie Carter.",17.5],["Interviewer","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",19.7],["Sophie","Sure. It's C-A-R-T-E-R.","Albatta. C-A-R-T-E-R.",23.5],["Interviewer","Thank you. Now, let's talk about your mornings. What time do you usually get up?","Rahmat. Endi ertalablaringiz haqida gaplashaylik. Odatda soat nechada turasiz?",27.9],["Sophie","Quite early. My alarm goes off at 6, but I don't get up immediately. I usually stay in bed for another 15 minutes, so I get up at 6.15. Then I have a shower and get dressed.","Ancha erta. Budilnik 6 da chaladi, lekin darrov turmayman. Odatda yana 15 daqiqa yotaman, shuning uchun 6.15 da turaman. Keyin dushga tushaman va kiyinaman.",34],["Interviewer","Do you have breakfast at home?","Nonushtani uyda qilasizmi?",48],["Sophie","Yes, always. I usually have some cereal and a banana. I used to drink coffee in the morning, but these days I prefer tea.","Ha, doim. Odatda bir oz quruq nonushta (kornfleks) va banan yeyman. Ilgari ertalab kofe ichardim, hozir esa choyni afzal koʻraman.",51],["Interviewer","And what time do you leave home?","Uydan soat nechada chiqasiz?",60.2],["Sophie","At about 7.20. I work at a bookshop in the town centre, and I normally go there by bus.","Taxminan 7.20 da. Men shahar markazidagi kitob doʻkonida ishlayman, odatda avtobusda boraman.",62.5],["Interviewer","Is it a long journey?","Yoʻl uzoqmi?",69.7],["Sophie","Not really. It usually takes about 30 minutes. I sometimes listen to music on the bus, but I often just look out of the window.","Unchalik emas. Odatda taxminan 30 daqiqa ketadi. Baʼzan avtobusda musiqa tinglayman, lekin koʻpincha oynadan tashqariga qarab ketaman.",72],["Interviewer","What happens after work?","Ishdan keyin nima qilasiz?",81.1],["Sophie","I finish at half past four. On Tuesdays, I go swimming at the sports centre. I swim for about an hour, so I normally get home just after six.","Soat toʻrt yarimda tugataman. Seshanba kunlari sport markazida suzishga boraman. Taxminan bir soat suzaman, shuning uchun uyga odatda oltidan sal oʻtib qaytaman.",83.5],["Interviewer","What do you do in the evening?","Kechqurun nima qilasiz?",93],["Sophie","I make dinner first. I really enjoy cooking, especially pasta and soup. After dinner, I usually watch TV or talk to my friends online.","Avval kechki ovqat tayyorlayman. Ovqat pishirishni juda yaxshi koʻraman, ayniqsa pasta va shoʻrva. Ovqatdan keyin odatda televizor koʻraman yoki doʻstlarim bilan onlayn gaplashaman.",96.1],["Interviewer","And what time do you normally go to bed?","Odatda soat nechada uxlaysiz?",107],["Sophie","Around 10.45. Before I sleep, I usually read for about 20 minutes. It helps me relax.","Taxminan 10.45 da. Uxlashdan oldin odatda 20 daqiqa kitob oʻqiyman. Bu dam olishimga yordam beradi.",110.5],["Interviewer","One last question. Are weekends different?","Oxirgi savol. Dam olish kunlari boshqachami?",118.5],["Sophie","Very different. On Saturdays, I don't use an alarm. I usually wake up around nine and meet my friends for breakfast.","Juda boshqacha. Shanba kunlari budilnik qoʻymayman. Odatda toʻqqizlarda uygʻonaman va doʻstlarim bilan nonushta qilish uchun uchrashaman.",122.2]],"q":[{"t":"What time does Sophie get up?","o":["6:00","6:15","7:20"],"a":1,"why":"Budilnik 6 da chaladi, u 15 daqiqadan keyin, 6.15 da turadi."},{"t":"What does Sophie usually have for breakfast?","o":["Toast and tea","Cereal and a banana","Only coffee"],"a":1},{"t":"How does Sophie get to work?","o":["By bus","By car","On foot"],"a":0},{"t":"What does Sophie do on Tuesdays after work?","o":["She plays tennis","She cooks for friends","She goes swimming"],"a":2},{"t":"What is different about Saturdays?","o":["She works at the bookshop","She doesn't use an alarm","She goes to bed early"],"a":1,"why":"On Saturdays, I don't use an alarm."}]},
{"id":"sb-02","u":2,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Family, Friends and Relationships","dur":131,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-02.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hi, I'm collecting information for a class project about families and friendships. Can I ask you a few questions?","Salom, men oila va doʻstlik haqidagi sinf loyihasi uchun maʼlumot yigʻyapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",6],["Lucy","Sure, that sounds interesting.","Albatta, qiziq ekan.",13.8],["Interviewer","Great! First, could you tell me your name?","Zoʻr! Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",16.6],["Lucy","My name's Lucy Bennett.","Ismim Lucy Bennett.",20.6],["Interviewer","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23.3],["Lucy","Yes, it's B-E-N-N-E-T-T.","Ha, B-E-N-N-E-T-T.",25.1],["Interviewer","Thanks. So, Lucy, do you have a big family?","Rahmat. Xoʻsh, Lucy, oilangiz kattami?",32.6],["Lucy","Not really. There are four people in my family. My parents, my younger brother and me. My brother's name is Jack. He's 15, so he's three years younger than I am.","Unchalik emas. Oilamizda toʻrt kishi: ota-onam, kichik ukam va men. Ukamning ismi Jack. U 15 yoshda, demak mendan uch yosh kichik.",37.5],["Interviewer","Do you spend much time together?","Birga koʻp vaqt oʻtkazasizlarmi?",50.2],["Lucy","Yes, especially at weekends. Jack and I sometimes argue about small things, but we're actually quite close. We both love films, so we usually watch one together on Friday evenings.","Ha, ayniqsa dam olish kunlari. Jack bilan baʼzan mayda narsalar uchun tortishamiz, lekin aslida juda yaqinmiz. Ikkimiz ham kinoni yaxshi koʻramiz, shuning uchun odatda juma kechqurunlari birga film koʻramiz.",52.6],["Interviewer","What about your parents?","Ota-onangiz-chi?",66.2],["Lucy","My mum works at a hospital, and my dad is a bus driver. They're both busy during the week. We always try to have dinner together at about 7.30.","Onam kasalxonada ishlaydi, dadam avtobus haydovchisi. Ikkalasi ham hafta davomida band. Biz doim soat 7.30 atrofida birga kechki ovqat yeyishga harakat qilamiz.",68.6],["Interviewer","Do any other relatives live near you?","Yaqin atrofda boshqa qarindoshlaringiz yashaydimi?",79.1],["Lucy","My grandmother does. She lives about 10 minutes away, so I visit her every Wednesday after college. We usually have tea and talk for an hour or two.","Buvim yashaydi. U taxminan 10 daqiqalik masofada yashaydi, shuning uchun har chorshanba kollejdan keyin uning oldiga boraman. Odatda choy ichib, bir-ikki soat gaplashamiz.",82.1],["Interviewer","And what about your friends? Who are you closest to?","Doʻstlaringiz-chi? Kim bilan eng yaqinsiz?",92.4],["Lucy","My best friend is Emma. We met at primary school when we were seven. She's friendly and really funny. We don't study at the same college now, but we still see each other regularly.","Eng yaqin doʻstim Emma. Biz yetti yoshimizda boshlangʻich maktabda tanishganmiz. U xushmuomala va juda quvnoq. Hozir bir kollejda oʻqimaymiz, lekin hamon muntazam koʻrishib turamiz.",96.5],["Interviewer","When do you normally meet?","Odatda qachon uchrashasizlar?",108.8],["Lucy","Usually on Saturdays. We often go shopping or meet at a café called Corner. Sometimes we just walk around town and talk.","Odatda shanba kunlari. Koʻpincha xarid qilgani boramiz yoki Corner nomli kafeda uchrashamiz. Baʼzan shunchaki shaharda aylanib gaplashamiz.",110.1],["Interviewer","How often do you speak during the week?","Hafta davomida qanchalik tez-tez gaplashasizlar?",120.6],["Lucy","Almost every day. We usually send messages, and we have a longer phone call on Thursday evenings.","Deyarli har kuni. Odatda xabar yozishamiz, payshanba kechqurunlari esa uzoqroq telefonda gaplashamiz.",123.8]],"q":[{"t":"How old is Lucy's brother?","o":["12","15","18"],"a":1,"why":"Jack 15 yoshda, Lucy'dan uch yosh kichik."},{"t":"What do Lucy and Jack usually do on Friday evenings?","o":["They go shopping.","They have dinner with their grandmother.","They watch a film."],"a":2},{"t":"What does Lucy's father do?","o":["He is a bus driver.","He works at a hospital.","He is a teacher."],"a":0},{"t":"When does Lucy visit her grandmother?","o":["On Saturdays","On Wednesdays","On Thursdays"],"a":1},{"t":"When do Lucy and Emma have a longer phone call?","o":["On Thursday evenings","On Friday evenings","On Saturday mornings"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"sb-03","u":3,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Hobbies and free time","dur":123,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-03.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hi. I'm doing a survey about how people spend their free time. Could I ask you a few questions?","Salom. Men odamlar boʻsh vaqtini qanday oʻtkazishi boʻyicha soʻrovnoma oʻtkazyapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",4.5],["Anna","Of course.","Albatta.",11.6],["Interviewer","Great. First, what's your name?","Zoʻr. Avval ismingiz nima?",13.2],["Anna","My name's Anna Wilson.","Ismim Anna Wilson.",16.4],["Interviewer","Could you spell your surname for me?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",19.1],["Anna","Sure. It's W-I-L-S-O-N.","Albatta. W-I-L-S-O-N.",21.8],["Interviewer","Thanks. So, Anna, what do you like doing in your free time?","Rahmat. Xoʻsh, Anna, boʻsh vaqtingizda nima qilishni yoqtirasiz?",27.4],["Anna","I have several hobbies, but my favourite is photography. I started about two years ago when my parents gave me a camera for my birthday. I usually take pictures of buildings, streets and people.","Mening bir nechta xobbim bor, lekin eng yaxshi koʻrganim fotografiya. Taxminan ikki yil oldin tugʻilgan kunimga ota-onam menga kamera sovgʻa qilganda boshlaganman. Odatda binolar, koʻchalar va odamlarni suratga olaman.",32.8],["Interviewer","When do you normally have time for photography?","Fotografiya uchun odatda qachon vaqtingiz boʻladi?",46.6],["Anna","Mostly at the weekend. On Saturday mornings, I usually walk around the town centre with my camera. I sometimes spend two or three hours outside if the weather is nice.","Asosan dam olish kunlari. Shanba kuni ertalab odatda kamera bilan shahar markazida aylanaman. Ob-havo yaxshi boʻlsa, baʼzan tashqarida ikki-uch soat oʻtkazaman.",49.9],["Interviewer","Do you prefer doing things outside?","Tashqarida shugʻullanishni afzal koʻrasizmi?",61.3],["Anna","Not always. During the week, I often stay at home after work. I enjoy reading, especially adventure stories. I normally read for about 30 minutes before dinner.","Har doim emas. Hafta davomida koʻpincha ishdan keyin uyda qolaman. Kitob oʻqishni yaxshi koʻraman, ayniqsa sarguzasht hikoyalarini. Odatda kechki ovqatdan oldin taxminan 30 daqiqa oʻqiyman.",64.5],["Interviewer","Do you have any hobbies that you do with other people?","Boshqalar bilan birga qiladigan xobbilaringiz bormi?",76.9],["Anna","Yes. My friend Chloe and I go to a dance class together. We used to go on Tuesdays, but the class moved to Thursday this month. It starts at seven in the evening.","Ha. Doʻstim Chloe bilan birga raqs darsiga qatnaymiz. Avval seshanba kunlari borardik, lekin bu oy dars payshanbaga koʻchdi. U kechqurun soat yettida boshlanadi.",80.3],["Interviewer","That sounds busy. Do you have time to relax?","Band ekansiz. Dam olishga vaqtingiz bormi?",91.8],["Anna","Definitely. I don't like planning every minute of my free time. Some evenings, I just listen to music or watch something online.","Albatta. Boʻsh vaqtimning har daqiqasini rejalashtirishni yoqtirmayman. Baʼzi kechqurunlari shunchaki musiqa tinglayman yoki internetda biror narsa koʻraman.",96.1],["Interviewer","Is there anything new you'd like to try?","Yangi sinab koʻrmoqchi boʻlgan narsangiz bormi?",105.3],["Anna","Yes, actually. I'd really like to learn painting. There's an art club near my house, and I'm thinking about joining it next month.","Ha, aslida bor. Rasm chizishni juda oʻrganmoqchiman. Uyim yaqinida sanʼat klubi bor, kelasi oy unga aʼzo boʻlish haqida oʻylayapman.",108.3],["Interviewer","Sounds good. Thanks for answering my questions.","Yaxshi ekan. Savollarimga javob berganingiz uchun rahmat.",117.8],["Anna","You're welcome.","Arzimaydi.",121.3]],"q":[{"t":"How did Anna start photography?","o":["She bought a camera herself.","Her parents gave her a camera.","Her friend Chloe taught her."],"a":1},{"t":"When does Anna usually take photos in the town centre?","o":["On Saturday mornings","On Sunday evenings","On Tuesday afternoons"],"a":0},{"t":"How long does Anna normally read before dinner?","o":["About 15 minutes","About an hour","About 30 minutes"],"a":2},{"t":"Which day is Anna's dance class now?","o":["Tuesday","Thursday","Saturday"],"a":1,"why":"Dars avval seshanba edi, hozir payshanbaga koʻchgan."},{"t":"What would Anna like to learn?","o":["Painting","Dancing","Photography"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"sb-04","u":4,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Food, Cooking and Eating","dur":124,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-04.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hello. I'm doing a survey about people's eating and cooking habits. Would you mind answering a few questions?","Salom. Men odamlarning ovqatlanish va ovqat pishirish odatlari boʻyicha soʻrovnoma oʻtkazyapman. Bir nechta savolga javob berolmaysizmi?",5.4],["Emily","Not at all.","Mayli, marhamat.",12.5],["Interviewer","Great. Could I have your name first?","Zoʻr. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",14.1],["Emily","Sure. I'm Emily Clark.","Albatta. Men Emily Clark.",17.3],["Interviewer","And how do you spell your surname?","Familiyangiz qanday yoziladi?",20.1],["Emily","It's C-L-A-R-K.","C-L-A-R-K.",22.6],["Interviewer","Thank you. Let's start with breakfast. What do you normally eat in the morning?","Rahmat. Nonushtadan boshlaylik. Odatda ertalab nima yeysiz?",26.6],["Emily","On work days, I need something quick. I used to have cereal every morning, but now I usually have yogurt with some fruit. I also drink tea, but I never have coffee.","Ish kunlari menga tez tayyor boʻladigan narsa kerak. Ilgari har ertalab quruq nonushta (kornfleks) yerdim, hozir esa odatda meva bilan yogurt yeyman. Choy ham ichaman, lekin kofe hech ichmayman.",31.9],["Interviewer","What about lunch?","Tushlik-chi?",43.9],["Emily","I work in an office, so I take my lunch with me. I normally make a sandwich at home. Sometimes I take soup instead, especially when the weather is cold.","Men idorada ishlayman, shuning uchun tushlikni oʻzim bilan olib boraman. Odatda uyda sendvich tayyorlayman. Baʼzan, ayniqsa havo sovuq boʻlganda, uning oʻrniga shoʻrva olaman.",45.8],["Interviewer","Do you enjoy cooking?","Ovqat pishirishni yoqtirasizmi?",56.8],["Emily","Yes, very much. I usually cook dinner at around seven o'clock. I don't make anything difficult during the week because I'm tired after work. Pasta is probably the easiest thing for me to make.","Ha, juda. Odatda kechki ovqatni soat yetti atrofida pishiraman. Hafta davomida murakkab narsa pishirmayman, chunki ishdan keyin charchagan boʻlaman. Makaron men uchun eng oson ovqat boʻlsa kerak.",59],["Interviewer","Do you cook every day?","Har kuni pishirasizmi?",72.6],["Emily","Almost. But on Friday evenings, I usually eat out with my sister. There's a small restaurant near her apartment that we both like.","Deyarli. Lekin juma kechqurunlari odatda opam bilan tashqarida ovqatlanaman. Uning kvartirasi yaqinida ikkimiz ham yoqtiradigan kichik restoran bor.",74.9],["Interviewer","What kind of food do you order there?","U yerda qanday taom buyurtma qilasiz?",83.8],["Emily","I often order chicken, but my favourite dish there is actually fish with rice and vegetables. My sister usually chooses pizza.","Koʻpincha tovuq buyurtma qilaman, lekin u yerdagi eng yaxshi koʻrgan taomim aslida sabzavotli guruch bilan baliq. Opam odatda pitsa tanlaydi.",86.3],["Interviewer","Do you ever cook with other people?","Boshqalar bilan birga ovqat pishirasizmi?",95.3],["Emily","Yes. On Sundays, my dad and I sometimes cook together. He's really good at making bread. I normally prepare the vegetables while he works on the main dish.","Ha. Yakshanba kunlari baʼzan dadam bilan birga pishiramiz. U non yopishni juda yaxshi biladi. Men odatda u asosiy taomni tayyorlayotganda sabzavotlarni tayyorlayman.",97.9],["Interviewer","Is there anything you'd like to learn to make?","Pishirishni oʻrganmoqchi boʻlgan narsangiz bormi?",109],["Emily","Definitely. I'd love to learn how to make cake. I can make simple biscuits, but cakes are still difficult for me.","Albatta. Tort pishirishni oʻrganishni juda xohlardim. Oddiy pechenye pishira olaman, lekin tortlar hali men uchun qiyin.",111.9],["Interviewer","Thanks, Emily. That's everything.","Rahmat, Emily. Hammasi shu.",120.3],["Emily","You're welcome.","Arzimaydi.",122.8]],"q":[{"t":"What does Emily usually have for breakfast now?","o":["Cereal","Yogurt with fruit","Coffee and toast"],"a":1,"why":"Ilgari kornfleks yerdi, hozir yogurt."},{"t":"What does Emily sometimes take for lunch when it is cold?","o":["Soup","Pasta","Pizza"],"a":0},{"t":"What time does Emily usually cook dinner?","o":["At about six","At about eight","At about seven"],"a":2},{"t":"What does Emily usually do on Friday evenings?","o":["She cooks with her dad.","She eats out with her sister.","She makes pasta at home."],"a":1},{"t":"What would Emily like to learn to make?","o":["Bread","Biscuits","Cake"],"a":2}]},
{"id":"sb-05","u":5,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Shopping and money","dur":120,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-05.mp3","lines":[["Assistant","Good afternoon. Customer services, how can I help you?","Xayrli kun. Mijozlarga xizmat koʻrsatish boʻlimi, sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.9],["Tom","Hi, I bought a jacket from your shop yesterday, but I think I need to change it.","Salom, kecha sizning doʻkoningizdan kurtka sotib oldim, lekin uni almashtirishim kerak shekilli.",9.4],["Assistant","That's fine. Can I take your name first?","Yaxshi. Avval ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",15.4],["Tom","Yes, it's Tom Harris.","Ha, men Tom Harris.",19],["Assistant","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",21.6],["Tom","Sure, it's H-A-R-R-I-S.","Albatta, H-A-R-R-I-S.",24.7],["Assistant","Thank you. Now, what seems to be the problem with the jacket?","Rahmat. Endi kurtka bilan nima muammo boʻldi?",30.4],["Tom","I bought a medium, but it's too small. I tried a large one in another colour, and that fitted much better. So, I'd like a large, please.","Men oʻrta oʻlchamni olgandim, lekin u juda kichik. Boshqa rangdagi katta oʻlchamni kiyib koʻrdim, u ancha yaxshi keldi. Shuning uchun katta oʻlchamni xohlayman.",35.2],["Assistant","No problem. What colour did you buy?","Muammo yoʻq. Qanday rangni olgandingiz?",45],["Tom","Blue. I really like it, so I don't want to change the colour. I saw a black one too, but blue looks better on me.","Koʻk. Menga juda yoqadi, shuning uchun rangini almashtirmoqchi emasman. Qorasini ham koʻrgandim, lekin koʻki menga yarashadi.",48.2],["Assistant","Do you still have your receipt?","Chekingiz hali bormi?",56.5],["Tom","Yes, I do. The jacket was £45, but there was a special offer yesterday, so I actually paid £36 for it.","Ha, bor. Kurtka 45 funt edi, lekin kecha maxsus chegirma bor edi, shuning uchun aslida 36 funt toʻladim.",58.9],["Assistant","That's fine. You can exchange it at the shop. When would you like to come in?","Yaxshi. Uni doʻkonda almashtirishingiz mumkin. Qachon kelmoqchisiz?",68.2],["Tom","I'm working tomorrow, so I can't come then. I'm free on Thursday afternoon. Is that OK?","Ertaga ishlayman, shuning uchun kela olmayman. Payshanba kuni tushdan keyin boʻshman. Shu boʻladimi?",73.5],["Assistant","Yes, we're open until 8. Do you remember which branch you bought it from?","Ha, soat 8 gacha ochiqmiz. Qaysi filialdan olganingiz esingizdami?",80],["Tom","Yes. The one in the town centre, next to the big supermarket. I usually shop there because it's close to my office.","Ha. Shahar markazidagi, katta supermarketning yonidagi. Odatda u yerdan xarid qilaman, chunki u ofisimga yaqin.",85.8],["Assistant","Good. We currently have three large blue jackets there, so there should be one available for you.","Yaxshi. Hozir u yerda uchta katta oʻlchamli koʻk kurtka bor, demak sizga bittasi chiqishi kerak.",93.4],["Tom","Perfect. Do I need to bring anything apart from the jacket and receipt?","Zoʻr. Kurtka va chekdan boshqa nima olib kelishim kerak?",100.3],["Assistant","No. Just make sure the price label is still on the jacket.","Yoʻq. Faqat kurtkada narx yorligʻi turganiga ishonch hosil qiling.",105.1],["Tom","Yes, it is. I only tried the jacket on at home.","Ha, turibdi. Kurtkani faqat uyda kiyib koʻrganman.",109.8],["Assistant","Great. Then there shouldn't be any problem.","Zoʻr. Unda hech qanday muammo boʻlmasligi kerak.",114],["Tom","Thanks for your help.","Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",117.3],["Assistant","You're welcome.","Arzimaydi.",119]],"q":[{"t":"What size does Tom want now?","o":["Medium","Large","Small"],"a":1},{"t":"How much did Tom pay for the jacket?","o":["£36","£45","£30"],"a":0,"why":"Kecha chegirma boʻlgani uchun u 45 emas, 36 funt toʻlagan."},{"t":"When will Tom go to the shop?","o":["Tomorrow","Thursday morning","Thursday afternoon"],"a":2},{"t":"What time does the shop close?","o":["6 o'clock","8 o'clock","10 o'clock"],"a":1},{"t":"Why does Tom usually shop at that branch?","o":["It is close to his office.","It is next to his home.","It has special offers every day."],"a":0}]},
{"id":"sb-06","u":6,"book":"Student's Book","title":"School, learning and study","dur":130,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-06.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. Welcome to Westfield Language School. How can I help you?","Xayrli tong. Westfield til maktabiga xush kelibsiz. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.8],["Nina","Hi. I'd like some information about your evening English classes.","Salom. Kechki ingliz tili darslaringiz haqida maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",11.1],["Receptionist","Of course. I'll take a few details first. What's your name?","Albatta. Avval bir oz maʼlumot yozib olaman. Ismingiz nima?",16.3],["Nina","Nina Cooper.","Nina Cooper.",21.3],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",22.8],["Nina","Yes. It's C-O-O-P-E-R.","Ha. C-O-O-P-E-R.",25.6],["Receptionist","Thank you. Have you studied English before?","Rahmat. Ilgari ingliz tilini oʻrganganmisiz?",30.8],["Nina","Yes. I studied it at school for about four years. I can have simple conversations, but I still make quite a lot of mistakes.","Ha. Maktabda taxminan toʻrt yil oʻrganganman. Oddiy suhbat qura olaman, lekin hali ancha xato qilaman.",34.5],["Receptionist","That's fine. You'll take a short level test before you start. Now, our evening classes are on Mondays and Wednesdays. Would both days be possible for you?","Mayli. Boshlashdan oldin qisqa daraja testini topshirasiz. Endi, kechki darslarimiz dushanba va chorshanba kunlari. Ikkala kun ham sizga qulaymi?",44.1],["Nina","Yes. I work during the day, but my evenings are usually free.","Ha. Kunduzi ishlayman, lekin kechqurunlari odatda boʻsh boʻlaman.",55],["Receptionist","Excellent. The class begins at 6 o'clock and finishes at 7.30. There's a short break in the middle.","Juda yaxshi. Dars soat 6 da boshlanadi va 7.30 da tugaydi. Oʻrtasida qisqa tanaffus bor.",60.2],["Nina","That sounds good. How many students are there in each class?","Bu yaxshi eshitilyapti. Har bir guruhda nechta oʻquvchi bor?",67.8],["Receptionist","We try to keep the groups small. There are usually about 10 students and the maximum is 12.","Biz guruhlarni kichik saqlashga harakat qilamiz. Odatda taxminan 10 oʻquvchi boʻladi, eng koʻpi 12 ta.",72.3],["Nina","Great. I find it difficult to speak when there are too many people.","Zoʻr. Odam juda koʻp boʻlsa, gapirish menga qiyin.",78.9],["Receptionist","Then this class should suit you. The teacher spends a lot of time on conversation, but you'll also practice reading, writing and listening. Students often say that speaking is their favourite part of the course.","Unda bu guruh sizga mos boʻlsa kerak. Oʻqituvchi suhbatga koʻp vaqt ajratadi, lekin oʻqish, yozish va tinglashni ham mashq qilasiz. Oʻquvchilar koʻpincha kursning eng yoqimli qismi gapirish deyishadi.",83.7],["Nina","That's exactly what I need. How much does the course cost?","Aynan menga kerak narsa shu. Kurs qancha turadi?",96.9],["Receptionist","It's £90 a month. That includes your lessons, but you need to buy the course book separately. It costs £18.","Oyiga 90 funt. Bunga darslar kiradi, lekin kurs kitobini alohida sotib olishingiz kerak. U 18 funt turadi.",101.7],["Nina","OK. And where are the evening classes held?","Mayli. Kechki darslar qayerda oʻtadi?",110.3],["Receptionist","Most lessons are upstairs, but your group will be in room 12 on the ground floor.","Darslarning koʻpi yuqori qavatda, lekin sizning guruhingiz birinchi qavatdagi 12-xonada boʻladi.",114.5],["Nina","Perfect. When can I take the level test?","Zoʻr. Daraja testini qachon topshirsam boʻladi?",120.4],["Receptionist","You can come in tomorrow afternoon, if you like.","Xohlasangiz, ertaga tushdan keyin kelishingiz mumkin.",124.1],["Nina","Great. I'll do that. Thank you.","Zoʻr. Shunday qilaman. Rahmat.",127]],"q":[{"t":"How long did Nina study English at school?","o":["Ten years","Two years","Four years"],"a":2},{"t":"On which days are the evening classes?","o":["Mondays and Wednesdays","Tuesdays and Thursdays","Mondays and Fridays"],"a":0},{"t":"What time does the class finish?","o":["6.00","7.00","7.30"],"a":2},{"t":"How much is the course book?","o":["£90","£18","£12"],"a":1,"why":"90 funt kursning oyiga narxi, kitob alohida 18 funt."},{"t":"Where will Nina's group have lessons?","o":["Room 12 on the ground floor","Room 12 upstairs","Room 10 on the ground floor"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"sb-07","u":7,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Jobs and Working Life","dur":124,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-07.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning, Park Hotel. You're calling about the weekend job, right?","Xayrli tong, Park Hotel. Siz hafta oxiridagi ish boʻyicha qoʻngʻiroq qilyapsiz, toʻgʻrimi?",4.9],["Jamie","Yes, I saw the advertisement online yesterday and I'd like some more information.","Ha, kecha eʼlonni internetda koʻrdim va koʻproq maʼlumot olmoqchi edim.",10.2],["Receptionist","Of course. Before we start, can I take your name?","Albatta. Boshlashdan oldin ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",16.1],["Jamie","It's Jamie Lewis.","Jamie Lewis.",20.2],["Receptionist","And could you spell your surname?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",22.4],["Jamie","Yes, it's L-E-W-I-S.","Ha, L-E-W-I-S.",25.1],["Receptionist","Thanks. The job is in our restaurant. We're looking for someone to help the waiters and clear the tables. Have you worked in a restaurant before?","Rahmat. Ish bizning restoranimizda. Ofitsiantlarga yordam beradigan va stollarni yigʻishtiradigan odam qidiryapmiz. Avval restoranda ishlaganmisiz?",30.5],["Jamie","No, but I worked in a cafe last summer. I served drinks and helped prepare sandwiches.","Yoʻq, lekin oʻtgan yozda kafeda ishlaganman. Ichimliklar tarqatganman va sendvichlar tayyorlashga yordam berganman.",40.1],["Receptionist","That's useful experience. The restaurant gets quite busy, especially at lunchtime, so you need to work quickly.","Bu foydali tajriba. Restoran ancha gavjum boʻladi, ayniqsa tushlik payti, shuning uchun tez ishlash kerak.",46.6],["Jamie","That's fine. I'm used to working with lots of customers.","Muammo yoʻq. Koʻp mijozlar bilan ishlashga oʻrganganman.",54.6],["Receptionist","Good. At the moment, we need someone on Saturday and Sunday. The Saturday shift starts at 10, but on Sunday you start at 1100 because breakfast finishes later.","Yaxshi. Hozir shanba va yakshanba kunlari odam kerak. Shanba kuni smena soat 10 da boshlanadi, yakshanba kuni esa 11 da boshlaysiz, chunki nonushta kechroq tugaydi.",58.6],["Jamie","Okay, and what time would I finish?","Mayli, soat nechada tugataman?",71.1],["Receptionist","Usually around 4. You'll get a 30-minute lunch break during the afternoon.","Odatda soat 4 atrofida. Kunning ikkinchi yarmida 30 daqiqalik tushlik tanaffusi boʻladi.",74.6],["Jamie","Great. What should I wear?","Zoʻr. Nima kiyishim kerak?",80.3],["Receptionist","We provide a shirt, but you need to wear your own black trousers. Please don't wear jeans.","Koylakni biz beramiz, lekin qora shimni oʻzingiz kiyasiz. Iltimos, jinsi kiymang.",83.3],["Jamie","No problem. And how much does the job pay?","Mayli. Ish uchun qancha toʻlanadi?",90.2],["Receptionist","It's £11 an hour. You also get a free meal during each shift.","Soatiga 11 funt. Har bir smenada bepul ovqat ham beriladi.",94.1],["Jamie","That sounds good.","Yaxshi eshitiladi.",99.6],["Receptionist","If you're interested, you'll need to come for a short interview. We're interviewing people on Thursday afternoon.","Qiziqsangiz, qisqa suhbatga kelishingiz kerak. Biz payshanba kuni tushdan keyin suhbat oʻtkazamiz.",101.4],["Jamie","Thursday's fine. Where should I go when I arrive?","Payshanba maʼqul. Kelganimda qayerga borishim kerak?",108.4],["Receptionist","Come to the main entrance and ask for Mrs Green at reception. She'll take you to the manager's office.","Asosiy kirishga keling va resepshnda Mrs Greenni soʻrang. U sizni menejer xonasiga olib boradi.",112.6],["Jamie","Perfect. Thanks very much.","Juda yaxshi. Katta rahmat.",119.5],["Receptionist","You're welcome. See you then.","Arzimaydi. Unda koʻrishguncha.",122]]},
{"id":"sb-08","u":8,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Travel and Transport","dur":127,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-08.mp3","lines":[["Clerk","Good morning, City Travel Centre. How can I help you?","Xayrli tong, City Travel Centre. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.7],["Alex","Hi, I'd like some information about buses to Lakeside. I'm planning to go there this weekend.","Salom, Lakesidega boradigan avtobuslar haqida maʼlumot olmoqchi edim. Hafta oxirida u yerga bormoqchiman.",8.6],["Clerk","Certainly. Are you travelling alone?","Albatta. Yolgʻiz sayohat qilyapsizmi?",15],["Alex","Yes, I'm visiting a friend who lives there.","Ha, u yerda yashaydigan doʻstimnikiga ketyapman.",18.2],["Clerk","OK, before we look at the times, can I take your name?","Mayli, vaqtlarni koʻrishdan oldin ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",22],["Alex","Sure, it's Alex Morgan.","Albatta, Alex Morgan.",26.9],["Clerk","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",29.8],["Alex","Yes, it's M-O-R-G-A-N.","Ha, M-O-R-G-A-N.",32.7],["Clerk","Thanks. Now, which day are you planning to travel?","Rahmat. Endi qaysi kuni bormoqchisiz?",38.3],["Alex","Saturday. I thought about going on Friday evening, but I have to work late that day.","Shanba kuni. Juma kuni kechqurun ketishni oʻylagandim, lekin oʻsha kuni kech ishlashim kerak.",42.9],["Clerk","No problem. There are several buses on Saturday morning. The first one leaves at 7.30, but the next bus at 8.15 is usually more convenient.","Muammo yoʻq. Shanba kuni ertalab bir nechta avtobus bor. Birinchisi 7.30 da ketadi, lekin keyingisi, 8.15 dagisi odatda qulayroq.",49.3],["Alex","Yes, 7.30 is a little early. How long does the journey take?","Ha, 7.30 biroz erta. Yoʻl qancha vaqt oladi?",60.4],["Clerk","Normally about an hour and 20 minutes. However, there are some road works this weekend, so it may take slightly longer.","Odatda taxminan bir soat 20 daqiqa. Lekin bu hafta oxirida yoʻl ishlari bor, shuning uchun biroz uzoqroq vaqt olishi mumkin.",66.1],["Alex","That's OK. How much is a return ticket?","Mayli. Borib-keladigan chipta qancha turadi?",74.8],["Clerk","A single is £9. The return ticket is £15, so that's better value if you're coming back the same weekend.","Bir tomonlama chipta 9 funt. Borib-keladigani 15 funt, shuning uchun shu hafta oxirida qaytsangiz, bu foydaliroq.",78.3],["Alex","Yes, I'm returning on Sunday. Where does the bus leave from?","Ha, yakshanba kuni qaytaman. Avtobus qayerdan ketadi?",87.2],["Clerk","From Central Station, but not from the main bus area. You need to go to Platform 6, which is near the cafe.","Central Stationdan, lekin asosiy avtobus maydonidan emas. 6-platformaga borishingiz kerak, u kafe yonida.",91.9],["Alex","OK, can I buy the ticket on the bus?","Mayli, chiptani avtobusda sotib olsam boʻladimi?",100.2],["Clerk","You can, but weekend buses are often crowded, so I recommend booking your ticket before you travel.","Boʻladi, lekin hafta oxiri avtobuslar koʻpincha gavjum boʻladi, shuning uchun chiptani yoʻlga chiqishdan oldin band qilishni tavsiya qilaman.",103.5],["Alex","Good idea. Can I take a suitcase?","Yaxshi fikr. Chamadon olsam boʻladimi?",111],["Clerk","Yes. One suitcase can go underneath the bus, and you can take a small bag with you to your seat.","Ha. Bitta chamadon avtobus ostiga qoʻyiladi, kichik sumkani esa oʻrningizgacha olib kirishingiz mumkin.",114.3],["Alex","Perfect. I'll book the ticket online today.","Juda yaxshi. Chiptani bugun internetda band qilaman.",121.4],["Clerk","Great. Have a good trip.","Zoʻr. Yoʻlingiz bexatar boʻlsin.",125]]},
{"id":"sb-09","u":9,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Cities, Towns and Neighbourhoods","dur":132,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-09.mp3","lines":[["Staff","Hello, welcome to the new residence centre. Are you new to the area?","Salom, yangi turar joy markaziga xush kelibsiz. Siz bu hududga yangi kelganmisiz?",5.5],["Laura","Yes, I moved here last week, so I'm still trying to find out where everything is.","Ha, oʻtgan hafta koʻchib keldim, shuning uchun hamma narsa qayerdaligini hali bilib olyapman.",10.7],["Staff","Of course, I can give you some information. Can I take your name first?","Albatta, sizga maʼlumot bera olaman. Avval ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",16.7],["Laura","Sure, I'm Laura Dawson.","Albatta, men Laura Dawson.",21.9],["Staff","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25],["Laura","Yes, it's D-A-W-S-O-N.","Ha, D-A-W-S-O-N.",27.7],["Staff","Thank you. And which part of town are you living in?","Rahmat. Shaharning qaysi qismida yashayapsiz?",33],["Laura","I've got a flat in Riverside. It's quite a quiet neighbourhood, near the river.","Riversidega kvartira olganman. Bu daryo yaqinidagi ancha tinch mahalla.",36.7],["Staff","Oh, that's a nice area. There are several useful places nearby. There's a supermarket on King Street and a small market every Saturday morning.","Oh, yaxshi hudud. Atrofda bir nechta foydali joylar bor. King Streetda supermarket bor va har shanba ertalab kichik bozor boʻladi.",42.6],["Laura","Great. I also need somewhere to exercise. Is there a gym near my flat?","Zoʻr. Menga mashq qiladigan joy ham kerak. Kvartiram yaqinida sport zali bormi?",52.9],["Staff","There is, but the sports centre is probably better. It has a gym and a swimming pool. It opens at six in the morning and closes at nine o'clock in the evening.","Bor, lekin sport markazi yaxshiroq boʻlsa kerak. U yerda sport zali ham, suzish havzasi ham bor. Ertalab soat oltida ochiladi va kechqurun soat toʻqqizda yopiladi.",59],["Laura","That's perfect, because I sometimes exercise after work.","Juda yaxshi, chunki baʼzan ishdan keyin mashq qilaman.",69.5],["Staff","You might also want to join the local library. It moved recently. It used to be next to the post office, but now it's opposite the museum.","Mahalliy kutubxonaga aʼzo boʻlishni ham xohlarsiz. U yaqinda koʻchdi. Avval pochta yonida edi, hozir esa muzey roʻparasida.",74.2],["Laura","Good to know. I enjoy reading, so I'll definitely visit it.","Yaxshi boʻlibdi. Kitob oʻqishni yaxshi koʻraman, albatta boraman.",83],["Staff","There's also a lovely park about ten minutes from Riverside. It's usually quiet during the week, although it gets quite busy on sunny weekends.","Riversidedan taxminan oʻn daqiqa narida chiroyli bogʻ ham bor. U hafta davomida odatda tinch, lekin quyoshli hafta oxirlarida ancha gavjum boʻladi.",88.1],["Laura","I'd like somewhere to walk in the evenings.","Kechqurunlari sayr qiladigan joy kerak edi.",96.9],["Staff","Then you'll enjoy it. There's a small lake and a café there too.","Unda sizga yoqadi. U yerda kichik koʻl va kafe ham bor.",99.9],["Laura","Sounds great. What's the easiest way to get into the town centre?","Zoʻr eshitiladi. Shahar markaziga eng oson qanday borsa boʻladi?",104.6],["Staff","Bus number 14 goes directly from Riverside. It runs every 20 minutes during the day.","14-avtobus Riversidedan toʻgʻri boradi. Kunduzi har 20 daqiqada qatnaydi.",109.8],["Laura","Excellent. Is there anything else I should know?","Ajoyib. Yana bilishim kerak boʻlgan narsa bormi?",116.6],["Staff","Yes. On Fridays, there's a street market in the main square. It's a good place to buy fresh fruit and vegetables.","Ha. Juma kunlari bosh maydonda koʻcha bozori boʻladi. Yangi meva va sabzavot sotib olish uchun yaxshi joy.",120.3],["Laura","Thanks. This has been really helpful.","Rahmat. Bu juda foydali boʻldi.",128.2]]},
{"id":"sb-10","u":10,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Technology and Everyday Life","dur":126,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-10.mp3","lines":[["Assistant","Good afternoon. Tech Help Centre. How can I help you?","Xayrli kun. Tech Help Centre. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.3],["Ryan","Hi. I'm having a problem with my new tablet. I bought it from your shop last week.","Salom. Yangi planshetim bilan muammo bor. Uni oʻtgan hafta sizning doʻkoningizdan sotib olgandim.",9.5],["Assistant","I'm sorry about that. I'll take a few details first. What's your name?","Buning uchun uzr. Avval bir nechta maʼlumot olaman. Ismingiz nima?",15.4],["Ryan","It's Ryan Baker.","Ryan Baker.",21.3],["Assistant","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23.2],["Ryan","Sure. It's B-A-K-E-R.","Albatta. B-A-K-E-R.",25],["Assistant","Thank you. Now, what exactly is wrong with the tablet?","Rahmat. Endi planshetda aynan nima muammo?",31.4],["Ryan","The screen is fine, and I can use most of the apps, but the camera isn't working. When I try to take a photo, the screen goes black.","Ekran yaxshi, ilovalarning koʻpini ishlata olaman, lekin kamera ishlamayapti. Suratga olmoqchi boʻlsam, ekran qorayib qoladi.",35.8],["Assistant","I see. Have you tried turning the tablet off and on again?","Tushunarli. Planshetni oʻchirib, qayta yoqib koʻrdingizmi?",45],["Ryan","Yes. Twice. I also charged it fully last night, but that didn't help.","Ha. Ikki marta. Kecha toʻliq zaryadlab ham qoʻydim, lekin foydasi boʻlmadi.",49.9],["Assistant","OK. Which model do you have?","Mayli. Qaysi modelingiz bor?",55.7],["Ryan","It's the T20. I nearly bought the T15 because it was cheaper, but I chose the T20 because it has more storage.","T20. T15 arzonroq boʻlgani uchun uni olishga oz qoldi, lekin xotirasi koʻproq boʻlgani uchun T20 ni tanladim.",58.7],["Assistant","Right. We can check it for you at the shop. When are you free to bring it in?","Tushunarli. Uni doʻkonda tekshirib bera olamiz. Qachon olib kelishga boʻshsiz?",66],["Ryan","I'm busy tomorrow, but I can come on Wednesday afternoon.","Ertaga bandman, lekin chorshanba kuni tushdan keyin kela olaman.",73],["Assistant","That's fine. Our repair desk is open from 10 until 6. If you come before 4, we can probably check it the same day.","Boʻladi. Taʼmirlash stolimiz soat 10 dan 6 gacha ochiq. 4 gacha kelsangiz, ehtimol oʻsha kuni tekshirib beramiz.",77.2],["Ryan","Great. Do I need to bring the box?","Zoʻr. Quti olib kelishim kerakmi?",86],["Assistant","No, but please bring your receipt. We need to check when and where you bought the tablet.","Yoʻq, lekin chekni olib keling. Planshetni qachon va qayerdan sotib olganingizni tekshirishimiz kerak.",89.3],["Ryan","No problem. I still have it.","Muammo yoʻq. U hali menda.",95.6],["Assistant","Good. If it's a simple software problem, the repair should take about 30 minutes. If there's a problem inside the tablet, we may need to keep it for a few days.","Yaxshi. Oddiy dasturiy muammo boʻlsa, taʼmirlash taxminan 30 daqiqa oladi. Planshet ichida nosozlik boʻlsa, uni bir necha kunga olib qolishimiz mumkin.",98.2],["Ryan","OK. Is there a charge for checking it?","Mayli. Tekshirish pullikmi?",109.6],["Assistant","Normally it costs £20, but because your tablet is new, the check is free.","Odatda 20 funt turadi, lekin planshetingiz yangi boʻlgani uchun tekshiruv bepul.",113.3],["Ryan","Excellent. Thanks for your help.","Ajoyib. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",119.8],["Assistant","You're welcome. We'll see you on Wednesday.","Arzimaydi. Chorshanba kuni kutamiz.",122.3]]},
{"id":"sb-11","u":11,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Health, Exercise and Sleep","dur":143,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-11.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. Active Life Centre. How can I help you?","Xayrli tong. Active Life Centre. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.7],["Daniel","Hi. I'd like to join one of your exercise classes. I want to become more active, but I'm not sure which class is best for me.","Salom. Mashgʻulotlaringizdan biriga yozilmoqchi edim. Faolroq boʻlishni xohlayman, lekin qaysi mashgʻulot menga eng mos ekanini bilmayman.",9.8],["Receptionist","No problem. I'll ask you a few questions first. What's your name?","Muammo yoʻq. Avval bir nechta savol beraman. Ismingiz nima?",18.4],["Daniel","It's Daniel Price.","Daniel Price.",23.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25.5],["Daniel","Yes. It's P-R-I-C-E.","Ha. P-R-I-C-E.",27.4],["Receptionist","Thanks. How much exercise do you do at the moment?","Rahmat. Hozir qancha mashq qilasiz?",33.7],["Daniel","Not enough, really. I walk to work most days, but that only takes about 15 minutes. At weekends, I sometimes go cycling, but not regularly.","Rostini aytsam, yetarli emas. Koʻp kunlar ishga piyoda boraman, lekin bu atigi 15 daqiqa oladi. Hafta oxirlari baʼzan velosiped minaman, lekin muntazam emas.",38],["Receptionist","OK. How are your energy levels during the day?","Mayli. Kun davomida quvvatingiz qanday?",48.3],["Daniel","I'm usually fine in the morning, but I often feel tired after lunch. That's one reason I want to exercise more.","Ertalab odatda yaxshi boʻlaman, lekin tushlikdan keyin koʻpincha charchayman. Koʻproq mashq qilmoqchi boʻlishimning sabablaridan biri shu.",52.5],["Receptionist","Exercise may help. We have a beginner fitness class that could suit you. It's on Monday and Wednesday evenings.","Mashq yordam berishi mumkin. Sizga mos kelishi mumkin boʻlgan boshlangʻich fitnes mashgʻulotimiz bor. U dushanba va chorshanba kunlari kechqurun.",60.3],["Daniel","What time does it start?","U soat nechada boshlanadi?",68.1],["Receptionist","The Monday class starts at 6, but Wednesday's class begins at 6.30.","Dushanba mashgʻuloti 6 da boshlanadi, chorshanba mashgʻuloti esa 6.30 da.",70.1],["Daniel","Wednesday would be easier, because I sometimes work late on Mondays.","Chorshanba qulayroq boʻladi, chunki dushanba kunlari baʼzan kech ishlayman.",75.8],["Receptionist","Great. Each class lasts 45 minutes. You'll do some simple exercises, but there's no running.","Zoʻr. Har bir mashgʻulot 45 daqiqa davom etadi. Oddiy mashqlar qilasiz, lekin yugurish yoʻq.",80.5],["Daniel","Good. I'm not a big fan of running.","Yaxshi. Men yugurishni unchalik yoqtirmayman.",88.2],["Receptionist","What about sleep? How many hours do you usually get?","Uyqu-chi? Odatda necha soat uxlaysiz?",91.5],["Daniel","Only about six hours. I often stay up too late watching videos, even when I have to get up early.","Atigi taxminan olti soat. Erta turishim kerak boʻlsa ham, koʻpincha juda kech yotib video koʻraman.",96.2],["Receptionist","You should try to get a little more sleep. It's also a good idea to stop using screens before bed.","Biroz koʻproq uxlashga harakat qilishingiz kerak. Yotishdan oldin ekranlardan foydalanmaslik ham yaxshi fikr.",103.4],["Daniel","Yes, I know. I'm trying to leave my phone in the living room at night instead of taking it to bed.","Ha, bilaman. Kechasi telefonni yotoqqa olib kirmasdan, mehmonxonada qoldirishga harakat qilyapman.",110.2],["Receptionist","That's a good habit. Now, for the exercise class, please bring comfortable clothes and a bottle of water.","Bu yaxshi odat. Endi mashgʻulot uchun qulay kiyim va bir shisha suv olib keling.",116.6],["Daniel","Do I need special shoes?","Maxsus poyabzal kerakmi?",124.7],["Receptionist","Just clean sports shoes. You'll also need a small towel, because some of the exercises can make you quite warm.","Faqat toza sport poyabzali. Kichik sochiq ham kerak boʻladi, chunki baʼzi mashqlar sizni ancha qizdirib yuboradi.",127.3],["Daniel","Fine. How much is the class?","Yaxshi. Mashgʻulot qancha turadi?",135.2],["Receptionist","Your first class is free, so you can try it before deciding whether to join.","Birinchi mashgʻulotingiz bepul, shuning uchun yozilish-yozilmaslikni hal qilishdan oldin sinab koʻrishingiz mumkin.",137.3]]},
{"id":"sb-12","u":12,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Sports and competitions","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-12.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Westside Sports Club. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. Westside Sports Club. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.4],["Oliver","Hi. I saw a poster about your summer sports competition and I'd like to take part.","Salom. Yozgi sport musobaqangiz haqidagi plakatni koʻrdim va qatnashmoqchi edim.",9.7],["Receptionist","Great. I can register you now. Can I have your name first?","Zoʻr. Hozir roʻyxatga olishim mumkin. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",15.8],["Oliver","Yes. It's Oliver Kent.","Ha. Oliver Kent.",21.1],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23.8],["Oliver","Of course. It's K-E-N-T.","Albatta. K-E-N-T.",26.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. We have competitions in tennis, basketball and badminton. Which one are you interested in?","Rahmat. Bizda tennis, basketbol va badminton boʻyicha musobaqalar bor. Qaysi biri sizni qiziqtiradi?",31.4],["Oliver","I play basketball quite often, but I'm already in a competition at college. I'd like to enter the tennis competition here.","Basketbolni tez-tez oʻynayman, lekin kollejda allaqachon musobaqada qatnashyapman. Bu yerda tennis musobaqasiga yozilmoqchiman.",39.4],["Receptionist","No problem. Have you played tennis for long?","Muammo yoʻq. Tennis oʻynaganingizga koʻp boʻldimi?",47.4],["Oliver","About three years. I usually play with my brother at weekends. I'm not an excellent player but I really enjoy it.","Taxminan uch yil. Odatda hafta oxirlari akam bilan oʻynayman. Aʼlo oʻyinchi emasman, lekin juda yoqtiraman.",50.4],["Receptionist","That's the important thing. The competition is on Saturday the 18th. It was originally planned for Sunday that we had to change the day.","Muhimi shu. Musobaqa 18-shanba kuni. Dastlab yakshanbaga rejalashtirilgandi, lekin kunni oʻzgartirishga toʻgʻri keldi.",58.4],["Oliver","Saturday is fine. What time does it start?","Shanba maʼqul. Soat nechada boshlanadi?",68.4],["Receptionist","The first matches begin at 10, but all players must arrive by 9.30. That gives us enough time to check everyone's names and explain the rules.","Birinchi oʻyinlar soat 10 da boshlanadi, lekin barcha oʻyinchilar 9.30 gacha kelishi kerak. Bu hammaning ismini tekshirish va qoidalarni tushuntirish uchun yetarli vaqt beradi.",72.4],["Oliver","OK, do I need to bring my own equipment?","Mayli, oʻz jihozlarimni olib kelishim kerakmi?",83],["Receptionist","We provide tennis balls, but you should bring your own racket. We have a few spare ones, but they're mainly for emergencies.","Tennis toplarini biz beramiz, lekin raketkani oʻzingiz olib keling. Bir nechta zaxira raketkamiz bor, lekin ular asosan favqulodda holatlar uchun.",86.7],["Oliver","That's fine. How much is it to enter?","Mayli. Qatnashish qancha turadi?",94.6],["Receptionist","The normal price is £12, but club members pay only £8.","Odatiy narx 12 funt, lekin klub aʼzolari atigi 8 funt toʻlaydi.",98.3],["Oliver","I joined the club last month, so I can pay the lower price, right?","Klubga oʻtgan oy aʼzo boʻlganman, demak arzonroq narxda toʻlay olaman, toʻgʻrimi?",104.2],["Receptionist","Exactly! There will also be water and fruit for all the players.","Toʻgʻri! Barcha oʻyinchilar uchun suv va meva ham boʻladi.",108.6],["Oliver","Great! Where should I go when I arrive?","Zoʻr! Kelganimda qayerga borishim kerak?",113.7],["Receptionist","Go to the main sports hall and ask for Martin. He'll show you which court you're playing on.","Asosiy sport zaliga boring va Martinni soʻrang. U sizga qaysi kortda oʻynashingizni koʻrsatadi.",117.5],["Oliver","Perfect! I'm looking forward to it!","Juda yaxshi! Intizorlik bilan kutyapman!",123.6],["Receptionist","Excellent! Good luck!","Ajoyib! Omad tilayman!",126.3]]},
{"id":"sb-13","u":13,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Weather and seasonal activities","dur":127,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-13.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. Green Valley Activity Centre. How can I help?","Xayrli tong. Green Valley faoliyat markazi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",6],["Megan","Hi. My family is visiting Green Valley next weekend and I'd like some information about your outdoor activities.","Salom. Oilam bilan kelasi hafta oxirida Green Valleyʼga boramiz va ochiq havodagi mashgʻulotlaringiz haqida maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",10.6],["Receptionist","Of course. I can help with that. Could I take your name first?","Albatta. Bunda yordam bera olaman. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",18.7],["Megan","Yes, it's Megan Frost.","Ha, men Megan Frost.",23.8],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",26.5],["Megan","Sure. It's F-R-O-S-T.","Albatta. F-R-O-S-T.",29.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. What kind of activity are you interested in?","Rahmat. Qanday mashgʻulot qiziqtiradi?",34.3],["Megan","We wanted to go cycling, but I checked the weather this morning and it looks quite wet. Is there anything else we could do?","Velosipedda sayr qilmoqchi edik, lekin bugun ertalab ob-havoni koʻrsam, ancha nam koʻrinadi. Boshqa nima qilsak boʻladi?",38.3],["Receptionist","Yes. The forecast says there will be rain on Saturday morning, but the afternoon should be much drier.","Ha. Prognozga koʻra shanba kuni ertalab yomgʻir yogʻadi, lekin tushdan keyin ancha quruq boʻladi.",46.4],["Megan","That's good. We'd still like to spend some time outside.","Yaxshi. Baribir biroz tashqarida vaqt oʻtkazmoqchimiz.",53.5],["Receptionist","In that case, you could join our afternoon forest walk. It starts at 2.30 and lasts about two hours.","Unda tushdan keyingi oʻrmon sayrimizga qoʻshilishingiz mumkin. U 2.30 da boshlanadi va taxminan ikki soat davom etadi.",57.7],["Megan","That sounds nice. Is it suitable for children?","Yaxshi eshitilyapti. Bolalarga mosmi?",65.1],["Receptionist","Yes. The route is easy and families often join us. However, the paths can be wet at this time of year, so everyone should wear boots rather than ordinary shoes.","Ha. Yoʻl oson, oilalar tez-tez qoʻshiladi. Lekin yilning bu faslida yoʻllar nam boʻlishi mumkin, shuning uchun hamma oddiy poyabzal oʻrniga etik kiyishi kerak.",69.1],["Megan","OK. We can bring those. What about Sunday?","Xop. Ularni olib kela olamiz. Yakshanba-chi?",80.6],["Receptionist","Sunday should be sunny, although it may be a little cold in the morning. It should reach about 16 degrees in the afternoon.","Yakshanba kuni quyoshli boʻladi, garchi ertalab biroz sovuq boʻlishi mumkin. Tushdan keyin taxminan 16 darajagacha isiydi.",84.8],["Megan","Great. Maybe we could go cycling then?","Zoʻr. Unda velosipedda sayr qilsak boʻlarmikin?",92.8],["Receptionist","Definitely. We rent bicycles here. An adult bicycle costs £12 for the day and a child's bicycle costs £8.","Albatta. Bu yerda velosiped ijaraga beramiz. Kattalar velosipedi kuniga £12, bolalarniki £8 turadi.",96.2],["Megan","Perfect. Do we need to book them?","Juda soz. Ularni oldindan band qilish kerakmi?",105.4],["Receptionist","At weekends, yes. Spring is a very popular time for cycling here, especially when the weather is good.","Dam olish kunlari ha. Bahor bu yerda velosiped uchun juda mashhur payt, ayniqsa ob-havo yaxshi boʻlsa.",108.4],["Megan","OK. I'll book them today.","Xop. Bugun band qilaman.",115.6],["Receptionist","Great. And remember to bring a light jacket, because the evenings can still be cool.","Zoʻr. Yengil kurtka olishni unutmang, chunki kechqurunlari hali ham salqin boʻlishi mumkin.",118.2],["Megan","We will. Thanks for your help.","Olamiz. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",124.3]]},
{"id":"sb-14","u":14,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Animals and Wildlife","dur":125,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-14.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning, Greenhill Wildlife Park, how can I help?","Xayrli tong, Greenhill yovvoyi tabiat parki, sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4],["Helen","Hi, I'm planning to visit the park with my family this weekend and I'd like some information.","Salom, shu hafta oxirida oilam bilan parkka bormoqchiman va maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",9],["Receptionist","Of course, are you interested in any particular animals?","Albatta, biror hayvon sizni ayniqsa qiziqtiradimi?",16.9],["Helen","My children really want to see the monkeys but I'd like to see everything if we have enough time.","Bolalarim maymunlarni juda koʻrmoqchi, lekin vaqt yetsa, hammasini koʻrmoqchiman.",20],["Receptionist","Certainly. Before we continue could I take your name?","Albatta. Davom etishdan oldin ismingizni aytsangiz.",27.1],["Helen","Yes, I'm Helen Webb.","Ha, men Helen Webb.",30.8],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",33.5],["Helen","Sure, it's W-E-B-B.","Albatta, W-E-B-B.",36.1],["Receptionist","Thank you. Which day are you thinking of visiting?","Rahmat. Qaysi kuni kelmoqchisiz?",40.3],["Helen","We're coming on Sunday. We originally planned to come on Saturday but my son has a football match.","Yakshanba kuni kelamiz. Dastlab shanba kuni kelmoqchi edik, lekin oʻgʻlimning futbol oʻyini bor.",43.9],["Receptionist","No problem. The park opens at nine. If your children like monkeys there's a feeding session at 10.30. A member of staff talks about the animals while they eat.","Muammo yoʻq. Park soat toʻqqizda ochiladi. Bolalaringiz maymunlarni yaxshi koʻrsa, 10.30 da ovqatlantirish seansi bor. Ular ovqatlanayotganda xodim hayvonlar haqida gapirib beradi.",50.5],["Helen","They'll love that! Where are the monkeys?","Ular buni yaxshi koʻradi! Maymunlar qayerda?",61],["Receptionist","They're in the forest area just past the lake. You'll also see several kinds of birds there. Some of them are very colourful so it's a popular place for photographs.","Ular koʻldan keyingi oʻrmon hududida. U yerda bir necha xil qushlarni ham koʻrasiz. Baʼzilari juda rang-barang, shuning uchun suratga olish uchun mashhur joy.",64.5],["Helen","Great! Are there any baby animals at the moment?","Zoʻr! Hozir bolalagan hayvonlar bormi?",76.8],["Receptionist","Yes, we have two young bears. They were born earlier this year and have recently started coming outside with their mother.","Ha, ikkita yosh ayigʻimiz bor. Ular shu yil boshida tugʻilgan va yaqinda onasi bilan tashqariga chiqa boshlagan.",80.9],["Helen","Wonderful! My children will be excited about those.","Ajoyib! Bolalarim ularni koʻrib xursand boʻladi.",88.4],["Receptionist","There's also a short wildlife talk in the afternoon. It starts at two and explains how we care for the animals.","Tushdan keyin yovvoyi tabiat haqida qisqa maʼruza ham bor. U soat ikkida boshlanadi va hayvonlarga qanday qarashimizni tushuntiradi.",93.2],["Helen","Is there somewhere to eat?","Ovqatlanadigan joy bormi?",100.7],["Receptionist","Yes. The cafe is next to the main entrance. You can also bring your own food and use the picnic area near the river.","Ha. Kafe asosiy kirish yonida. Oʻz ovqatingizni olib kelib, daryo yonidagi piknik joyidan ham foydalanishingiz mumkin.",103.8],["Helen","Good! How much are children's tickets?","Yaxshi! Bolalar chiptasi qancha?",111.9],["Receptionist","Adults are 14 pounds and a child's ticket is nine pounds. Children under three enter free.","Kattalar uchun 14 funt, bola chiptasi toʻqqiz funt. Uch yoshgacha bolalar bepul kiradi.",114],["Helen","Perfect! Thanks for all the information.","Juda soz! Barcha maʼlumot uchun rahmat.",120.6]]},
{"id":"sb-15","u":15,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Nature and the Environment","dur":128,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-15.mp3","lines":[["Coordinator","Hello, Green Town Project. How can I help?","Salom, Green Town loyihasi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",3.9],["Ben","Hi, I saw your poster about the community clean-up and I'd like to join.","Salom, mahalla tozalash haqidagi plakatingizni koʻrdim va qoʻshilmoqchiman.",9],["Coordinator","That's great. We're still looking for volunteers. Can I take your name first?","Ajoyib. Hali ham ixtiyoriylar qidiryapmiz. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",14.6],["Ben","Yes, I'm Ben Russell.","Ha, men Ben Russell.",20.5],["Coordinator","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23.5],["Ben","Sure. It's R-U-S-S-E-L-L.","Albatta. R-U-S-S-E-L-L.",26.2],["Coordinator","Thank you. We're cleaning several outdoor areas this month. The next event is at Lakewood Park. Have you been there before?","Rahmat. Bu oy bir nechta ochiq hududni tozalaymiz. Keyingi tadbir Lakewood bogʻida. Ilgari u yerda boʻlganmisiz?",32],["Ben","Yes. I sometimes go there for walks. It's a beautiful place. But I noticed quite a lot of rubbish near the lake last weekend.","Ha. Baʼzan u yerga sayr qilgani boraman. Chiroyli joy. Lekin oʻtgan hafta oxirida koʻl yonida juda koʻp axlat koʻrdim.",40.6],["Coordinator","That's one of the reasons we chose it. We're meeting this Saturday. We considered Sunday, but the park is usually much busier then.","Aynan shu sabablardan biri tufayli uni tanladik. Shu shanba kuni yigʻilamiz. Yakshanbani ham oʻylagan edik, lekin u kuni park odatda ancha gavjum boʻladi.",49.7],["Ben","Saturday is fine. What time should I arrive?","Shanba durust. Soat nechada kelishim kerak?",58.6],["Coordinator","We'll start cleaning at ten, but volunteers should arrive by nine forty-five. That gives us time to explain what everyone needs to do.","Tozalashni soat oʻnda boshlaymiz, lekin ixtiyoriylar toʻqqiz qirq beshgacha kelishi kerak. Shunda hammaga nima qilish kerakligini tushuntirishga vaqtimiz boʻladi.",62],["Ben","Okay. Do I need to bring anything?","Xop. Biror narsa olib kelishim kerakmi?",71],["Coordinator","We provide rubbish bags and gloves. Please bring a bottle of water and wear comfortable clothes. Strong shoes are also a good idea because the ground near the lake can be muddy.","Axlat xaltalari va qoʻlqoplarni oʻzimiz beramiz. Iltimos, bir shisha suv olib keling va qulay kiyining. Mustahkam poyabzal ham foydali, chunki koʻl yonidagi yer loyli boʻlishi mumkin.",74.2],["Ben","No problem. What kind of rubbish do you usually find?","Muammo yoʻq. Odatda qanday axlat topasizlar?",86],["Coordinator","Mostly plastic bottles, paper and food packaging. We separate everything we collect so that as much as possible can be recycled.","Asosan plastik shisha, qogʻoz va oziq-ovqat qadoqlari. Yigʻgan hamma narsamizni ajratamiz, shunda iloji boricha koʻproq qayta ishlanadi.",90.3],["Ben","That makes sense. How long will the clean-up take?","Mantiqli. Tozalash qancha davom etadi?",99.8],["Coordinator","About three hours. At one o'clock we'll stop and have lunch together. We provide sandwiches, but volunteers should bring their own drink.","Taxminan uch soat. Soat birda toʻxtab, birga tushlik qilamiz. Sendvichlarni oʻzimiz beramiz, lekin ichimlikni ixtiyoriylar oʻzlari olib kelishi kerak.",103.6],["Ben","Great. Can children take part too?","Zoʻr. Bolalar ham qatnasha oladimi?",112.8],["Coordinator","Yes, but anyone under sixteen needs to come with an adult.","Ha, lekin on oltiga yetmaganlar kattalar bilan kelishi kerak.",116.2],["Ben","Perfect. I might bring my younger brother.","Juda soz. Ukamni olib kelishim mumkin.",121.4],["Coordinator","Excellent. The more people we have, the better.","Ajoyib. Odam qancha koʻp boʻlsa, shuncha yaxshi.",124.3]]},
{"id":"sb-16","u":16,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Films, music, books and entertainment","dur":127,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-16.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Central Arts Centre. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. Central Arts Centre. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",6.8],["Amy","Hi. I saw a poster about your film and music weekend and I'd like some more information.","Salom. Kino va musiqa hafta oxirligingiz haqidagi plakatni koʻrdim va koʻproq maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",11.1],["Receptionist","Of course. Are you interested in booking something?","Albatta. Biror narsani band qilmoqchimisiz?",18.1],["Amy","Yes, probably. I'm coming with a friend.","Ha, ehtimol. Doʻstim bilan kelaman.",22],["Receptionist","Great. Before we start, can I take your name?","Zoʻr. Boshlashdan oldin ismingizni aytsangiz.",26],["Amy","Sure. I'm Amy Stone.","Albatta. Men Amy Stone.",29.9],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",32.6],["Amy","Yes. It's S-T-O-N-E.","Ha. S-T-O-N-E.",35.5],["Receptionist","Thank you. The festival starts on Friday evening, but most activities are on Saturday. There are films, live music and a book event.","Rahmat. Festival juma kuni kechqurun boshlanadi, lekin tadbirlarning koʻpi shanba kuni. Filmlar, jonli musiqa va kitob tadbiri boʻladi.",40.7],["Amy","Saturday is better for us. What films are you showing?","Biz uchun shanba qulayroq. Qanday filmlar koʻrsatasizlar?",50.3],["Receptionist","There's a comedy in the afternoon and an adventure film in the evening. The comedy starts at 2, but the adventure film begins at 6.30.","Tushdan keyin komediya va kechqurun sarguzasht filmi bor. Komediya soat 2 da boshlanadi, sarguzasht filmi esa 6.30 da.",54.3],["Amy","I think we'd prefer the adventure film.","Menimcha, sarguzasht filmini afzal koʻramiz.",63.5],["Receptionist","That's been very popular. It's about a group of friends who travel across South America looking for a lost village.","U juda mashhur boʻldi. U Janubiy Amerika boʻylab yoʻqolgan qishloqni izlab sayohat qilgan doʻstlar guruhi haqida.",66.6],["Amy","Sounds interesting. Is there any live music?","Qiziq eshitilyapti. Jonli musiqa bormi?",74],["Receptionist","Yes. After the film, a local band will play in the main hall. They mostly play pop and rock music.","Ha. Filmdan keyin asosiy zalda mahalliy guruh chiqish qiladi. Ular asosan pop va rok musiqa ijro etadi.",77.8],["Amy","Great. What about the book event you mentioned?","Zoʻr. Aytgan kitob tadbiringiz-chi?",85.1],["Receptionist","A travel writer called James Wood is giving a short talk. He'll speak about his new book and answer questions from the audience.","James Wood ismli sayohat yozuvchisi qisqa maʼruza qiladi. U yangi kitobi haqida gapiradi va tomoshabinlar savollariga javob beradi.",88.8],["Amy","I'd like that too. How much are tickets?","Bu ham yoqadi. Chiptalar qancha?",97.3],["Receptionist","You can buy separate tickets, but the full day ticket is better value. It used to be £20, but this year it costs £18.","Alohida chiptalar olish mumkin, lekin butun kunlik chipta foydaliroq. Ilgari £20 edi, bu yil £18 turadi.",100.8],["Amy","That sounds reasonable. Do we need to book in advance?","Maqul narx. Oldindan band qilish kerakmi?",110.1],["Receptionist","I recommend it. Last year, the evening events were completely full by Friday morning.","Tavsiya qilaman. Oʻtgan yili kechki tadbirlar juma kuni ertalabgacha butunlay band boʻlib boʻlgan edi.",114.2],["Amy","Okay. I'll book two tickets online tonight.","Xop. Bugun kechqurun onlayn ikkita chipta band qilaman.",120.4],["Receptionist","Excellent. I hope you both enjoy the festival.","Ajoyib. Ikkalangizga ham festival yoqadi degan umiddaman.",124.1]]},
{"id":"sb-17","u":17,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Interesting people and their lives","dur":123,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-17.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome back to People in Our Town. Today I'm talking to a young photographer who has travelled to many interesting places. Thanks for joining us. Could you introduce yourself?","People in Our Town dasturiga xush kelibsiz. Bugun men koʻplab qiziqarli joylarga sayohat qilgan yosh fotograf bilan suhbatlashyapman. Kelganingiz uchun rahmat. Oʻzingizni tanishtirib bera olasizmi?",4.5],["Nina","Sure. My name is Nina Hayes.","Albatta. Ismim Nina Hayes.",16.7],["Host","And could you spell your surname for our listeners?","Tinglovchilarimiz uchun familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",20],["Nina","Of course. It's H-A-Y-E-S.","Albatta. H-A-Y-E-S.",24],["Host","Thanks Nina. Where did you grow up?","Rahmat, Nina. Qayerda oʻsgansiz?",27.9],["Nina","I was born in London, but my family moved when I was very young. I actually grew up in a small village near Oxford. There were only about 500 people there.","Londonda tugʻilganman, lekin oilam men juda yosh paytimda koʻchib ketgan. Aslida Oksford yaqinidagi kichik qishloqda oʻsganman. U yerda atigi 500 ga yaqin odam yashardi.",31.9],["Host","When did you become interested in photography?","Fotografiyaga qachon qiziqib qoldingiz?",42.9],["Nina","When I was 14, my grandfather gave me his old camera for my birthday. At first I just took pictures of my family and friends.","14 yoshimda bobom tugʻilgan kunimga eski kamerasini sovgʻa qildi. Avval faqat oilam va doʻstlarimni suratga olardim.",45.9],["Host","Did you study photography later?","Keyinroq fotografiyani oʻqidingizmi?",54.9],["Nina","Yes. After school, I studied art at college for two years. I wanted to study painting at first, but I decided to choose photography because I enjoyed it more.","Ha. Maktabdan keyin kollejda ikki yil sanʼat oʻqidim. Avval rassomlikni oʻqimoqchi edim, lekin fotografiyani tanladim, chunki u menga koʻproq yoqardi.",57.9],["Host","And when did you start travelling?","Sayohat qilishni qachon boshladingiz?",69.9],["Nina","My first big trip was to Italy. I stayed there for three months and took hundreds of pictures. After that, I visited several other countries.","Birinchi katta safarim Italiyaga boʻldi. U yerda uch oy turdim va yuzlab surat oldim. Shundan keyin yana bir nechta davlatga bordim.",71.9],["Host","Which place has been your favourite?","Eng yoqqan joyingiz qaysi?",82.9],["Nina","Probably Japan. I spent six weeks there last year. I loved the busy cities, but I also visited some beautiful quiet places in the countryside.","Ehtimol, Yaponiya. Oʻtgan yili u yerda olti hafta boʻldim. Gavjum shaharlar menga yoqdi, lekin qishloq joylardagi goʻzal sokin joylarga ham bordim.",84.9],["Host","What do you photograph most often now?","Hozir koʻproq nimani suratga olasiz?",96.9],["Nina","I used to take lots of pictures of buildings, but these days I mainly photograph people. I enjoy meeting someone and learning a little about their life before taking their picture.","Avval koʻp binolarni suratga olardim, hozir esa asosan odamlarni. Odam bilan tanishib, suratga olishdan oldin uning hayoti haqida bir oz bilib olish menga yoqadi.",99.9],["Host","Do you have any plans for the future?","Kelajak uchun rejalaringiz bormi?",111.9],["Nina","Yes. Next year I want to make a book of my favourite photographs.","Ha. Kelasi yil eng sevimli suratlarimdan kitob qilmoqchiman.",114.9],["Host","That sounds exciting. Good luck with it.","Qiziqarli eshitilyapti. Omad tilayman.",119.9]]},
{"id":"sb-18","u":18,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Festivals, Celebrations and Traditions","dur":126,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-18.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning, Riverside Festival Office. How can I help?","Xayrli tong, Riverside festival ofisi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.3],["Anna","Hi, my family has just moved to the area and we'd like some information about the Summer Festival.","Salom, oilam shu hududga yaqinda koʻchib keldi va Yoz festivali haqida maʼlumot olmoqchimiz.",10.5],["Receptionist","Of course, it's one of our biggest celebrations of the year. Can I take your name first?","Albatta, bu yilning eng katta bayramlaridan biri. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",17],["Anna","Yes, I'm Anna Mitchell.","Ha, men Anna Mitchell.",24],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",26.5],["Anna","Sure, it's M-I-T-C-H-E-L-L.","Albatta, M-I-T-C-H-E-L-L.",29.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. The festival is usually held on the first Saturday in July, but this year it will be on Sunday because there's another large event on Saturday.","Rahmat. Festival odatda iyulning birinchi shanbasida oʻtkaziladi, lekin bu yil yakshanba kuni boʻladi, chunki shanba kuni boshqa katta tadbir bor.",36.6],["Anna","Great! What time does everything begin?","Zoʻr! Hammasi soat nechada boshlanadi?",46.6],["Receptionist","The market opens at 10, but the main celebration starts at 11.30 with a parade through the town centre.","Bozor soat 10 da ochiladi, asosiy bayram esa 11.30 da shahar markazidan oʻtadigan parad bilan boshlanadi.",50.2],["Anna","My children would enjoy that. What happens after the parade?","Bolalarim buni yaxshi koʻrishadi. Paraddan keyin nima boʻladi?",57.7],["Receptionist","There's live music in Riverside Park. We'll also have traditional dancing, games for children and plenty of food.","Riverside bogʻida jonli musiqa boʻladi. Shuningdek, milliy raqslar, bolalar uchun oʻyinlar va koʻp ovqat boʻladi.",62.2],["Anna","What kind of traditional food can we try?","Qanday milliy taomlarni totib koʻrsak boʻladi?",70.2],["Receptionist","Several things, but our local bread is especially popular. It's made fresh in the morning and visitors can watch how it's prepared.","Bir nechta narsa, lekin mahalliy nonimiz ayniqsa mashhur. U ertalab yangi pishiriladi va mehmonlar uning qanday tayyorlanishini koʻrishi mumkin.",73.5],["Anna","That sounds interesting. Do people wear anything special?","Qiziq eshitilyapti. Odamlar maxsus biror narsa kiyadimi?",82.2],["Receptionist","Some of the dancers wear traditional clothes. Visitors can wear whatever they like, although many people choose something colourful because it makes the festival feel more cheerful.","Baʼzi raqqosalar milliy kiyim kiyadi. Mehmonlar xohlagan narsasini kiyishi mumkin, lekin koʻpchilik rang-barang kiyimni tanlaydi, chunki bu festivalni quvnoqroq qiladi.",86.8],["Anna","Is there anything in the evening?","Kechqurun biror tadbir bormi?",97.7],["Receptionist","Yes. At seven there's a concert, and later there will be fireworks near the river. They begin when it gets dark.","Ha. Soat yettida konsert, keyinroq daryo yonida otashbozlik boʻladi. Ular qorongʻi tushganda boshlanadi.",99.5],["Anna","Do we need tickets?","Chipta kerakmi?",108.2],["Receptionist","Most activities are free. The evening concert costs £5 for adults, but children can enter free.","Koʻp tadbirlar bepul. Kechki konsert kattalar uchun £5, lekin bolalar bepul kiradi.",109.5],["Anna","Perfect! We'll definitely come.","Juda soz! Albatta kelamiz.",117.4],["Receptionist","Wonderful! I hope your family enjoys its first Riverside Festival.","Ajoyib! Oilangizga birinchi Riverside festivali yoqadi degan umiddaman.",120.5]]},
{"id":"sb-19","u":19,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Childhood and Memories","dur":119,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-19.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome to Memories of Home. Today we're talking to people about their childhood. Could you introduce yourself?","Memories of Home dasturiga xush kelibsiz. Bugun odamlar bilan ularning bolaligi haqida gaplashamiz. Oʻzingizni tanishtirsangiz.",4.6],["Rachel","Sure. My name's Rachel Perry.","Albatta. Ismim Rachel Perry.",11.2],["Host","Could you spell your surname for us?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",16.3],["Rachel","Yes, it's P-E-R-R-Y.","Ha, P-E-R-R-Y.",19.3],["Host","Thanks, Rachel. Where did you grow up?","Rahmat, Rachel. Qayerda katta boʻldingiz?",22.3],["Rachel","I grew up in a small town near the sea. It wasn't a very busy place, but I loved living there because we could walk to the beach.","Men dengiz yaqinidagi kichik shaharchada katta boʻlganman. U unchalik gavjum joy emas edi, lekin men u yerda yashashni yaxshi koʻrardim, chunki plyajga piyoda borish mumkin edi.",26.7],["Host","What was your home like?","Uyingiz qanday edi?",35.3],["Rachel","We lived in an old house with a large garden. I shared a bedroom with my younger sister until I was 12. We sometimes argued because she was untidy, but we were very close.","Biz katta bogʻli eski uyda yashardik. 12 yoshimgacha kichik singlim bilan bir xonada turganman. Baʼzan u tartibsiz boʻlgani uchun janjallashardik, lekin biz juda yaqin edik.",37.9],["Host","What do you remember about school?","Maktab haqida nimalarni eslaysiz?",50.2],["Rachel","I went to a small primary school about 15 minutes from our house. I usually walked there with two friends. My favourite subject was art because I loved drawing and making things.","Men uyimizdan taxminan 15 daqiqalik masofadagi kichik boshlangʻich maktabga borardim. Odatda u yerga ikki doʻstim bilan piyoda borardim. Sevimli fanim tasviriy sanʼat edi, chunki rasm chizish va biror narsa yasashni yaxshi koʻrardim.",53.2],["Host","What did you do after school?","Maktabdan keyin nima qilardingiz?",66.2],["Rachel","We spent a lot of time outside. There weren't many computer games in our house, so my friends and I usually played in the garden or rode our bikes around the neighbourhood.","Biz koʻp vaqtni tashqarida oʻtkazardik. Uyimizda kompyuter oʻyinlari koʻp emas edi, shuning uchun doʻstlarim bilan odatda bogʻda oʻynardik yoki mahallada velosipedda aylanardik.",69.2],["Host","Did your family have any special weekend routines?","Oilangizda dam olish kunlariga xos odatlar bormidi?",79.2],["Rachel","Yes, every Saturday morning my dad took us to the market. In the afternoon we often visited my grandparents. My grandmother always made cake for us.","Ha, har shanba ertalab dadam bizni bozorga olib borardi. Tushdan keyin esa koʻpincha bobo-buvimnikiga borardik. Buvim doim biz uchun tort pishirardi.",83.2],["Host","That sounds like a nice memory. What about holidays?","Bu yaxshi xotiraga oʻxshaydi. Taʼtillar-chi?",94.2],["Rachel","Every summer we went camping for a week. My favourite trip was when I was 14. We stayed near a lake and I learnt to swim there.","Har yozda bir hafta chodirda dam olishga borardik. Sevimli sayohatim 14 yoshimda boʻlgan. Biz koʻl yaqinida turdik va men u yerda suzishni oʻrgandim.",99.2],["Host","Do you still visit the town where you grew up?","Katta boʻlgan shaharchangizga hozir ham borib turasizmi?",108.2],["Rachel","Yes, usually once or twice a year. It has changed a lot, but it still feels like home.","Ha, odatda yilda bir-ikki marta. U juda oʻzgarib ketgan, lekin hanuz uy kabi tuyuladi.",111.2]]},
{"id":"sb-20","u":20,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Everyday problems and solutions","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-20.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. West Park Apartments. How can I help you?","Xayrli tong. West Park Apartments. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",6],["Emma","Hi. I live in one of your apartments and I need to report a problem.","Salom. Men sizlarning kvartiralaringizdan birida yashayman va muammo haqida xabar berishim kerak.",9.8],["Receptionist","Of course. Can I take your name first?","Albatta. Avval ismingizni olsam?",15.4],["Emma","Yes. I'm Emma Walsh.","Ha. Men Emma Walsh.",18.7],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",21.6],["Emma","Sure. It's W-A-L-S-H.","Albatta. W-A-L-S-H.",24.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. And which apartment are you in?","Rahmat. Qaysi kvartirada turasiz?",29.3],["Emma","Apartment 24 on the second floor. I moved in about three months ago.","Ikkinchi qavatdagi 24-kvartira. Taxminan uch oy oldin koʻchib kelganman.",32.9],["Receptionist","Okay. What seems to be the problem?","Xoʻp. Muammo nimada?",38.8],["Emma","There's something wrong with the shower. The water was fine yesterday morning, but last night it suddenly became cold. I tried it again this morning and it's still cold.","Dushda nimadir notoʻgʻri. Kecha ertalab suv yaxshi edi, lekin kecha kechqurun birdan sovib qoldi. Bugun ertalab yana urinib koʻrdim, hali ham sovuq.",42.1],["Receptionist","I see. Is there hot water anywhere else in the apartment?","Tushunarli. Kvartiraning boshqa joyida issiq suv bormi?",54.2],["Emma","Yes. The kitchen tap is working normally, so I think the problem is only in the bathroom.","Ha. Oshxonadagi jumrak odatdagidek ishlayapti, shuning uchun muammo faqat vannaxonada deb oʻylayman.",58.9],["Receptionist","All right. We'll need to send someone to look at it. Are you at home today?","Yaxshi. Koʻrib chiqish uchun kimnidir yuborishimiz kerak. Bugun uydamisiz?",66.1],["Emma","I'm at work until five. I could be home by five thirty, but not before then.","Soat beshgacha ishdaman. Beshu yarimgacha uyda boʻlishim mumkin, bundan oldin emas.",71.3],["Receptionist","That should be fine. Our repair person can come between five thirty and seven.","Bu mos keladi. Taʼmirchimiz beshu yarim bilan yetti oraligʻida kelishi mumkin.",77.5],["Emma","Great. Will I need to pay anything?","Zoʻr. Biror narsa toʻlashim kerakmi?",83.2],["Receptionist","No. Bathroom repairs like this are free for residents, unless the problem was caused by damage.","Yoʻq. Bunday vannaxona taʼmirlari yashovchilar uchun bepul, agar muammo shikastlanishdan kelib chiqmagan boʻlsa.",86.4],["Emma","Okay. That's good.","Xoʻp. Bu yaxshi.",92.9],["Receptionist","Is there anything else you'd like us to check?","Yana biror narsani tekshirishimizni xohlaysizmi?",95.4],["Emma","Actually, yes. The light in the kitchen is also very weak. I changed the bulb, but it didn't make any difference.","Aslida, ha. Oshxonadagi chiroq ham juda xira. Lampochkani almashtirdim, lekin foydasi boʻlmadi.",98.2],["Receptionist","I'll add that to the repair request. The repair person can check both problems.","Buni taʼmir arizasiga qoʻshib qoʻyaman. Taʼmirchi ikkala muammoni ham tekshirishi mumkin.",107.1],["Emma","Perfect. What should I do if I'm late getting home?","Ajoyib. Uyga kech qolsam, nima qilishim kerak?",112.5],["Receptionist","Call the office on seven three oh four one eight six. Someone will be here until seven.","Ofisga yetti uch nol toʻrt bir sakkiz oltiga qoʻngʻiroq qiling. Soat yettigacha kimdir shu yerda boʻladi.",117],["Emma","Great. I'll write that down. Thanks for your help.","Zoʻr. Buni yozib olaman. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",123.6],["Receptionist","You're welcome.","Arzimaydi.",127.4]]},
{"id":"sb-21","u":21,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Helping people and community life","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-21.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning, Brookside Community Centre. How can I help?","Xayrli tong, Brookside Community Centre. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",6.2],["Alice","Hi, I saw your notice asking for volunteers and I'd like to help.","Salom, ixtiyoriylar kerakligi haqidagi eʼloningizni koʻrdim va yordam bermoqchiman.",10.3],["Receptionist","That's great. We have several volunteer activities at the moment. Can I take your name first?","Bu ajoyib. Hozir bizda bir nechta ixtiyoriy faoliyat bor. Avval ismingizni olsam?",15.9],["Alice","Sure, I'm Alice Young.","Albatta, men Alice Young.",22.3],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25],["Alice","Yes, it's Y-O-U-N-G.","Ha, Y-O-U-N-G.",27.8],["Receptionist","Thank you. What kind of volunteer work are you interested in?","Rahmat. Qanday ixtiyoriy ish sizni qiziqtiradi?",33],["Alice","I enjoy working with older people. I used to visit my grandmother every week and I often helped her with shopping and things around the house.","Men keksalar bilan ishlashni yaxshi koʻraman. Avval buvimnikiga har hafta borardim va unga xarid qilishda hamda uy ishlarida koʻp yordam berardim.",37.3],["Receptionist","Then our shopping service might suit you. Volunteers help older residents who find it difficult to carry heavy bags home.","Unda bizning xarid xizmati sizga mos kelishi mumkin. Ixtiyoriylar ogʻir xaltalarni uyga olib borishi qiyin boʻlgan keksa yashovchilarga yordam beradi.",46.6],["Alice","That sounds like something I could do.","Bu men qila oladigan ishga oʻxshaydi.",54.4],["Receptionist","Good. We need volunteers on Tuesday and Thursday afternoons. Tuesday's almost full, so Thursday would be more useful for us.","Yaxshi. Bizga seshanba va payshanba kunlari tushdan keyin ixtiyoriylar kerak. Seshanba deyarli band, shuning uchun payshanba biz uchun foydaliroq.",57],["Alice","Thursday is fine. I finish work early that day.","Payshanba mayli. U kuni ishni erta tugataman.",65.9],["Receptionist","Excellent. Volunteers meet here at the community centre at 2.15. We give everyone a shopping list and an address before they leave.","Ajoyib. Ixtiyoriylar bu yerda, markazda soat 2.15 da yigʻiladi. Ketishdan oldin har kimga xarid roʻyxati va manzil beramiz.",70],["Alice","How long does it usually take?","Odatda qancha vaqt oladi?",79.8],["Receptionist","About two hours. Most volunteers help one or two people each afternoon.","Taxminan ikki soat. Koʻpchilik ixtiyoriylar har kuni tushdan keyin bir-ikki kishiga yordam beradi.",82.4],["Alice","Do I need a car?","Mashina kerakmi?",88.2],["Receptionist","No. All the homes are nearby. Most volunteers walk, although some people use bicycles.","Yoʻq. Hamma uylar yaqin. Koʻpchilik piyoda boradi, baʼzilar velosipeddan foydalanadi.",90.2],["Alice","Great. Is there anything I should bring?","Zoʻr. Biror narsa olib kelishim kerakmi?",96.9],["Receptionist","We provide shopping bags, but please bring a phone in case you need to contact the centre while you're out.","Xarid xaltalarini oʻzimiz beramiz, lekin tashqarida markaz bilan bogʻlanish kerak boʻlib qolsa, telefon olib keling.",100.1],["Alice","OK. Is there any training before I start?","Xoʻp. Boshlashdan oldin biror oʻqitish bormi?",106.7],["Receptionist","Yes. Just a short meeting. The next one is on Monday evening and lasts about 40 minutes.","Ha. Shunchaki qisqa uchrashuv. Keyingisi dushanba kechqurun va taxminan 40 daqiqa davom etadi.",110.6],["Alice","Perfect. I can come to that.","Ajoyib. Men kela olaman.",117.5],["Receptionist","Wonderful. We really appreciate your help. The service is very important to people in the neighbourhood.","Juda yaxshi. Yordamingiz uchun chin dildan minnatdormiz. Bu xizmat mahalladagi odamlar uchun juda muhim.",120.2],["Alice","I'm happy to help.","Yordam berganimdan xursandman.",127.1]]},
{"id":"sb-22","u":22,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Trying something new","dur":138,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-22.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Adventure club, how can I help?","Xayrli kun. Adventure club, qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.2],["Jessica","Hi, I saw your advertisement for beginner activities. I'd like to try something new, but I'm not sure which activity to choose.","Salom, boshlovchilar uchun mashgʻulotlar haqidagi eʼloningizni koʻrdim. Yangi narsani sinab koʻrmoqchiman, lekin qaysi mashgʻulotni tanlashni bilmayapman.",9.1],["Receptionist","No problem. Can I take your name first?","Muammo yoʻq. Avval ismingizni olsam?",18.9],["Jessica","Yes, I'm Jessica Miles.","Ha, men Jessica Miles.",22.2],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25.2],["Jessica","Sure. It's M-I-L-E-S.","Albatta. M-I-L-E-S.",28],["Receptionist","Thank you. Have you done any adventure sports before?","Rahmat. Avval biror ekstremal sport bilan shugʻullanganmisiz?",33.1],["Jessica","Not really. I go swimming sometimes and I ride my bike at weekends, but I've never tried anything very exciting.","Unchalik emas. Baʼzan suzishga boraman, dam olish kunlari velosiped minaman, lekin hech qachon juda hayajonli narsani sinab koʻrmaganman.",37],["Receptionist","Well, we have several activities for beginners. You could try climbing, kayaking or horse riding.","Xoʻsh, bizda boshlovchilar uchun bir nechta mashgʻulot bor. Toqqa chiqish, qayiqda eshkak eshish yoki ot minishni sinab koʻrishingiz mumkin.",45.8],["Jessica","I'm a little afraid of heights, so climbing probably isn't for me. I think kayaking sounds the most interesting.","Men balandlikdan biroz qoʻrqaman, shuning uchun toqqa chiqish menga mos emas shekilli. Qayiqda eshkak eshish eng qiziqarli tuyulyapti.",53.1],["Receptionist","Good choice. Our beginner kayaking sessions take place at Blue Lake. You don't need any previous experience.","Yaxshi tanlov. Boshlovchilar uchun qayiq mashgʻulotlarimiz Blue Lake koʻlida oʻtadi. Oldingi tajriba kerak emas.",61.4],["Jessica","Great. When are the sessions?","Zoʻr. Mashgʻulotlar qachon?",69],["Receptionist","We have them on Saturday and Sunday mornings. Saturday is nearly full this week, so the other day would be better.","Ular shanba va yakshanba kunlari ertalab boʻladi. Shanba bu hafta deyarli band, shuning uchun ikkinchi kun yaxshiroq.",71.6],["Jessica","Sunday is fine. What time does it start?","Yakshanba mayli. Soat nechada boshlanadi?",79],["Receptionist","The activity starts at 10, but everyone needs to arrive by 9.30. The instructor will explain the safety rules before you go onto the water.","Mashgʻulot soat 10 da boshlanadi, lekin hamma 9.30 gacha kelishi kerak. Suvga chiqishingizdan oldin instruktor xavfsizlik qoidalarini tushuntiradi.",82.6],["Jessica","Okay. Do I need to bring any special equipment?","Xoʻp. Maxsus jihoz olib kelishim kerakmi?",91.8],["Receptionist","We provide the kayak, helmet and life jacket. You should bring a towel and some dry clothes because you may get wet.","Qayiq, shlem va qutqaruv jiletini oʻzimiz beramiz. Sochiq va quruq kiyim olib keling, chunki ivib qolishingiz mumkin.",95.8],["Jessica","I expected that. How long does the session last?","Buni kutgandim. Mashgʻulot qancha davom etadi?",103.6],["Receptionist","About two hours. There's a short break halfway through.","Taxminan ikki soat. Oʻrtasida qisqa tanaffus bor.",107.8],["Jessica","And how much does it cost?","Narxi qancha?",112.2],["Receptionist","The normal price is £25, but your first beginner session costs £18.","Odatdagi narxi £25, lekin birinchi boshlovchi mashgʻulotingiz £18 turadi.",114.6],["Jessica","That sounds good. I'd like to book it.","Yaxshi eshitilyapti. Buni band qilmoqchiman.",120.9],["Receptionist","Excellent. One final thing. The water can be quite cold, even in summer, so wearing warm clothes is a good idea.","Ajoyib. Oxirgi narsa. Suv yozda ham ancha sovuq boʻlishi mumkin, shuning uchun issiq kiyinib kelgan yaxshi.",124],["Jessica","Thanks. I'm a little nervous, but I'm excited to try it.","Rahmat. Biroz hayajonlanyapman, lekin sinab koʻrishni intiq kutyapman.",133.3]]},
{"id":"sb-23","u":23,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Interesting places and different cultures","dur":128,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-23.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. World Travel Club. How can I help?","Xayrli tong. World Travel Club. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",6.4],["Lucy","Hi. I saw your poster about the International Culture Day and I'd like some information.","Salom. Xalqaro madaniyat kuni haqidagi plakatingizni koʻrdim va maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",10.2],["Receptionist","Of course. Can I take your name first?","Albatta. Avval ismingizni olsam?",16.6],["Lucy","Yes. I'm Lucy Warren.","Ha. Men Lucy Warren.",19.8],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",22.7],["Lucy","Sure. It's W-A-R-R-E-N.","Albatta. W-A-R-R-E-N.",25.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. Culture Day is a chance to learn about different countries through food, music, clothes and activities. This year, the main country is Japan.","Rahmat. Madaniyat kuni turli mamlakatlar haqida taom, musiqa, kiyim va mashgʻulotlar orqali bilib olish imkoniyati. Bu yil asosiy mamlakat — Yaponiya.",30],["Lucy","That's great! I've always wanted to visit there. What activities will you have?","Zoʻr! Men u yerga doim borishni xohlaganman. Qanday mashgʻulotlar boʻladi?",41],["Receptionist","There are several. In the morning, a traveller will give a talk about Japanese cities and everyday life. It starts at 10.30 in the main hall.","Bir nechta. Ertalab sayyoh Yaponiya shaharlari va kundalik hayot haqida maʼruza qiladi. U asosiy zalda soat 10.30 da boshlanadi.",47],["Lucy","That sounds interesting. I'd like to hear about what daily life is really like there.","Qiziqarli eshitilyapti. U yerda kundalik hayot haqiqatan qanday ekanini eshitmoqchiman.",57],["Receptionist","After the talk, there's a short language lesson. You can learn some simple greetings and useful words.","Maʼruzadan keyin qisqa til darsi boʻladi. Bir nechta oddiy salomlashish va foydali soʻzlarni oʻrganishingiz mumkin.",63],["Lucy","Nice. What happens in the afternoon?","Yaxshi. Tushdan keyin nima boʻladi?",70],["Receptionist","At one o'clock, there's a cooking demonstration. The chef will show visitors how to prepare a traditional rice dish. Everyone can taste it afterwards.","Soat birda pazandalik namoyishi boʻladi. Oshpaz mehmonlarga guruchdan tayyorlanadigan milliy taomni qanday pishirishni koʻrsatadi. Keyin hamma tatib koʻrishi mumkin.",73],["Lucy","Excellent! I love trying food from other countries.","Ajoyib! Men boshqa mamlakatlar taomlarini tatib koʻrishni yaxshi koʻraman.",84],["Receptionist","There's also a display of traditional clothes. Some visitors can try them on and take photographs.","Milliy kiyimlar koʻrgazmasi ham bor. Baʼzi mehmonlar ularni kiyib koʻrib, suratga tushishi mumkin.",88],["Lucy","Do you have any music?","Musiqa ham bormi?",95],["Receptionist","Yes. A group of musicians will perform at three. They use traditional drums so the performance can be quite loud.","Ha. Soat uchda bir guruh musiqachilar chiqish qiladi. Ular milliy doʻmbiralardan foydalanadi, shuning uchun chiqish ancha shovqinli boʻlishi mumkin.",97],["Lucy","Sounds fun! How much does Culture Day cost?","Qiziqarli ekan! Madaniyat kuni qancha turadi?",105],["Receptionist","Adult tickets are normally £12, but students pay £8 if they bring a student card.","Kattalar chiptasi odatda £12, lekin talabalar talabalik guvohnomasini olib kelsa, £8 toʻlaydi.",110],["Lucy","Perfect! I'm a student. Where is the event?","Ajoyib! Men talabaman. Tadbir qayerda boʻladi?",116.3],["Receptionist","At the International Centre on Park Street, opposite the Museum.","Park Street dagi Xalqaro markazda, muzeyning roʻparasida.",120.7],["Lucy","Great! I'll definitely come.","Zoʻr! Albatta kelaman.",124.8]]},
{"id":"sb-24","u":24,"book":"Student's Book","title":"Life in the past and life today","dur":130,"audio":"audio/a2/student/unit-24.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome to Then and Now. Today we're talking about how everyday life has changed. Could you introduce yourself?","Then and Now dasturiga xush kelibsiz. Bugun kundalik hayot qanday oʻzgargani haqida gaplashamiz. Oʻzingizni tanishtirsangiz.",6.2],["Margaret","Of course. I'm Margaret Hill.","Albatta. Men Margaret Hill.",14.2],["Host","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",17.3],["Margaret","Yes, it's H-I-L-L.","Ha, H-I-L-L.",20.3],["Host","Thank you. Margaret, where did you grow up?","Rahmat. Margaret, qayerda katta boʻlgansiz?",24.6],["Margaret","I grew up in a small village. There were only a few shops and everybody seemed to know each other.","Men kichik qishloqda katta boʻlganman. Faqat bir nechta doʻkon bor edi va hamma bir-birini taniydigandek edi.",27.8],["Host","How did you usually get to school?","Maktabga odatda qanday borardingiz?",34.5],["Margaret","I normally walked. The school was about two kilometres from our house. My brother and I went together, even when the weather was bad.","Odatda piyoda borardim. Maktab uyimizdan taxminan ikki kilometr uzoqlikda edi. Akam bilan birga borardik, ob-havo yomon boʻlganda ham.",37.1],["Host","Did your family have a television?","Oilangizda televizor bormidi?",46.2],["Margaret","Yes, but only one. We got our first television when I was about ten. It was quite small and there weren't many programs to choose from.","Ha, lekin faqat bitta. Birinchi televizorimiz men taxminan oʻn yoshda boʻlganimda paydo boʻldi. U ancha kichik edi va tanlash uchun dasturlar koʻp emas edi.",49.1],["Host","That's very different from today. What did you do for entertainment?","Bu hozirgidan juda farq qiladi. Koʻngil ochish uchun nima qilardingiz?",60],["Margaret","We spent much more time outside. After school we played games in the street or rode our bikes. In the evening I often read books or listened to the radio.","Biz tashqarida ancha koʻp vaqt oʻtkazardik. Maktabdan keyin koʻchada oʻynardik yoki velosipedda aylanardik. Kechqurun koʻpincha kitob oʻqirdim yoki radio tinglardim.",65],["Host","What about shopping?","Xarid qilish-chi?",76],["Margaret","My mother went to the local shops almost every day because we didn't have a big fridge. There was no supermarket nearby. Today I usually go shopping only once a week.","Onam deyarli har kuni mahalliy doʻkonlarga borardi, chunki bizda katta muzlatkich yoʻq edi. Yaqin atrofda supermarket yoʻq edi. Bugun esa odatda haftada bir marta xarid qilaman.",78],["Host","How did people keep in touch with friends and family?","Odamlar doʻstlari va oila bilan qanday aloqada boʻlardi?",91.3],["Margaret","We wrote letters or used the telephone at home. Calls were quite expensive so we didn't stay on the phone for very long.","Biz xat yozardik yoki uydagi telefondan foydalanardik. Qoʻngʻiroqlar ancha qimmat edi, shuning uchun telefonda uzoq gaplashmasdik.",94.9],["Host","Which do you prefer? Life then or life today?","Qaysi biri yoqadi? Oʻsha davrdagi hayotmi yoki hozirgimi?",103.5],["Margaret","Some things were nicer in the past because people spent more time together, but everyday life is certainly easier today. I can speak to my grandchildren online, buy things from home and find information in seconds.","Baʼzi narsalar oʻtmishda yaxshiroq edi, chunki odamlar birga koʻproq vaqt oʻtkazardi, lekin kundalik hayot bugun, shubhasiz, osonroq. Nevaralarim bilan onlayn gaplasha olaman, uydan turib xarid qilaman va maʼlumotni soniyalarda topaman.",108],["Host","So technology has made a big difference.","Demak, texnologiya katta oʻzgarish qildi.",122.7],["Margaret","Definitely. I wouldn't want to give up the internet now.","Albatta. Hozir internetdan voz kechishni xohlamasdim.",125.8]]},
{"id":"wb-01","u":1,"book":"Workbook","title":"Daily routines and habits","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-01.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hello. I'm asking people about their daily habits for our college project. Could I ask you some questions?","Salom. Kollej loyihamiz uchun odamlardan kundalik odatlari haqida soʻrayapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",5.3],["Daniel","Of course.","Albatta.",12.6],["Interviewer","Thanks. First, what's your name?","Rahmat. Avval, ismingiz nima?",13.9],["Daniel","I'm Daniel Brooks.","Men Daniel Brooks.",17.7],["Interviewer","And could you spell your surname for me?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",19.8],["Daniel","Yes, it's B-R-O-O-K-S.","Ha, B-R-O-O-K-S.",22.7],["Interviewer","Great. Let's start with your morning routine. Do you get up early?","Zoʻr. Ertalabki tartibingizdan boshlaylik. Erta turasizmi?",27.8],["Daniel","Yes, because I start work quite early. My alarm rings at 6.20 and I usually get up 10 minutes later at 6.30. I wash my face, get dressed and then make breakfast.","Ha, chunki ishni ancha erta boshlayman. Budilnik 6.20 da chaladi, men odatda 10 daqiqadan keyin, 6.30 da turaman. Yuzimni yuvaman, kiyinaman va nonushta tayyorlayman.",33.3],["Interviewer","What do you normally have?","Odatda nima yeysiz?",46.4],["Daniel","I usually have toast with cheese. I sometimes have eggs at the weekend, but they take too long on work days. I always drink a glass of juice with breakfast.","Odatda pishloqli tost yeyman. Dam olish kunlari baʼzan tuxum yeyman, lekin ish kunlari u juda uzoq pishadi. Nonushtada doim bir stakan sharbat ichaman.",48.5],["Interviewer","How do you get to work?","Ishga qanday borasiz?",59.5],["Daniel","I usually cycle. I bought a new bicycle last year and I really enjoy riding it. If the weather is bad, I take the bus instead.","Odatda velosipedda boraman. Oʻtgan yili yangi velosiped sotib oldim va unda yurishni juda yaxshi koʻraman. Ob-havo yomon boʻlsa, oʻrniga avtobusga chiqaman.",61.6],["Interviewer","And what time do you start work?","Ishni soat nechada boshlaysiz?",70.8],["Daniel","At 8 o'clock. I work in a small hotel so mornings can be quite busy. I have lunch at about 12.30, usually in the staff room.","Soat 8 da. Kichik mehmonxonada ishlayman, shuning uchun ertalablari ancha band boʻladi. Tushlikni taxminan 12.30 da, odatda xodimlar xonasida qilaman.",73.4],["Interviewer","What do you do when you finish work?","Ishdan keyin nima qilasiz?",83.4],["Daniel","I finish at 4. On Thursdays, I meet my brother and we play tennis in the park. On other weekdays, I normally go home and relax.","Soat 4 da tugataman. Payshanba kunlari akam bilan uchrashamiz va bogʻda tennis oʻynaymiz. Boshqa ish kunlari odatda uyga borib dam olaman.",85.9],["Interviewer","Do you cook in the evening?","Kechqurun ovqat pishirasizmi?",95.3],["Daniel","Most days. I usually make something simple because I don't like spending hours in the kitchen. After dinner, I often listen to music or watch a film.","Koʻp kunlari. Odatda oddiy narsa tayyorlayman, chunki oshxonada soatlab vaqt oʻtkazishni yoqtirmayman. Kechki ovqatdan keyin koʻpincha musiqa tinglayman yoki film koʻraman.",97.6],["Interviewer","What about bedtime?","Uxlash vaqti-chi?",108.1],["Daniel","I usually go to bed at 10.30, but I don't fall asleep immediately. I normally read a few pages of a book first.","Odatda soat 10.30 da yotaman, lekin darrov uxlab qolmayman. Avval odatda kitobdan bir necha sahifa oʻqiyman.",110.2],["Interviewer","And do you follow the same routine at weekends?","Dam olish kunlari ham shu tartibga amal qilasizmi?",118.7],["Daniel","Not at all. On Sunday mornings, I sleep longer and usually go for a walk after breakfast.","Aslo. Yakshanba kunlari ertalab koʻproq uxlayman va odatda nonushtadan keyin sayr qilaman.",122.3]],"q":[{"t":"What time does Daniel get up?","o":["6.20","6.30","7.30"],"a":1,"why":"Budilnik 6.20 da chaladi, lekin u 10 daqiqadan keyin turadi."},{"t":"How does Daniel go to work when the weather is bad?","o":["He takes the bus.","He walks.","He drives."],"a":0},{"t":"What does Daniel do on Thursdays after work?","o":["He cooks dinner.","He goes for a walk.","He plays tennis with his brother."],"a":2},{"t":"What time does Daniel finish work?","o":["12.30","4 o'clock","10.30"],"a":1},{"t":"What does Daniel do before he goes to sleep?","o":["He reads a few pages of a book.","He listens to music.","He plays tennis."],"a":0}]},
{"id":"wb-02","u":2,"book":"Workbook","title":"Family, Friends and Relationships","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-02.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hello. I'm doing a short project about the people who are important in our lives. Would you mind answering a few questions?","Salom. Men hayotimizdagi muhim insonlar haqida qisqa loyiha qilyapman. Bir nechta savolga javob berasizmi?",6.1],["Oliver","No, that's fine.","Yoʻq, mayli.",13.5],["Interviewer","Thanks. Let's start with your name.","Rahmat. Ismingizdan boshlaylik.",16.3],["Oliver","I'm Oliver Reed.","Men Oliver Reed.",18.5],["Interviewer","Is that R-E-A-D?","Bu R-E-A-D mi?",21.6],["Oliver","No, it's R-E-E-D.","Yoʻq, R-E-E-D.",24],["Interviewer","Got it. Now, Oliver, who do you live with?","Tushunarli. Endi, Oliver, kim bilan yashaysiz?",26.9],["Oliver","I live with my mum, my dad and my older sister, Hannah. She's 23. She used to live away from home when she was at university, but she moved back last summer.","Onam, dadam va katta opam Hannah bilan yashayman. U 23 yoshda. Universitetda oʻqiyotganida uydan uzoqda yashagan, lekin oʻtgan yozda qaytib kelgan.",32.2],["Interviewer","Do you and Hannah get on well?","Siz va Hannah inoq yashaysizlarmi?",43.2],["Oliver","Most of the time. She's very helpful, and I can talk to her when I have a problem. We have different interests, though. She loves reading, while I prefer playing computer games.","Koʻpincha ha. U juda yordamchi, muammom boʻlsa u bilan gaplasha olaman. Lekin qiziqishlarimiz boshqa. U kitob oʻqishni yaxshi koʻradi, men esa kompyuter oʻyinlarini afzal koʻraman.",45.7],["Interviewer","Do you do anything together?","Birga biror ish qilasizlarmi?",57.2],["Oliver","Yes. We both enjoy cooking, so on Sunday evenings we usually make dinner for our parents. Last Sunday we made chicken and rice.","Ha. Ikkalamiz ham ovqat pishirishni yaxshi koʻramiz, shuning uchun yakshanba kechqurunlari odatda ota-onamizga kechki ovqat tayyorlaymiz. Oʻtgan yakshanba tovuq va guruch pishirdik.",59.7],["Interviewer","Is there anyone else in your family you see regularly?","Oilangizda muntazam koʻrishadigan yana kim bor?",68.9],["Oliver","My uncle lives nearby. He has two young children, so I sometimes look after them. I usually help on Friday afternoons when he's still at work.","Amakim yaqin atrofda yashaydi. Uning ikkita kichik farzandi bor, shuning uchun baʼzan ularga qarab turaman. Odatda juma kunlari tushdan keyin, u hali ishda boʻlganida yordam beraman.",72.6],["Interviewer","Now, tell me about your friends.","Endi doʻstlaringiz haqida gapirib bering.",82.4],["Oliver","My closest friend is Sam. We first met at a football club about six years ago. He doesn't play football anymore, but we still spend a lot of time together.","Eng yaqin doʻstim Sam. Biz birinchi marta taxminan olti yil oldin futbol klubida uchrashganmiz. U endi futbol oʻynamaydi, lekin biz hali ham koʻp vaqt birga oʻtkazamiz.",85.3],["Interviewer","What's Sam like?","Sam qanday inson?",95.7],["Oliver","He's quiet when you first meet him, but he's very kind. He's also patient, which is useful because I'm sometimes a little impatient.","Dastlab tanishganda u jim, lekin juda mehribon. U sabrli ham, bu foydali, chunki men baʼzan sal sabrsizman.",97.5],["Interviewer","How often do you see him?","Uni qanchalik tez-tez koʻrasiz?",107.1],["Oliver","Usually twice a week. We meet at the library on Wednesday because we're both studying for exams. At the weekend, we sometimes play basketball or go out for lunch.","Odatda haftada ikki marta. Chorshanba kuni kutubxonada uchrashamiz, chunki ikkalamiz ham imtihonlarga tayyorlanyapmiz. Dam olish kunlari baʼzan basketbol oʻynaymiz yoki tushlik qilgani chiqamiz.",109.4],["Interviewer","And how do you keep in touch on other days?","Boshqa kunlari qanday aloqada boʻlasizlar?",120.2],["Oliver","Mostly by text. We rarely phone each other because messaging is easier.","Asosan xabar orqali. Bir-birimizga kamdan-kam qoʻngʻiroq qilamiz, chunki xabar yozish osonroq.",123.2]],"q":[{"t":"How old is Oliver's sister, Hannah?","o":["20","23","32"],"a":1},{"t":"When does Oliver usually help his uncle?","o":["On Friday afternoons","On Sunday evenings","On Wednesday evenings"],"a":0},{"t":"Where did Oliver and Sam first meet?","o":["At the library","At university","At a football club"],"a":2},{"t":"Why do Oliver and Sam meet at the library on Wednesday?","o":["They play basketball there.","They are studying for exams.","They have lunch there."],"a":1,"why":"Ular imtihonlarga tayyorlanishadi."},{"t":"How do Oliver and Sam usually keep in touch?","o":["By text","By phone","By email"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"wb-03","u":3,"book":"Workbook","title":"Hobbies and Free Time","dur":132,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-03.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hello, I'm asking students about their hobbies for our college website. Can I ask you a few questions?","Salom, men kollejimiz veb-sayti uchun talabalardan hobbilari haqida soʻrayapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",4.8],["Leo","Sure.","Albatta.",12.5],["Interviewer","Thanks. Can I start with your name?","Rahmat. Ismingizdan boshlasam boʻladimi?",13.8],["Leo","Yes, I'm Leo Martin.","Ha, men Leo Martin.",17.4],["Interviewer","Sorry, how do you spell your surname?","Kechirasiz, familiyangiz qanday yoziladi?",20.5],["Leo","It's M-A-R-T-I-N.","M-A-R-T-I-N.",23.6],["Interviewer","Thank you. So, Leo, what do you usually do when you have some free time?","Rahmat. Xoʻsh, Leo, boʻsh vaqtingiz boʻlsa odatda nima qilasiz?",27.3],["Leo","I really enjoy being outdoors. My main hobby is cycling. I sometimes ride around town, but at weekends I prefer going into the countryside because the roads are quieter.","Men tashqarida boʻlishni juda yaxshi koʻraman. Asosiy hobbim velosiped haydash. Baʼzan shahar boʻylab haydayman, lekin dam olish kunlari qishloqqa chiqishni afzal koʻraman, chunki yoʻllar tinchroq.",34.5],["Interviewer","Do you go cycling every weekend?","Har dam olish kuni velosiped haydaysizmi?",46.6],["Leo","Almost. I normally go on Sunday morning. I used to go on Saturdays, but I started working at a café on Saturday mornings about three months ago.","Deyarli. Odatda yakshanba ertalab chiqaman. Oldin shanba kunlari chiqardim, lekin taxminan uch oy oldin shanba ertalablari kafeda ishlay boshladim.",49.3],["Interviewer","Do you cycle alone?","Yolgʻiz haydaysizmi?",59.5],["Leo","Sometimes, but I usually go with my cousin. We leave home quite early, usually at about 8.30, because there aren't many cars on the road then. We normally ride for two hours and stop somewhere for a drink.","Baʼzan, lekin odatda amakivachcham bilan boraman. Uydan ancha erta, odatda soat 8.30 atrofida chiqamiz, chunki u payt yoʻlda mashina kam boʻladi. Odatda ikki soat haydaymiz va biror joyda ichimlik ichish uchun toʻxtaymiz.",61.7],["Interviewer","What do you do when the weather is bad?","Ob-havo yomon boʻlsa nima qilasiz?",75.9],["Leo","Then I stay indoors. I'm learning to play the guitar at the moment. I'm still a beginner, so I practice simple songs. I try to practice several times during the week.","Unda uyda qolaman. Hozir gitara chalishni oʻrganyapman. Hali boshlovchiman, shuning uchun oddiy qoʻshiqlarni mashq qilaman. Hafta davomida bir necha marta mashq qilishga harakat qilaman.",78.7],["Interviewer","Do you have any other hobbies?","Yana boshqa hobbilaringiz bormi?",90.2],["Leo","Yes. I like playing chess. There's a small club at my college, and we meet every Wednesday after classes. I'm not the best player there, but it's fun, and I'm getting better.","Ha. Shaxmat oʻynashni yaxshi koʻraman. Kollejimizda kichik klub bor, har chorshanba darsdan keyin yigʻilamiz. Men u yerdagi eng yaxshi oʻyinchi emasman, lekin qiziq va yaxshilanib boryapman.",92.6],["Interviewer","How do you usually relax in the evening?","Kechqurun odatda qanday dam olasiz?",104.4],["Leo","I sometimes watch films, but I spend more time listening to podcasts. I like ones about travel, because I enjoy learning about different countries.","Baʼzan film koʻraman, lekin koʻproq vaqtimni podkastlar tinglashga sarflayman. Sayohat haqidagilarini yoqtiraman, chunki turli davlatlar haqida bilishni yaxshi koʻraman.",107.7],["Interviewer","Is there a hobby you'd like to try in the future?","Kelajakda sinab koʻrmoqchi boʻlgan hobbingiz bormi?",117.5],["Leo","I'd like to try fishing. My uncle goes quite often, and he says he'll take me with him this summer.","Baliq ovlashni sinab koʻrmoqchiman. Amakim ancha tez-tez boradi va bu yozda meni ham olib ketishini aytdi.",121.2],["Interviewer","Great. Thanks, Leo.","Zoʻr. Rahmat, Leo.",127.8],["Leo","No problem.","Arzimaydi.",130.1]],"q":[{"t":"Why does Leo cycle on Sunday now, not on Saturday?","o":["He plays chess on Saturdays.","He works at a café on Saturday mornings.","The roads are busy on Saturdays."],"a":1,"why":"U shanba ertalablari kafeda ishlaydi."},{"t":"What time do Leo and his cousin usually leave home?","o":["About 8.30","About 7.30","About 9.30"],"a":0},{"t":"When does the chess club meet?","o":["On Sunday mornings","On Saturday afternoons","On Wednesdays after classes"],"a":2},{"t":"What kind of podcasts does Leo like?","o":["About music","About travel","About sport"],"a":1},{"t":"Who will take Leo fishing this summer?","o":["His uncle","His cousin","His friend"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"wb-04","u":4,"book":"Workbook","title":"Food, Cooking and Eating","dur":138,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-04.mp3","lines":[["Interviewer","Hi, I'm collecting information about how people cook and eat at home. Could I ask you a few questions?","Salom, men odamlar uyda qanday ovqat pishirishi va yeyishi haqida maʼlumot yigʻyapman. Bir nechta savol bersam boʻladimi?",5.5],["Adam","Sure.","Albatta.",12.5],["Interviewer","Thanks. Can I have your name first?","Rahmat. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",14.6],["Adam","Yes, I'm Adam Foster.","Ha, men Adam Foster.",17],["Interviewer","Sorry, could you spell your surname?","Kechirasiz, familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",21.3],["Adam","Of course, it's F-O-S-T-E-R.","Albatta, F-O-S-T-E-R.",24],["Interviewer","Great. Adam, do you usually have a big breakfast?","Zoʻr. Adam, odatda toʻyimli nonushta qilasizmi?",28.5],["Adam","Not really. I'm often in a hurry in the morning. I used to eat just a banana, but these days I normally make toast and have it with some cheese. I drink a glass of water too.","Unchalik emas. Ertalab koʻpincha shoshaman. Oldin faqat banan yer edim, lekin hozir odatda tost qilib, uni pishloq bilan yeyman. Bir stakan suv ham ichaman.",34.6],["Interviewer","What about lunch? Do you cook something?","Tushlik-chi? Biror narsa pishirasizmi?",46.4],["Adam","No, because I'm at college during the day. There's a café next to the library. I usually buy lunch there at about one o'clock. The sandwiches are good, but I normally choose soup because it's cheaper.","Yoʻq, chunki kunduzi kollejdaman. Kutubxona yonida kafe bor. Tushlikni odatda u yerdan soat birlarda sotib olaman. Sendvichlar yaxshi, lekin odatda shoʻrva tanlayman, chunki arzonroq.",49.9],["Interviewer","How much does lunch usually cost?","Tushlik odatda qancha turadi?",62.2],["Adam","The soup used to be £4, but it went up recently. It now costs £5. A sandwich is about £6, so I still save some money.","Shoʻrva oldin £4 edi, lekin yaqinda qimmatlashdi. Hozir £5 turadi. Sendvich taxminan £6, shuning uchun baribir biroz pul tejayman.",65.1],["Interviewer","Do you cook in the evening?","Kechqurun ovqat pishirasizmi?",75.3],["Adam","Yes. I share a flat with my friend Ben, and we take turns cooking. I cook on Mondays, Wednesdays and Saturdays. Ben cooks on the other days.","Ha. Doʻstim Ben bilan bitta kvartirada turaman va navbatma-navbat ovqat pishiramiz. Men dushanba, chorshanba va shanba kunlari pishiraman. Qolgan kunlari Ben pishiradi.",77.6],["Interviewer","What are you good at making?","Nimani yaxshi pishirasiz?",88.2],["Adam","I make a really good masala. It's quite simple. I use potatoes, onions, tomatoes and some spices. Ben prefers my pasta, but curry is my favourite.","Men juda yaxshi masala pishiraman. Bu ancha oddiy. Kartoshka, piyoz, pomidor va bir oz ziravorlar ishlataman. Ben mening pastamni afzal koʻradi, lekin eng yaxshi koʻrganim karri.",90.4],["Interviewer","Do you ever invite people for dinner?","Hech kimni kechki ovqatga taklif qilasizmi?",102.6],["Adam","Sometimes. We usually invite a few friends once a month. Everyone brings something, so we don't have to prepare all the food ourselves.","Baʼzan. Odatda oyda bir marta bir necha doʻstimizni taklif qilamiz. Hamma nimadir olib keladi, shuning uchun hamma ovqatni oʻzimiz tayyorlamaymiz.",105.4],["Interviewer","What do you usually bring when someone else invites you?","Boshqalar sizni taklif qilganda odatda nima olib borasiz?",114.2],["Adam","I normally bring juice or something sweet. I'm terrible at making desserts, so I usually buy them from a shop.","Odatda sharbat yoki biror shirinlik olib boraman. Desert tayyorlashni umuman bilmayman, shuning uchun odatda doʻkondan sotib olaman.",118.2],["Interviewer","Is there anything you want to learn to cook?","Pishirishni oʻrganmoqchi boʻlgan narsangiz bormi?",125.7],["Adam","Yes. Bread. My grandmother makes amazing bread, and I'd like her to teach me.","Ha. Non. Buvim ajoyib non yopadi va u menga oʻrgatishini xohlayman.",128.6],["Interviewer","Great. Thanks for your time.","Zoʻr. Vaqtingiz uchun rahmat.",135]],"q":[{"t":"What does Adam usually have for breakfast these days?","o":["Toast with cheese","Just a banana","Cereal and tea"],"a":0,"why":"Oldin faqat banan yer edi, hozir tost va pishloq."},{"t":"How much does the soup cost now?","o":["£4","£6","£5"],"a":2},{"t":"On which days does Adam cook?","o":["Tuesdays, Thursdays and Sundays","Mondays, Wednesdays and Saturdays","Mondays, Fridays and Sundays"],"a":1},{"t":"What does Adam usually bring when someone invites him for dinner?","o":["Juice or something sweet","Bread","Homemade desserts"],"a":0,"why":"U desert tayyorlashni bilmaydi, shuning uchun sotib oladi."},{"t":"Who does Adam want to learn to make bread from?","o":["His friend Ben","His mother","His grandmother"],"a":2}]},
{"id":"wb-05","u":5,"book":"Workbook","title":"Shopping and money","dur":127,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-05.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning. Green Street Market. How can I help?","Xayrli tong. Green Street bozori. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.7],["Rachel","Hi. I'm calling about the weekend market. I'd like to sell some things there on Saturday.","Salom. Men dam olish kunlaridagi bozor haqida qoʻngʻiroq qilyapman. Shanba kuni u yerda baʼzi narsalarni sotmoqchiman.",8.5],["Receptionist","Of course. I just need to take a few details. What's your name?","Albatta. Bir nechta maʼlumotni yozib olishim kerak. Ismingiz nima?",15],["Rachel","Rachel King.","Rachel King.",20.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",21.9],["Rachel","Yes. It's K-I-N-G.","Ha. K-I-N-G.",24.7],["Receptionist","Thank you. And what are you planning to sell?","Rahmat. Nima sotmoqchisiz?",29.4],["Rachel","Mostly clothes. I have some jackets and t-shirts that I don't wear anymore. I also have a few books, but I think clothes will be the main thing.","Asosan kiyim. Endi kiymaydigan bir nechta kurtka va futbolkam bor. Bir nechta kitobim ham bor, lekin asosiysi kiyim boʻladi deb oʻylayman.",33.3],["Receptionist","That's fine. You'll need to rent a table. We have small and large ones available.","Yaxshi. Stol ijaraga olishingiz kerak. Kichik va katta stollarimiz bor.",43.7],["Rachel","How much are they?","Ular qancha turadi?",50.4],["Receptionist","A large table is £15 for the day. The small one used to cost £8, but from this month,","Katta stol bir kunga £15. Kichigi avval £8 turardi, lekin shu oydan boshlab",52.1],["Rachel","it's £10. I think the small one will be enough.","£10 boʻldi. Menimcha, kichigi yetarli boʻladi.",59.4],["Receptionist","OK. The market opens to customers at 10, but sellers need to arrive earlier. Please be there by 9.15, so you have time to prepare your table.","Xoʻp. Bozor xaridorlar uchun soat 10 da ochiladi, lekin sotuvchilar barvaqt kelishi kerak. Iltimos, stolingizni tayyorlashga vaqt boʻlishi uchun 9.15 gacha keling.",64.4],["Rachel","That's fine. Where exactly is the market?","Mayli. Bozor aynan qayerda?",75.5],["Receptionist","It's in Green Street Hall. Do you know the building?","Green Street Hall ichida. Bu binoni bilasizmi?",79],["Rachel","I know Green Street, but I'm not sure about the hall.","Green Street koʻchasini bilaman, lekin zalni aniq bilmayman.",83],["Receptionist","It's opposite the bank. There's a café on one side and a pharmacy on the other, so it's quite easy to find.","U bankning roʻparasida. Bir tomonida kafe, ikkinchi tomonida dorixona bor, shuning uchun topish ancha oson.",87.3],["Rachel","Great. Can customers pay by card?","Zoʻr. Xaridorlar karta bilan toʻlay oladimi?",95.4],["Receptionist","Some sellers accept cards, but you would need your own card machine. Most people bring cash, especially for cheaper things.","Baʼzi sotuvchilar karta qabul qiladi, lekin buning uchun oʻzingizning karta terminalingiz boʻlishi kerak. Koʻpchilik naqd pul olib keladi, ayniqsa arzonroq narsalar uchun.",98.7],["Rachel","OK. I'll remember that.","Xoʻp. Buni eslab qolaman.",107.4],["Receptionist","One more thing. Sellers must bring their own bags for customers. We provide the tables and chairs, but not bags.","Yana bir narsa. Sotuvchilar xaridorlar uchun oʻzlarining xaltalarini olib kelishi kerak. Stol va stullarni biz beramiz, xalta esa yoʻq.",109.8],["Rachel","No problem. I have plenty at home.","Muammo yoʻq. Uyda juda koʻp bor.",118.4],["Receptionist","Excellent. We'll see you on Saturday.","Ajoyib. Shanba kuni koʻrishamiz.",121.5],["Rachel","Thanks. Bye.","Rahmat. Xayr.",124.8]],"q":[{"t":"What time must sellers arrive at the market?","o":["At 9","At 9.15","At 10"],"a":1,"why":"Xaridorlar 10 da kiradi, sotuvchilar 9.15 gacha kelishi kerak."},{"t":"How much is a small table now?","o":["£10","£8","£15"],"a":0,"why":"£8 eski narx, shu oydan £10 boʻldi."},{"t":"Where is Green Street Hall?","o":["Opposite the pharmacy","Opposite the café","Opposite the bank"],"a":2},{"t":"What must sellers bring themselves?","o":["Bags for customers","Tables","Chairs"],"a":0},{"t":"How do most people pay at the market?","o":["By card","With cash","By phone"],"a":1}]},
{"id":"wb-06","u":6,"book":"Workbook","title":"School, Learning and Study","dur":132,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-06.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, City Study Centre, how can I help?","Salom, City Study Centre, sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.3],["Marcus","Hi, I'm interested in your weekend computer course. I saw a poster about it at my college.","Salom, men sizlarning dam olish kunlaridagi kompyuter kursingizga qiziqyapman. Bu haqda kollejimizda plakat koʻrdim.",9.1],["Receptionist","Certainly, I can give you some information. First, can I take your name?","Albatta, sizga maʼlumot bera olaman. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",15],["Marcus","Yes, it's Marcus Hill.","Ha, men Marcus Hill.",21.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",24.6],["Marcus","Of course, it's H-I-L-L.","Albatta, H-I-L-L.",27],["Receptionist","Thanks. Have you done a computer course before?","Rahmat. Avval kompyuter kursida oʻqiganmisiz?",32.5],["Marcus","No, but I use a computer every day for my studies. I can type and find information online, but I'd like to learn more.","Yoʻq, lekin oʻqishim uchun har kuni kompyuterdan foydalanaman. Matn terishni va internetdan maʼlumot topishni bilaman, lekin koʻproq oʻrganmoqchiman.",36.5],["Receptionist","Then the beginner course should be suitable. Classes are on Saturday mornings. We used to have a Sunday class too, but that isn't running this term.","Unda boshlangʻich kurs mos boʻlsa kerak. Darslar shanba kuni ertalab boʻladi. Avval yakshanba kuni ham dars bor edi, lekin bu semestrda u ochilmayapti.",45.7],["Marcus","Saturday is perfect. What time does it start?","Shanba juda yaxshi. Soat nechada boshlanadi?",55.8],["Receptionist","The building opens at 9, but the lesson begins at 9.30. Each lesson lasts two hours.","Bino soat 9 da ochiladi, lekin dars 9.30 da boshlanadi. Har bir dars ikki soat davom etadi.",59.7],["Marcus","OK, what do students learn?","Xoʻp, oʻquvchilar nimalarni oʻrganadi?",67.2],["Receptionist","During the first few weeks, you'll learn how to create documents and organise files. Later, you'll learn to make simple presentations. There's also a lesson about using the internet safely.","Dastlabki bir necha haftada hujjatlar yaratish va fayllarni tartibga solishni oʻrganasiz. Keyinroq oddiy taqdimotlar yasashni oʻrganasiz. Internetdan xavfsiz foydalanish haqida ham dars bor.",70.2],["Marcus","That sounds useful. Do I need to bring my own computer?","Bu foydali ekan. Oʻz kompyuterimni olib kelishim kerakmi?",83.2],["Receptionist","No. Every student can use one of our computers. You should bring a notebook though, because the teacher gives lots of useful tips.","Yoʻq. Har bir oʻquvchi bizning kompyuterlarimizdan birini ishlatishi mumkin. Lekin daftar olib kelganingiz yaxshi, chunki oʻqituvchi juda koʻp foydali maslahatlar beradi.",87.4],["Marcus","Fine. How much is the course?","Yaxshi. Kurs qancha turadi?",96.5],["Receptionist","The full course is £75. It was £85 last term, so it's a little cheaper now.","Toʻliq kurs £75. Oʻtgan semestrda £85 edi, shuning uchun hozir biroz arzonroq.",99.3],["Marcus","Good. Where exactly is the study centre?","Yaxshi. Oʻquv markazi aynan qayerda?",107.5],["Receptionist","We're on King Road, opposite the library. Your lessons will be in room 8, which is on the first floor.","Biz King Road koʻchasida, kutubxonaning roʻparasidamiz. Darslaringiz 8-xonada boʻladi, u birinchi qavatda.",111],["Marcus","Great. Can I register online?","Zoʻr. Onlayn roʻyxatdan oʻta olamanmi?",118.2],["Receptionist","Yes. Or you can come to the centre and complete a form here.","Ha. Yoki markazga kelib, shu yerda anketa toʻldirishingiz mumkin.",121.1],["Marcus","I think I'll do it online tonight.","Menimcha, bugun kechqurun onlayn qilaman.",126.4],["Receptionist","Perfect. We hope to see you soon.","Ajoyib. Tez orada koʻrishamiz degan umiddamiz.",128.9]],"q":[{"t":"What time does the lesson begin?","o":["At 9.00","At 9.15","At 9.30"],"a":2,"why":"Bino 9 da ochiladi, dars 9.30 da boshlanadi."},{"t":"How long is each lesson?","o":["One hour","Two hours","Three hours"],"a":1},{"t":"What should Marcus bring to the lessons?","o":["A notebook","A computer","A poster"],"a":0},{"t":"How much is the full course now?","o":["£85","£75","£65"],"a":1,"why":"£85 oʻtgan semestrdagi narx edi."},{"t":"Where will the lessons be?","o":["Room 8 on the first floor","Room 8 on the second floor","Room 18 on the first floor"],"a":0}]},
{"id":"wb-07","u":7,"book":"Workbook","title":"Jobs and Working Life","dur":130,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-07.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Bright office services. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. Bright office services. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.1],["Maya","Hi. I'm calling about the part-time office job you advertised.","Salom. Siz eʼlon qilgan yarim kunlik ofis ishi boʻyicha qoʻngʻiroq qilyapman.",9.2],["Receptionist","Of course. Can I take your name first?","Albatta. Avval ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",13.8],["Maya","Yes. It's Maya Evans.","Ha. Men Maya Evans.",17.2],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",20.3],["Maya","Sure. It's E-V-A-N-S.","Albatta. E-V-A-N-S.",23.1],["Receptionist","Thank you. The job is for an office assistant. Have you done office work before?","Rahmat. Ish ofis yordamchisi uchun. Ilgari ofisda ishlaganmisiz?",28],["Maya","A little. Last year I worked in my uncle's business for two months. I answered emails, organised papers and sometimes spoke to customers on the phone.","Ozgina. Oʻtgan yili amakimning biznesida ikki oy ishladim. Elektron xatlarga javob berdim, qogʻozlarni tartibga soldim va baʼzan mijozlar bilan telefonda gaplashdim.",34],["Receptionist","Good. Being organised is very important here because we have a lot of documents and customer information.","Yaxshi. Bu yerda tartibli boʻlish juda muhim, chunki bizda hujjatlar va mijozlar maʼlumoti koʻp.",45.2],["Maya","That's fine. I like keeping things in the right place.","Muammo yoʻq. Men narsalarni oʻz joyida saqlashni yaxshi koʻraman.",52.5],["Receptionist","Excellent. The job is three days a week. Monday, Wednesday and Friday. On Mondays and Fridays, you start at nine, but on Wednesday you start at ten o'clock because we have a staff meeting first.","Zoʻr. Ish haftasiga uch kun: dushanba, chorshanba va juma. Dushanba va juma kunlari soat toʻqqizda boshlaysiz, chorshanba kuni esa soat oʻnda, chunki avval xodimlar yigʻilishi boʻladi.",56.6],["Maya","That works well for me. What would I usually do during the day?","Bu menga juda mos. Kun davomida odatda nima qilaman?",70.3],["Receptionist","Mostly answer emails and prepare documents. You'll also take messages when customers phone. Sometimes we'll ask you to make copies of documents for meetings.","Asosan elektron xatlarga javob berasiz va hujjatlar tayyorlaysiz. Mijozlar telefon qilganda xabarlarni ham qabul qilasiz. Baʼzan yigʻilishlar uchun hujjat nusxalarini koʻpaytirishni soʻraymiz.",75],["Maya","Okay. Do I need to wear anything special?","Xop. Maxsus biror narsa kiyishim kerakmi?",85.7],["Receptionist","Nothing too formal. A shirt or smart top is fine, but please wear black shoes. Trainers aren't suitable in the office.","Juda rasmiy emas. Koʻylak yoki chiroyli kofta boʻlsa boʻladi, lekin iltimos, qora poyabzal kiying. Ofisda krossovka mos emas.",89.6],["Maya","No problem. How much do you pay?","Muammo yoʻq. Qancha toʻlaysiz?",98.8],["Receptionist","The starting rate is £12 an hour. After three months, it can increase if everything goes well.","Boshlangʻich stavka soatiga £12. Uch oydan keyin, hammasi yaxshi ketsa, oshishi mumkin.",101.8],["Maya","Great. How can I apply?","Zoʻr. Qanday ariza topshiraman?",108.4],["Receptionist","Please bring your CV to the office. Ask for Mr Taylor at the front desk. He's interviewing applicants on Tuesday and Thursday this week.","Iltimos, rezyumengizni ofisga olib keling. Qabulxonada janob Taylorni soʻrang. U shu hafta seshanba va payshanba kunlari nomzodlar bilan suhbat oʻtkazadi.",111],["Maya","Thursday would be better for me.","Payshanba men uchun yaxshiroq.",120.2],["Receptionist","Perfect. Come any time between two and four.","Ajoyib. Soat ikkidan toʻrtgacha istalgan payt keling.",122.8],["Maya","Thanks very much.","Katta rahmat.",126.8],["Receptionist","You're welcome.","Arzimaydi.",128.8]]},
{"id":"wb-08","u":8,"book":"Workbook","title":"Travel and transport","dur":130,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-08.mp3","lines":[["Clerk","Good afternoon. Northside train station. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. Northside temir yoʻl bekati. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.8],["Sarah","Hi. I'm travelling to Brighton tomorrow and I'd like some information about the trains.","Salom. Ertaga Brightonga boraman va poyezdlar haqida maʼlumot olmoqchiman.",9.3],["Clerk","Certainly. Are you travelling in the morning or afternoon?","Albatta. Ertalab yoki tushdan keyin yoʻlga chiqasizmi?",15.6],["Sarah","In the morning. I need to be in Brighton before lunch time.","Ertalab. Tushlikdan oldin Brightonda boʻlishim kerak.",20.1],["Clerk","No problem. Before I check the trains, could I take your name?","Muammo yoʻq. Poyezdlarni tekshirishdan oldin ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",24.6],["Sarah","Yes. It's Sarah Blake.","Ha. Men Sarah Blake.",29.3],["Clerk","Could you spell your surname for me?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",31.5],["Sarah","Of course. It's B-L-A-K-E.","Albatta. B-L-A-K-E.",34.8],["Clerk","Thank you. Now, there's a train at 8.10 but that one stops at every station. The faster train leaves at 8.40.","Rahmat. Endi, soat 8.10 da poyezd bor, lekin u har bir bekatda toʻxtaydi. Tezroq poyezd 8.40 da joʻnaydi.",38],["Sarah","I'd prefer the faster one. Does it go directly to Brighton?","Tezroq poyezdni afzal koʻraman. U Brightonga toʻgʻridan-toʻgʻri boradimi?",48.6],["Clerk","Not quite. You need to change once at Greenford. Don't worry. You'll have about 20 minutes to get to the next train.","Unchalik emas. Greenfordda bir marta almashtirishingiz kerak. Xavotir olmang. Keyingi poyezdga yetib olish uchun taxminan 20 daqiqangiz boʻladi.",53.4],["Sarah","That should be enough. How much is the ticket?","Bu yetarli boʻlsa kerak. Chipta qancha turadi?",61.4],["Clerk","A normal single ticket is £22. But if you have a student card, it's only £17.","Oddiy bir tomonlama chipta £22. Lekin talabalik kartangiz boʻlsa, atigi £17.",64.8],["Sarah","Great. I'm a student and I have my card with me.","Zoʻr. Men talabaman va kartam yonimda.",72.2],["Clerk","Perfect. Would you like to reserve a seat?","Ajoyib. Joy band qilmoqchimisiz?",76.1],["Sarah","Yes, please. I'd rather sit by the window if possible. I don't really like aisle seats.","Ha, iltimos. Imkon boʻlsa, deraza yonida oʻtirganim yaxshi. Yoʻlak tomondagi joylarni unchalik yoqtirmayman.",79.2],["Clerk","That's fine. There are still several window seats available.","Boʻladi. Deraza yonida hali bir nechta boʻsh joy bor.",85.8],["Sarah","Great. Can I take my bicycle on the train?","Zoʻr. Velosipedimni poyezdga olib chiqsam boʻladimi?",89.8],["Clerk","Yes, but there's only space for four bicycles, so you need to book a place for it before travelling.","Ha, lekin faqat toʻrtta velosiped uchun joy bor, shuning uchun yoʻlga chiqishdan oldin unga joy band qilishingiz kerak.",93.8],["Sarah","OK. Where should I go when I arrive at the station tomorrow?","Xop. Ertaga bekatga kelganimda qayerga borishim kerak?",101],["Clerk","Your train normally leaves from Platform 5, but tomorrow it will leave from Platform 3 because some work is being done near Platform 5.","Poyezdingiz odatda 5-platformadan joʻnaydi, lekin ertaga 3-platformadan joʻnaydi, chunki 5-platforma yonida taʼmirlash ishlari olib borilyapti.",105.8],["Sarah","I'm glad I asked.","Soʻraganim yaxshi boʻldi.",115.7],["Clerk","Yes, it's always worth checking. Try to arrive about 15 minutes before departure.","Ha, doim tekshirib koʻrgan maʼqul. Joʻnashdan taxminan 15 daqiqa oldin kelishga harakat qiling.",117.9],["Sarah","I will. Thanks for your help.","Shunday qilaman. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",124.2],["Clerk","You're welcome. Have a good journey.","Arzimaydi. Yoʻlingiz oq boʻlsin.",127.1]]},
{"id":"wb-09","u":9,"book":"Workbook","title":"Cities, Towns and Neighbourhoods","dur":139,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-09.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good morning, Hilltown Information Office. How can I help?","Xayrli tong, Hilltown maʼlumot markazi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.5],["David","Hi, my family and I are moving to Hilltown next month and I'd like to know more about the area.","Salom, oilam bilan kelasi oy Hilltownga koʻchib kelyapmiz va bu hudud haqida koʻproq bilmoqchiman.",9.7],["Receptionist","Of course, I can send you some information later. First, could I take your name?","Albatta, keyinroq sizga maʼlumot yuborishim mumkin. Avval ismingizni olsam boʻladimi?",16.1],["David","Yes, I'm David Palmer.","Ha, men David Palmer.",22.2],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25.3],["David","Sure, it's P-A-L-M-E-R.","Albatta, P-A-L-M-E-R.",28.2],["Receptionist","Thank you. Do you know which neighbourhood you're moving to?","Rahmat. Qaysi mahallaga koʻchib kelayotganingizni bilasizmi?",33.4],["David","Yes, our new house is in Westwood. We chose it because my wife works nearby.","Ha, yangi uyimiz Westwoodda. Uni tanladik, chunki rafiqam shu yaqin atrofda ishlaydi.",37.7],["Receptionist","That's a popular area for families. There's a primary school, several shops and a large playground.","Bu oilalar orasida mashhur hudud. Bu yerda boshlangʻich maktab, bir nechta doʻkon va katta oʻyin maydonchasi bor.",43.8],["David","That sounds good. We have two young children. Is there a supermarket within walking distance?","Bu yaxshi eshitilyapti. Bizning ikkita kichik farzandimiz bor. Piyoda borsa boʻladigan masofada supermarket bormi?",51],["Receptionist","Yes, there are actually two. The larger one is on Station Road. It stays open until 10 o'clock every evening except Sunday.","Ha, aslida ikkita bor. Kattasi Station Road koʻchasida. U yakshanbadan boshqa har kuni kechqurun soat 10 gacha ochiq.",57.5],["David","Excellent. What about public transport?","Zoʻr. Jamoat transporti-chi?",67.3],["Receptionist","Bus number 18 goes through Westwood. It stops outside the supermarket and then continues to the town centre.","18-avtobus Westwood orqali oʻtadi. U supermarket oldida toʻxtaydi va keyin shahar markazigacha davom etadi.",71],["David","Is there a train station too?","Temir yoʻl bekati ham bormi?",79],["Receptionist","Yes, but it's on the other side of town. The easiest way to reach it is by bus. The journey from Westwood takes about 25 minutes.","Ha, lekin u shaharning narigi tomonida. Unga eng oson avtobusda borish mumkin. Westwooddan yoʻl taxminan 25 daqiqa davom etadi.",81.6],["David","Okay, my children also enjoy being outdoors. Is there a park nearby?","Xop, bolalarim ochiq havoda boʻlishni ham yaxshi koʻradi. Yaqin atrofda park bormi?",91.4],["Receptionist","Yes, Oak Park is about a 15-minute walk away. It has a playground and a large lake. People often walk or cycle around it.","Ha, Oak Park piyoda taxminan 15 daqiqalik masofada. U yerda oʻyin maydonchasi va katta koʻl bor. Odamlar koʻpincha uning atrofida sayr qiladi yoki velosiped haydaydi.",97.6],["David","Lovely. Is the neighbourhood generally quiet?","Ajoyib. Mahalla odatda tinchmi?",107.4],["Receptionist","During the week, yes. Station Road can get quite noisy on Saturday afternoons because many people come to do their shopping.","Hafta davomida ha. Shanba kunlari tushdan keyin Station Road ancha shovqinli boʻlishi mumkin, chunki koʻp odam xarid qilgani keladi.",111.1],["David","That shouldn't be a problem. And is there a doctor near Westwood?","Bu muammo boʻlmasa kerak. Westwood yaqinida shifokor bormi?",120],["Receptionist","Yes, the health centre is on Market Street next to the pharmacy. It's about 10 minutes away by bus.","Ha, tibbiyot markazi Market Street koʻchasida, dorixona yonida. U yerga avtobusda taxminan 10 daqiqa.",124.8],["David","Great. That's all I needed. Thank you very much.","Zoʻr. Menga kerak boʻlgani shu edi. Katta rahmat.",132],["Receptionist","You're welcome. I hope the move goes well.","Arzimaydi. Koʻchish yaxshi oʻtsin.",135.8]]},
{"id":"wb-10","u":10,"book":"Workbook","title":"Technology and everyday life","dur":134,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-10.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello. Digital Skills Club. How can I help?","Salom. Digital Skills Club. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.2],["Chloe","Hi. I saw your poster at the library and I'd like to join one of your classes.","Salom. Kutubxonada afishangizni koʻrdim va darslaringizdan biriga qoʻshilmoqchiman.",9.2],["Receptionist","Of course. I'll take some details first. What's your name?","Albatta. Avval baʼzi maʼlumotlarni olaman. Ismingiz nima?",15],["Chloe","I'm Chloe Grant.","Men Chloe Grant.",19.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",21.2],["Chloe","Yes, it's G-R-A-N-T.","Ha, G-R-A-N-T.",23.1],["Receptionist","Thank you. We have several classes. What would you like help with?","Rahmat. Bizda bir nechta dars bor. Qaysi masalada yordam kerak?",29.1],["Chloe","I can use my phone quite well, but I've just bought a new laptop and I'd like to learn how to use it better.","Telefonimdan ancha yaxshi foydalana olaman, lekin yaqinda yangi noutbuk sotib oldim va undan yaxshiroq foydalanishni oʻrganmoqchiman.",34.1],["Receptionist","Then, our everyday technology class might be right for you. Students learn how to organise files, use useful apps and keep their information safe online.","Unda bizning kundalik texnologiya darsimiz sizga mos boʻlishi mumkin. Talabalar fayllarni tartibga solishni, foydali ilovalardan foydalanishni va maʼlumotlarini internetda xavfsiz saqlashni oʻrganadi.",41.1],["Chloe","That sounds useful. When is the class?","Bu foydali eshitilyapti. Dars qachon?",52.1],["Receptionist","We have one on Tuesday afternoon and another on Thursday evening. The evening class is more popular with people who work during the day.","Bittasi seshanba kuni tushdan keyin, yana biri payshanba kuni kechqurun. Kechki dars kunduzi ishlaydigan odamlar orasida mashhurroq.",55.1],["Chloe","Thursday would be much better for me.","Payshanba men uchun ancha yaxshi.",64.1],["Receptionist","Fine. It starts at 6.15. We ask students to arrive about 10 minutes early, so please be here by 6.05.","Yaxshi. U 6.15 da boshlanadi. Talabalardan taxminan 10 daqiqa erta kelishni soʻraymiz, shuning uchun iltimos, soat 6.05 gacha shu yerda boʻling.",67.1],["Chloe","No problem. Do I need to bring my own computer?","Muammo yoʻq. Oʻz kompyuterimni olib kelishim kerakmi?",76.1],["Receptionist","You can, but you don't have to. We have computers here. However, please bring your phone because one part of the lesson is about connecting different devices.","Olib kelishingiz mumkin, lekin shart emas. Bu yerda kompyuterlar bor. Biroq telefoningizni olib keling, chunki darsning bir qismi turli qurilmalarni ulashga bagʻishlangan.",80.1],["Chloe","OK, how many people are usually in the class?","Xop, odatda guruhda necha kishi boʻladi?",91.2],["Receptionist","The maximum is 12, but there are normally around 8. Small groups make it easier for the teacher to help everyone.","Eng koʻpi 12 kishi, lekin odatda 8 atrofida boʻladi. Kichik guruhlarda oʻqituvchiga hammaga yordam berish osonroq.",95.6],["Chloe","Good, and how much does it cost?","Yaxshi, narxi qancha?",103.4],["Receptionist","It's £8 for each class. You can pay online or at the centre when you arrive.","Har bir dars uchun £8. Onlayn yoki markazga kelganingizda toʻlashingiz mumkin.",107.3],["Chloe","Where exactly is the class held?","Dars aynan qayerda oʻtadi?",113.8],["Receptionist","We're inside the community centre on Park Road. Go through the main entrance and take the stairs to the first floor. The class is in Room 5.","Biz Park Road koʻchasidagi jamoat markazi ichidamiz. Asosiy kirishdan kiring va zinadan birinchi qavatga chiqing. Dars 5-xonada.",115.5],["Chloe","Great! Can I book a place now?","Ajoyib! Hozir joy band qilsam boʻladimi?",126],["Receptionist","Certainly. I'll add your name to Thursday's class.","Albatta. Ismingizni payshanba kungi darsga qoʻshaman.",128.6],["Chloe","Thanks very much.","Katta rahmat.",132.8]]},
{"id":"wb-11","u":11,"book":"Workbook","title":"Health, exercise and sleep","dur":136,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-11.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Wellbeing centre. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. Wellbeing markazi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.8],["Emma","Hi. I'd like some information about your healthy living programme. My friend joined last month and recommended it to me.","Salom. Sogʻlom turmush dasturingiz haqida maʼlumot olmoqchiman. Doʻstim oʻtgan oy qoʻshilgan va menga uni tavsiya qildi.",9.8],["Receptionist","Certainly. I'll take a few details first. What's your name?","Albatta. Avval bir nechta maʼlumotni olaman. Ismingiz nima?",18.5],["Emma","I'm Emma Norton.","Men Emma Norton.",23.1],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25],["Emma","Sure. It's N-O-R-T-O-N.","Albatta. N-O-R-T-O-N.",27.8],["Receptionist","Thank you. What would you most like to improve?","Rahmat. Eng koʻp nimani yaxshilamoqchisiz?",33.8],["Emma","Probably my sleep. I usually go to bed at about 11, but I sometimes lie awake for a long time. In the morning, I often feel sleepy, especially when I have to get up early for work.","Ehtimol, uyqumni. Odatda soat 11 atrofida yotaman, lekin baʼzan uzoq vaqt uxlamay yotaman. Ertalab koʻpincha uyqum kelib turadi, ayniqsa ishga erta turishim kerak boʻlganda.",37.4],["Receptionist","I see. Do you drink much coffee?","Tushundim. Koʻp kofe ichasizmi?",51.3],["Emma","I used to drink three cups a day, including one after dinner. Now I only have coffee in the morning, and I drink water with my evening meal.","Ilgari kuniga uch chashka ichardim, jumladan, kechki ovqatdan keyin bittasini. Endi faqat ertalab kofe ichaman, kechki ovqat bilan esa suv ichaman.",54.6],["Receptionist","That's a good change. What about exercise?","Bu yaxshi oʻzgarish. Jismoniy mashqlar-chi?",64.6],["Emma","I go swimming once a week. I'd like to exercise more often, but I don't enjoy going to the gym.","Haftada bir marta suzishga boraman. Koʻproq mashq qilgim keladi, lekin sport zaliga borishni yoqtirmayman.",68.2],["Receptionist","You could try our evening walking group. It meets twice a week. Tuesday's walk starts at seven, and the Thursday walk starts half an hour earlier.","Kechki piyoda yurish guruhimizni sinab koʻrishingiz mumkin. U haftada ikki marta uchrashadi. Seshanba kungi sayr soat yettida boshlanadi, payshanba kungisi esa yarim soat oldin.",75.6],["Emma","Thursday sounds good. How long do you walk for?","Payshanba yaxshi eshitilyapti. Qancha vaqt yurasiz?",85.1],["Receptionist","About an hour. We normally meet outside the centre and walk through the park.","Taxminan bir soat. Odatda markaz oldida uchrashamiz va park boʻylab yuramiz.",88.9],["Emma","Do I need to bring anything?","Biror narsa olib kelishim kerakmi?",94.3],["Receptionist","Comfortable shoes are important. We also recommend bringing a bottle of water, especially when the weather is warm.","Qulay poyabzal muhim. Shuningdek, bir shisha suv olib kelishni tavsiya qilamiz, ayniqsa ob-havo iliq boʻlganda.",96.4],["Emma","Okay. And what time should I try to go to sleep?","Xop. Soat nechada uxlashga harakat qilishim kerak?",104.2],["Receptionist","That depends on when you get up. You said you start work early. What time does your alarm ring?","Bu qachon turishingizga bogʻliq. Ishni erta boshlashingizni aytdingiz. Budilnikingiz soat nechada chaladi?",108.5],["Emma","At 6.30.","6.30 da.",114.9],["Receptionist","Then try to be asleep by around 10.30. Also, avoid looking at a screen for 30 minutes before bed. Reading a book can be a better way to relax.","Unda soat 10.30 atrofida uxlab qolishga harakat qiling. Yana, yotishdan 30 daqiqa oldin ekranga qaramang. Kitob oʻqish dam olishning yaxshiroq usuli boʻlishi mumkin.",116.8],["Emma","I can try that. I enjoy reading anyway.","Buni sinab koʻrishim mumkin. Baribir kitob oʻqishni yaxshi koʻraman.",127.8],["Receptionist","Excellent. Small changes can make a big difference.","Ajoyib. Kichik oʻzgarishlar katta farq qilishi mumkin.",131.6]]},
{"id":"wb-12","u":12,"book":"Workbook","title":"Sports and competitions","dur":131,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-12.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, Riverside Sports Centre. How can I help?","Salom, Riverside sport markazi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5],["Hannah","Hi. I'm calling about the running event next month. I'd like to enter.","Salom. Kelasi oydagi yugurish musobaqasi haqida qoʻngʻiroq qilyapman. Qatnashmoqchiman.",9],["Receptionist","Certainly. I can complete the registration with you now. Can I have your name?","Albatta. Roʻyxatdan oʻtkazishni hozir siz bilan yakunlashim mumkin. Ismingizni aytsangiz?",14.8],["Hannah","Yes. I'm Hannah Cole.","Ha. Men Hannah Cole.",20.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23],["Hannah","Sure. It's C-O-L-E.","Albatta. C-O-L-E.",26],["Receptionist","Thank you. We have two races this year. A 5km race and a 10km race. Which would you like to enter?","Rahmat. Bu yil ikkita poyga bor. 5 km va 10 km. Qaysi birida qatnashmoqchisiz?",30],["Hannah","I thought about doing 10km, but I've only been running regularly for six months. I think the 5km race is better for me this time.","10 km ni oʻylagandim, lekin men atigi olti oydan beri muntazam yuguryapman. Bu safar 5 km poyga men uchun yaxshiroq deb oʻylayman.",39.1],["Receptionist","Good choice. You can always try the longer one next year. The event is on Sunday 12th. The race itself begins at 11, but registration closes at 10.15.","Yaxshi tanlov. Uzunrogʻini kelasi yil ham sinab koʻrishingiz mumkin. Musobaqa yakshanba, 12-sanada. Poyganing oʻzi soat 11 da boshlanadi, roʻyxatga olish esa 10.15 da yopiladi.",49],["Hannah","OK. I'll make sure I'm there before then.","Xop. Ungacha u yerda boʻlishga harakat qilaman.",60.6],["Receptionist","Good. Have you taken part in a running competition before?","Yaxshi. Ilgari yugurish musobaqasida qatnashganmisiz?",64.1],["Hannah","No. This will be my first one. I usually run in the park near my house three times a week.","Yoʻq. Bu birinchisi boʻladi. Odatda uyim yaqinidagi parkda haftasiga uch marta yuguraman.",68.3],["Receptionist","Great. The route is mostly through Riverside Park. There's one short hill near the middle, but the rest of the route is quite flat.","Ajoyib. Yoʻl asosan Riverside Park orqali oʻtadi. Oʻrtasiga yaqin bitta qisqa tepalik bor, qolgan yoʻl esa ancha tekis.",75.1],["Hannah","That sounds fine. Do runners need to bring their own water?","Yaxshi eshitilyapti. Yuguruvchilar oʻz suvini olib kelishi kerakmi?",84],["Receptionist","You can if you want, but we provide water at two points along the route. You should definitely bring a small towel for after the race.","Xohlasangiz olib kelishingiz mumkin, lekin yoʻl boʻylab ikki joyda suv beramiz. Poygadan keyin uchun kichik sochiq olib kelishingiz shart.",88.4],["Hannah","OK. How much does it cost to enter?","Xop. Qatnashish qancha turadi?",97],["Receptionist","It's normally £14, but students pay £10 if they show a student card.","Odatda £14, lekin talabalar talabalik kartasini koʻrsatsa, £10 toʻlaydi.",100.2],["Hannah","Perfect. I'm a student.","Ajoyib. Men talabaman.",106.5],["Receptionist","Excellent. After the race, everyone gets a drink and some fruit. The first three runners also receive a prize.","Zoʻr. Poygadan keyin hamma ichimlik va biroz meva oladi. Dastlabki uchta yuguruvchi sovrin ham oladi.",109],["Hannah","Where do I collect my race number?","Poyga raqamimni qayerdan olaman?",117],["Receptionist","From the information desk inside the sports centre. It will be open from 9 o'clock.","Sport markazi ichidagi maʼlumot stolidan. U soat 9 dan ochiq boʻladi.",119.5],["Hannah","Great. Thanks for your help.","Zoʻr. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",125.1],["Receptionist","You're welcome. Good luck with your training.","Arzimaydi. Mashgʻulotlaringizda omad.",127.7]]},
{"id":"wb-13","u":13,"book":"Workbook","title":"Weather and seasonal activities","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-13.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, Mountain View Visitor Centre. How can I help you?","Salom, Mountain View mehmonlar markazi. Sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.8],["Peter","Hi, I'm planning to visit Mountain View with some friends during the winter holiday. I'd like to know what activities are available.","Salom, men qishki taʼtilda doʻstlarim bilan Mountain View ga borishni rejalashtiryapman. Qanday mashgʻulotlar borligini bilmoqchi edim.",10.3],["Receptionist","Certainly. Can I take your name first?","Albatta. Avval ismingizni olsam.",18.4],["Peter","Yes, I'm Peter Shaw.","Ha, men Peter Shaw.",21.8],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",24.7],["Peter","Of course. It's S-H-A-W.","Albatta. S-H-A-W.",27.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. When are you planning to come?","Rahmat. Qachon kelmoqchisiz?",32.2],["Peter","Next Friday. We were thinking about Saturday, but one of my friends has to work that day.","Kelasi juma kuni. Shanba kuni haqida oʻylagandik, lekin doʻstlarimdan biri oʻsha kuni ishlashi kerak.",35.6],["Receptionist","Friday should be a good day. We had heavy snow earlier this week, so there are lots of winter activities available.","Juma yaxshi kun boʻladi. Bu hafta boshida qattiq qor yogʻdi, shuning uchun qishki mashgʻulotlar koʻp.",41.9],["Peter","Great. We'd really like to try skiing.","Zoʻr. Biz changʻi uchishni juda sinab koʻrgimiz keladi.",49.4],["Receptionist","The beginner ski lesson would be suitable. The morning lesson starts at nine, but that group is already full. There are still places in the afternoon lesson at 1.30.","Boshlovchilar uchun changʻi darsi mos keladi. Ertalabki dars soat toʻqqizda boshlanadi, lekin u guruh allaqachon toʻlgan. Soat 1.30 dagi tushdan keyingi darsda hali joy bor.",52.7],["Peter","That's fine. None of us has skied before, so a lesson would be useful.","Yaxshi. Hech birimiz oldin changʻi uchmaganmiz, shuning uchun dars foydali boʻladi.",63.6],["Receptionist","Definitely. You can rent all the equipment here. We provide skis and boots, but everyone needs to bring their own gloves.","Albatta. Barcha jihozni shu yerda ijaraga olishingiz mumkin. Changʻi va botinkani biz beramiz, lekin qoʻlqopni hamma oʻzi olib kelishi kerak.",69],["Peter","Okay. What will the weather be like?","Xop. Ob-havo qanday boʻladi?",77.6],["Receptionist","It should stay dry, but it will be very cold. The temperature may fall to minus six degrees in the morning.","Quruq boʻlishi kerak, lekin juda sovuq boʻladi. Ertalab harorat minus olti darajagacha tushishi mumkin.",80.8],["Peter","We'll make sure we wear warm clothes. How much is the lesson?","Issiq kiyinib olamiz. Dars qancha turadi?",88.7],["Receptionist","The lesson normally costs £25 per person. Because you're coming on a weekday, the price is only £20.","Dars odatda bir kishiga £25 turadi. Siz hafta kuni kelayotganingiz uchun narxi atigi £20.",93],["Peter","Good. Is there anything to do after the lesson?","Yaxshi. Darsdan keyin qiladigan biror narsa bormi?",101.4],["Receptionist","Yes. You can go ice skating until seven o'clock or visit the cafe. They serve hot drinks, soup and sandwiches.","Ha. Soat yettigacha muz ustida uchishingiz yoki kafega kirishingiz mumkin. U yerda issiq ichimliklar, shoʻrva va sendvichlar beriladi.",105],["Peter","The cafe sounds good after being outside all afternoon.","Tushdan keyin butun vaqt tashqarida boʻlgandan soʻng kafe yaxshi eshitiladi.",113.9],["Receptionist","I'm sure it will. Just remember that it gets dark early in winter, so don't start any long walks late in the day.","Albatta yaxshi boʻladi. Faqat qishda qorongʻi erta tushishini eslab qoling, shuning uchun kunning kech payti uzoq sayrni boshlamang.",117.9],["Peter","Good advice. Thanks very much.","Yaxshi maslahat. Katta rahmat.",126.2]]},
{"id":"wb-14","u":14,"book":"Workbook","title":"Animals and Wildlife","dur":134,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-14.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello. Riverbank Animal Centre. How can I help?","Salom. Riverbank hayvonlar markazi. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",4.2],["Sophie","Hi. I saw some information online about helping at the centre and I'm interested in becoming a volunteer.","Salom. Internetda markazda yordam berish haqida maʼlumot koʻrdim va koʻngilli boʻlishga qiziqyapman.",9.4],["Receptionist","That's great. We're always looking for people to help. Can I take your name first?","Zoʻr. Biz doim yordamchilar qidiramiz. Avval ismingizni olsam.",17],["Sophie","Yes, I'm Sophie Lane. Could you spell your surname, please?","Ha, men Sophie Lane. Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",23.6],["Receptionist","Of course. It's L-A-N-E.","Albatta. L-A-N-E.",28.3],["Receptionist","Thank you. Have you worked with animals before?","Rahmat. Avval hayvonlar bilan ishlaganmisiz?",33.3],["Sophie","Not as a job, but my family has always had pets. We have two cats now and I used to look after my neighbour's dog when she was away.","Ish sifatida emas, lekin oilamizda doim uy hayvonlari boʻlgan. Hozir ikkita mushukimiz bor, qoʻshnimning itiga esa u yoʻq paytda qarab turardim.",37.3],["Receptionist","That's useful. Most new volunteers start by helping with the rabbits. They need fresh food, clean water and a clean living area every day.","Bu foydali. Koʻpchilik yangi koʻngillilar quyonlarga qarashdan boshlaydi. Ularga har kuni yangi ovqat, toza suv va toza yashash joyi kerak.",46.3],["Sophie","I'd be happy to do that. When do you need volunteers?","Buni mamnuniyat bilan qilaman. Koʻngillilar qachon kerak?",57.3],["Receptionist","We need the most help at weekends. Saturday morning is already quite busy, but we still need people on Sunday.","Eng koʻp yordam dam olish kunlari kerak. Shanba ertalab ancha band, lekin yakshanba kuni hali odam kerak.",61.3],["Sophie","Sunday is actually better for me. What time would I start?","Aslida yakshanba men uchun qulayroq. Soat nechada boshlayman?",69.3],["Receptionist","Volunteers usually arrive at 8.30. The centre opens to visitors at 10, so we try to finish most of the cleaning before then.","Koʻngillilar odatda 8.30 da keladi. Markaz tashrifchilar uchun 10 da ochiladi, shuning uchun tozalashning koʻpini oʻshagacha tugatishga harakat qilamiz.",74.3],["Sophie","OK. What should I wear?","Xop. Nima kiyishim kerak?",83.3],["Receptionist","Comfortable clothes are best. Please wear strong boots because some areas can get wet and muddy.","Qulay kiyim eng yaxshisi. Mustahkam botinka kiying, chunki baʼzi joylar nam va loyli boʻlishi mumkin.",86.3],["Sophie","Fine. Do volunteers work with the wild animals too?","Yaxshi. Koʻngillilar yovvoyi hayvonlar bilan ham ishlaydimi?",91.2],["Receptionist","Not at first. We sometimes care for injured birds and other local wildlife but only experienced volunteers work closely with them.","Dastlab yoʻq. Baʼzan jarohatlangan qushlar va boshqa mahalliy yovvoyi hayvonlarga qaraymiz, lekin ular bilan faqat tajribali koʻngillilar yaqindan ishlaydi.",94],["Sophie","I understand. Is there any training?","Tushundim. Oʻqitish bormi?",106],["Receptionist","Yes, all new volunteers attend a short training session. The next one is on the 16th and lasts about two hours.","Ha, barcha yangi koʻngillilar qisqa oʻquv mashgʻulotida qatnashadi. Keyingisi 16 da va taxminan ikki soat davom etadi.",110.5],["Sophie","Great! Is there anything I should bring to that?","Zoʻr! U yerga biror narsa olib kelishim kerakmi?",119.8],["Receptionist","Just a notebook. We'll provide everything else.","Faqat daftar. Qolgan hammasini biz beramiz.",123.9],["Sophie","Perfect! I'd definitely like to join.","Juda yaxshi! Albatta qoʻshilmoqchiman.",127],["Receptionist","Excellent! I'll add your name to the list.","Ajoyib! Ismingizni roʻyxatga qoʻshib qoʻyaman.",130.4]]},
{"id":"wb-15","u":15,"book":"Workbook","title":"Nature and the Environment","dur":131,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-15.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. Green Community Centre, how can I help you?","Xayrli kun. Green jamoat markazi, sizga qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.8],["Laura","Hi, I saw a notice about your tree planting day and I'd like to take part.","Salom, daraxt ekish kuningiz haqidagi eʼlonni koʻrdim va qatnashmoqchiman.",10.2],["Receptionist","Wonderful. We still need a few more volunteers. Can I take your name?","Ajoyib. Bizga hali bir nechta koʻngilli kerak. Ismingizni olsam?",16.5],["Laura","Yes, it's Laura Finch.","Ha, Laura Finch.",21.8],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",24.6],["Laura","Of course, it's F-I-N-C-H.","Albatta, F-I-N-C-H.",27.4],["Receptionist","Thank you. This time we're planting trees near the river. We planted some in the town park last year so we wanted to choose a different area.","Rahmat. Bu safar daryo yonida daraxt ekamiz. Oʻtgan yili shahar bogʻiga ekkandik, shuning uchun boshqa joyni tanlamoqchi boʻldik.",32.7],["Laura","That sounds good. I cycle along the river sometimes and it would be nice to see more trees there.","Bu yaxshi. Men baʼzan daryo boʻylab velosipedda yuraman va u yerda koʻproq daraxt boʻlsa yaxshi boʻlardi.",42.2],["Receptionist","Exactly. The planting day is next Sunday. We normally organise these events on Saturdays but there's a big market in the area that day.","Aynan shunday. Ekish kuni kelasi yakshanba. Biz bunday tadbirlarni odatda shanba kuni oʻtkazamiz, lekin oʻsha kuni hududda katta bozor bor.",49],["Laura","Sunday works for me. When does it begin?","Yakshanba menga mos. U qachon boshlanadi?",58.5],["Receptionist","We start at ten o'clock but please arrive by nine thirty. We need to put everyone into small groups and explain how to plant the trees correctly.","Soat oʻnda boshlaymiz, lekin iltimos, toʻqqiz yarimgacha keling. Hammani kichik guruhlarga ajratib, daraxtni toʻgʻri ekishni tushuntirishimiz kerak.",61.6],["Laura","Sure. Do I need any experience?","Xop. Tajriba kerakmi?",71.4],["Receptionist","Not at all. A team leader will show you what to do. We provide all the tools including gloves and small spades.","Umuman kerak emas. Guruh rahbari nima qilishni koʻrsatadi. Barcha asboblarni, jumladan qoʻlqop va kichik belkuraklarni biz beramiz.",74.8],["Laura","Great. What should I wear?","Zoʻr. Nima kiyishim kerak?",82.7],["Receptionist","Old clothes are best. Please bring a jacket too. The forecast says it should stay dry but it may be cool near the water.","Eski kiyim yaxshi. Kurtka ham olib keling. Bashoratga koʻra yogʻin boʻlmaydi, lekin suv yonida salqin boʻlishi mumkin.",85.6],["Laura","Okay. How many trees are you hoping to plant?","Xop. Nechta daraxt ekmoqchisiz?",94.6],["Receptionist","We originally planned to plant fifty but a local business gave us some extra trees. We now hope to plant seventy.","Dastlab ellikta ekishni rejalagandik, lekin mahalliy bir kompaniya bizga qoʻshimcha daraxtlar berdi. Endi yetmishta ekmoqchimiz.",98.3],["Laura","Wow. That's quite a lot.","Voy. Bu ancha koʻp.",106.6],["Receptionist","It is but we already have nearly forty volunteers. We'll also stop for a short break at midday.","Ha, lekin bizda allaqachon qariyb qirq nafar koʻngilli bor. Tush payti qisqa tanaffus ham qilamiz.",109.5],["Laura","Will there be food?","Ovqat boʻladimi?",117.1],["Receptionist","We provide fruit and water. Please bring your own lunch though because the event continues until about three.","Meva va suv beramiz. Lekin tushligingizni oʻzingiz olib keling, chunki tadbir taxminan soat uchgacha davom etadi.",118.8],["Laura","No problem. I'll be there.","Muammo yoʻq. Boraman.",125.8],["Receptionist","Excellent. Thanks for helping us.","Ajoyib. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",128.1]]},
{"id":"wb-16","u":16,"book":"Workbook","title":"Films, Music, Books and Entertainment","dur":138,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-16.mp3","lines":[["Librarian","Hello, Riverside Library. How can I help?","Salom, Riverside kutubxonasi. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",7],["Nathan","Hi. I saw an advertisement for your evening entertainment club and I'd like some information.","Salom. Kechki koʻngilochar klubingiz eʼlonini koʻrdim va maʼlumot olmoqchi edim.",11],["Librarian","Certainly. We organise different activities each week. Can I take your name first?","Albatta. Biz har hafta turli tadbirlar oʻtkazamiz. Avval ismingizni olsam.",18],["Nathan","Yes, I'm Nathan Bell.","Ha, men Nathan Bell.",24],["Librarian","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",27],["Nathan","Sure, it's B-E-L-L.","Albatta, B-E-L-L.",30],["Librarian","Thank you. What kind of entertainment are you most interested in?","Rahmat. Qanday koʻngilochar turi sizni koʻproq qiziqtiradi?",34],["Nathan","I love films and music, but I'm especially interested in books. I read almost every evening.","Men filmlar va musiqani yaxshi koʻraman, lekin ayniqsa kitoblarga qiziqaman. Deyarli har kecha oʻqiyman.",39],["Librarian","Then you might enjoy our reading group. We meet twice a month and discuss a different book each time.","Unda kitobxonlik guruhimiz sizga yoqishi mumkin. Oyiga ikki marta yigʻilamiz va har safar boshqa kitobni muhokama qilamiz.",46],["Nathan","That sounds good. Which day do you meet?","Bu yaxshi eshitiladi. Qaysi kuni yigʻilasizlar?",53],["Librarian","We used to meet on Tuesdays, but this month the meetings are on Wednesday evenings because the library has another event on Tuesdays.","Avval seshanba kunlari yigʻilardik, lekin bu oy uchrashuvlar chorshanba kechqurunlari, chunki kutubxonada seshanba kunlari boshqa tadbir bor.",56],["Nathan","Wednesday is fine. What time does it start?","Chorshanba mayli. Soat nechada boshlanadi?",64],["Librarian","At 7.15. Most people arrive a little earlier and have tea or coffee before the discussion begins.","7.15 da. Koʻpchilik biroz oldinroq kelib, muhokama boshlanishidan oldin choy yoki kofe ichadi.",68],["Nathan","Nice. What book are you reading at the moment?","Yaxshi. Hozir qaysi kitobni oʻqiyapsizlar?",75],["Librarian","It's an adventure story called The Long Road. It's about two friends travelling through the mountains. The writer is coming to our next meeting.","Bu The Long Road nomli sarguzasht hikoyasi. U togʻlar boʻylab sayohat qilayotgan ikki doʻst haqida. Yozuvchi keyingi uchrashuvimizga keladi.",79],["Nathan","Really? That sounds interesting.","Rostdanmi? Qiziq eshitiladi.",88],["Librarian","Yes. After the discussion, she'll answer questions and talk about how she became a writer.","Ha. Muhokamadan keyin u savollarga javob beradi va qanday qilib yozuvchi boʻlgani haqida gapirib beradi.",91],["Nathan","Great. Do I have to buy the book?","Zoʻr. Kitobni sotib olishim kerakmi?",98],["Librarian","No. Members can borrow a copy from the library for three weeks. Just show your library card at the front desk.","Yoʻq. Aʼzolar kutubxonadan nusxasini uch haftaga olishi mumkin. Faqat qabul stolida kutubxona kartangizni koʻrsating.",101],["Nathan","Perfect. Is there a cost to join the group?","Juda yaxshi. Guruhga qoʻshilish pullikmi?",109],["Librarian","The reading group itself is free. We sometimes organise cinema trips and members pay for those separately.","Kitobxonlik guruhining oʻzi bepul. Baʼzan kinoga borishni ham tashkil qilamiz, buning uchun aʼzolar alohida toʻlaydi.",112],["Nathan","Do you have any other events this month?","Bu oy boshqa tadbirlar ham bormi?",120],["Librarian","Yes, there's a live music evening on the 24th. A local singer will perform in the café. Tickets are £6.","Ha, 24 da jonli musiqa kechasi boʻladi. Mahalliy qoʻshiqchi kafeda chiqish qiladi. Chiptalar £6.",122],["Nathan","I might come to that too.","Bunga ham kelishim mumkin.",132],["Librarian","Great! I'll give you the details when you come to the reading group.","Zoʻr! Kitobxonlik guruhiga kelganingizda batafsil maʼlumot beraman.",134]]},
{"id":"wb-17","u":17,"book":"Workbook","title":"Interesting people and their lives","dur":118,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-17.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome to young people doing interesting things. Today we're talking to someone who started his own small business while he was still at school. Thanks for coming. Could you introduce yourself?","Qiziqarli ishlar bilan shugʻullanayotgan yoshlar dasturiga xush kelibsiz. Bugun biz hali maktabda oʻqib yurganida oʻz kichik biznesini boshlagan inson bilan suhbatlashamiz. Kelganingiz uchun rahmat. Oʻzingizni tanishtira olasizmi?",6],["Daniel","Sure, I'm Daniel Moore.","Albatta, men Daniel Moore.",19.2],["Host","Could you spell your surname for our listeners?","Tinglovchilarimiz uchun familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",22],["Daniel","Yes, it's M-O-O-R-E.","Ha, M-O-O-R-E.",25.1],["Host","Thanks, Daniel. Where are you from?","Rahmat, Daniel. Qayerliksiz?",30],["Daniel","I was born in Manchester, but when I was six, my family moved to Bristol. I've lived there ever since.","Men Manchesterda tugʻilganman, lekin olti yoshimda oilam Bristolga koʻchib oʻtgan. Shundan beri oʻsha yerda yashayman.",32.9],["Host","Tell us about your business. How did it begin?","Biznesingiz haqida gapirib bering. U qanday boshlangan?",39.8],["Daniel","I've always enjoyed making things. When I was 16, I started making simple wooden boxes at home. At first, they were just presents for family members.","Men doim biror narsa yasashni yoqtirganman. 16 yoshimda uyda oddiy yogʻoch qutilar yasay boshladim. Dastlab ular oila aʼzolari uchun shunchaki sovgʻalar edi.",43.3],["Host","So when did it become a business?","Xoʻsh, u qachon biznesga aylandi?",53.8],["Daniel","A friend asked if she could buy one. Then other people became interested. I started selling the boxes online, and after a few months, I was getting several orders each week.","Bir doʻstim bittasini sotib olsam boʻladimi deb soʻradi. Keyin boshqalar ham qiziqib qolishdi. Qutilarni internetda sota boshladim va bir necha oydan keyin har hafta bir nechta buyurtma olardim.",56.6],["Host","Did you make everything at home?","Hammasini uyda yasadingizmi?",67.4],["Daniel","At first, yes. I worked in our garage because there wasn't enough space in my bedroom. Last year, I rented a small workshop near my house.","Dastlab ha. Yotoqxonamda joy yetmagani uchun garajimizda ishladim. Oʻtgan yili uyimga yaqin joyda kichik ustaxona ijaraga oldim.",70],["Host","Do you work there alone?","U yerda yolgʻiz ishlaysizmi?",79.6],["Daniel","Not anymore. My cousin works with me three days a week. She answers customer messages and takes photos of our products for the website.","Endi yoʻq. Amakivachcham haftasiga uch kun men bilan ishlaydi. U mijozlarning xabarlariga javob beradi va sayt uchun mahsulotlarimizni suratga oladi.",81.8],["Host","What do you enjoy most about your work?","Ishingizning nimasi sizga eng koʻp yoqadi?",90.8],["Daniel","I like designing new things. Making the same box again and again can get boring, so creating something different is much more exciting.","Yangi narsalarni loyihalash menga yoqadi. Bir xil qutini qayta-qayta yasash zerikarli boʻlishi mumkin, shuning uchun boshqacha narsa yaratish ancha qiziqarli.",93.8],["Host","And what are your plans for the future?","Kelajak rejalaringiz qanday?",103.1],["Daniel","I'd like to open a small shop one day. I enjoy selling online, but I think it would be nice to meet more of my customers.","Bir kun kichik doʻkon ochmoqchiman. Internetda sotishni yaxshi koʻraman, lekin mijozlarim bilan koʻproq uchrashsam yaxshi boʻlardi deb oʻylayman.",106.1],["Host","Sounds like a great plan. Thanks for talking to us.","Ajoyib reja ekan. Biz bilan suhbatlashganingiz uchun rahmat.",113.7]]},
{"id":"wb-18","u":18,"book":"Workbook","title":"Festivals, Celebrations and Traditions","dur":132,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-18.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, Oakfield Community Centre, how can I help?","Salom, Oakfield jamoat markazi, qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.3],["Robert","Hi, I saw a poster about your spring celebration and I'd like to bring my family.","Salom, bahor bayramingiz haqidagi plakatni koʻrdim va oilam bilan kelmoqchiman.",11.2],["Receptionist","Wonderful, it's a traditional event we organise every year. Can I take your name first?","Ajoyib, bu har yili oʻtkazadigan anʼanaviy tadbirimiz. Avval ismingizni olsam.",17.8],["Robert","Yes, I'm Robert Dean.","Ha, men Robert Dean.",24.7],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",27.6],["Robert","Of course, it's D-E-A-N.","Albatta, D-E-A-N.",30.6],["Receptionist","Thank you. This year's celebration will be on Saturday the 9th. Last year we held it on a Sunday, but Saturday is easier for most families.","Rahmat. Bu yilgi bayram 9 shanba kuni boʻladi. Oʻtgan yili yakshanba kuni oʻtkazgandik, lekin shanba koʻpchilik oilalar uchun qulayroq.",35.2],["Robert","Great. What time should we arrive?","Zoʻr. Soat nechada kelishimiz kerak?",45.6],["Receptionist","The doors open at 10, but the first activity begins at 10.45. It's a traditional dance performed by children from the local school.","Eshiklar 10 da ochiladi, lekin birinchi tadbir 10.45 da boshlanadi. Bu mahalliy maktab bolalari ijro etadigan anʼanaviy raqs.",48.6],["Robert","My daughter will enjoy that. What else is happening?","Qizimga bu yoqadi. Yana nima boʻladi?",58.3],["Receptionist","After the dance, there'll be music and several family games. At lunchtime, local families will serve traditional food.","Raqsdan keyin musiqa va bir nechta oilaviy oʻyinlar boʻladi. Tushlik payti mahalliy oilalar anʼanaviy taomlar tortiq qiladi.",62.3],["Robert","What kind of food?","Qanday taomlar?",70.9],["Receptionist","There'll be rice dishes, meat and vegetables. We'll also have a special sweet cake that people usually make for this celebration.","Guruchli taomlar, goʻsht va sabzavotlar boʻladi. Yana odamlar odatda shu bayram uchun pishiradigan maxsus shirin tort ham boʻladi.",72.7],["Robert","Sounds delicious. Can children take part in the activities?","Mazali eshitiladi. Bolalar tadbirlarda qatnasha oladimi?",82.2],["Receptionist","Absolutely. One popular activity is making traditional decorations from paper. Children can take them home afterwards.","Albatta. Mashhur tadbirlardan biri qogʻozdan anʼanaviy bezaklar yasash. Bolalar ularni keyin uyga olib ketishi mumkin.",87],["Robert","Nice. Is there anything we should bring?","Yaxshi. Biror narsa olib kelishimiz kerakmi?",96.1],["Receptionist","If the weather is good, some activities will be outside, so bring a hat for the children. It can get quite sunny in the afternoon.","Ob-havo yaxshi boʻlsa, baʼzi tadbirlar tashqarida boʻladi, shuning uchun bolalarga shapka olib keling. Tushdan keyin ancha quyoshli boʻlishi mumkin.",99.4],["Robert","OK. Do we need to buy tickets?","Xop. Chipta sotib olishimiz kerakmi?",108.6],["Receptionist","Entry is free for children under 12. Adult tickets are £7 and that includes all the activities.","12 yoshgacha bolalar uchun kirish bepul. Kattalar chiptasi £7 va bu barcha tadbirlarni oʻz ichiga oladi.",111.5],["Robert","Excellent. Can we buy tickets when we arrive?","Ajoyib. Chiptani kelganimizda sotib olsak boʻladimi?",119.6],["Receptionist","Yes, but the event is usually busy, so coming early is a good idea.","Ha, lekin tadbir odatda gavjum boʻladi, shuning uchun erta kelgan yaxshi.",123.3],["Robert","We will. Thanks for your help.","Shunday qilamiz. Yordamingiz uchun rahmat.",129.1]]},
{"id":"wb-19","u":19,"book":"Workbook","title":"Childhood and Memories","dur":129,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-19.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome back to Growing Up. Today, we're asking people about things they remember from childhood. Could you introduce yourself?","Growing Up dasturiga qaytganingiz bilan. Bugun odamlardan bolalikdan nimalarni eslashlarini soʻraymiz. Oʻzingizni tanishtirib oʻtasizmi?",5.4],["Michael","Of course. I'm Michael Green.","Albatta. Men Michael Green.",13.5],["Host","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",17.8],["Michael","Sure. It's G-R-E-E-N.","Albatta. G-R-E-E-N.",20.5],["Host","Thanks, Michael. Where did you live when you were a child?","Rahmat, Michael. Bolaligingizda qayerda yashagansiz?",25.9],["Michael","I was born in a city, but when I was five, we moved to a small village in the countryside. My parents wanted somewhere quieter for us to grow up.","Men shaharda tugʻilganman, lekin besh yoshimda qishloq joydagi kichik bir qishloqqa koʻchib oʻtganmiz. Ota-onam biz ulgʻayishimiz uchun tinchroq joy xohlagan.",30.2],["Host","What did you like about living there?","U yerda yashashning nimasi yoqardi?",39.8],["Michael","I loved being outdoors. There was a field behind our house, and my friends and I spent hours there. We played football, climbed trees, and sometimes had picnics.","Ochiq havoda boʻlishni yaxshi koʻrardim. Uyimiz orqasida dala bor edi, doʻstlarim bilan u yerda soatlab vaqt oʻtkazardik. Futbol oʻynardik, daraxtlarga chiqardik, goho piknik qilardik.",42.5],["Host","What was school like?","Maktab qanday edi?",52.5],["Michael","It was quite small. I started there when I was six, and there were only about 20 children in my class. I was nervous at first, but I soon made friends.","Ancha kichik edi. U yerda olti yoshimda oʻqishni boshlaganman, sinfimda atigi 20 ga yaqin bola bor edi. Avvaliga hayajonlangandim, lekin tez orada doʻst orttirdim.",55.3],["Host","Did you have a favourite teacher?","Yoqtirgan oʻqituvchingiz boʻlganmi?",66.5],["Michael","Yes, Mr Thomas. He taught science. His lessons were always interesting, because we did simple experiments instead of only reading from books.","Ha, Thomas janoblari. U tabiiy fanlardan dars berardi. Darslari doim qiziqarli edi, chunki faqat kitobdan oʻqimay, oddiy tajribalar qilardik.",68.6],["Host","What did you usually do when you got home from school?","Maktabdan uyga kelganingizda odatda nima qilardingiz?",78.2],["Michael","My mum usually gave me something to eat first. Then I did my homework. After that, I often rode my bike to my best friend's house.","Onam odatda avval menga biror narsa yegani berardi. Keyin uy vazifamni qilardim. Undan soʻng koʻpincha velosipedda eng yaqin doʻstimning uyiga borardim.",81.9],["Host","Do you remember your birthdays?","Tugʻilgan kunlaringizni eslaysizmi?",89],["Michael","Definitely. My parents usually organised a small party at home. On my tenth birthday, I got a camera. I took pictures of absolutely everything for months.","Albatta. Ota-onam odatda uyda kichik bayram uyushtirardi. Oʻn yoshimda menga fotoapparat sovgʻa qilishgan. Bir necha oy davomida hamma narsani suratga olardim.",93.4],["Host","What is your favourite childhood memory?","Bolalikdagi eng yaxshi xotirangiz qaysi?",104.9],["Michael","Probably our summer holidays. We went to the same place every year and stayed in a small house near a forest. My brother and I loved exploring it with our dad.","Ehtimol, yozgi taʼtillarimiz. Har yili bir joyga borardik va oʻrmon yaqinidagi kichik uyda turardik. Ukam bilan dadam hamroh boʻlib u yerlarni kezib chiqishni yaxshi koʻrardik.",108],["Host","Do you still have any of those old photographs?","Oʻsha eski suratlardan hali ham bormi?",118.6],["Michael","Yes, I keep them in a box at my parents' house. Looking at them always brings back good memories.","Ha, ularni ota-onamning uyida bir qutida saqlayman. Ularga qaraganimda doim yaxshi xotiralar esimga tushadi.",122]]},
{"id":"wb-20","u":20,"book":"Workbook","title":"Everyday problems and solutions","dur":125,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-20.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Good afternoon. City Bus lost property office. How can I help?","Xayrli kun. City Bus yoʻqolgan buyumlar boʻlimi. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.5],["James","Hi, I think I left my bag on a bus this morning.","Salom, bugun ertalab sumkamni avtobusda unutib qoldirganga oʻxshayman.",10.6],["Receptionist","Okay, I'll take some details and see if anyone has found it. Can I have your name first?","Mayli, baʼzi maʼlumotlarni yozib olaman va kimdir topib berganmi, tekshiraman. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",14.6],["James","Yes, I'm James Cook.","Ha, men James Cook.",21.7],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",24.5],["James","Of course. It's C-O-O-K.","Albatta. C-O-O-K.",26.5],["Receptionist","Thank you. Do you remember which bus you were on?","Rahmat. Qaysi avtobusda ketganingizni eslaysizmi?",31.5],["James","Yes, it was the number 27. I usually take the 19, but that bus was late this morning, so I took a different one.","Ha, 27-avtobus edi. Odatda 19-ga minaman, lekin bugun ertalab u kech qoldi, shuning uchun boshqasiga mindim.",35.5],["Receptionist","I see. What time did you get off the bus?","Tushunarli. Avtobusdan soat nechada tushdingiz?",44.5],["James","At about 8.20. I didn't notice the bag was missing until I arrived at work about 15 minutes later.","Taxminan 8.20 da. Taxminan 15 daqiqadan keyin ishga yetib borgunimcha sumka yoʻqolganini sezmadim.",48.5],["Receptionist","Can you describe the bag?","Sumkani taʼriflab bera olasizmi?",55.5],["James","It's a small black backpack. I also have a blue one at home, but the one I lost is definitely black.","Kichkina qora ryukzak. Uyda koʻk rangligi ham bor, lekin yoʻqotganim aniq qora.",57.5],["Receptionist","And what was inside it?","Ichida nima bor edi?",65.5],["James","My lunch, a notebook and a pair of glasses. Luckily I had my phone and wallet in my coat pocket.","Tushlik ovqatim, daftar va koʻzoynak. Yaxshiyamki, telefonim va hamyonim palto choʻntagida edi.",67.5],["Receptionist","That's good. Did the bag have your name on it?","Yaxshi. Sumkada ismingiz yozilganmi?",74.5],["James","No, but there's a small green keyring on the front. It looks like a football.","Yoʻq, lekin old tomonida kichkina yashil kalit taqinchogʻi bor. U futbol toʻpiga oʻxshaydi.",78.5],["Receptionist","All right. We haven't received a black backpack yet, but drivers usually bring lost items here after their shift. The bus you took should return to the station at 2.30 this afternoon.","Yaxshi. Hozircha qora ryukzak kelmagan, lekin haydovchilar odatda smenadan keyin yoʻqolgan buyumlarni shu yerga olib kelishadi. Siz mingan avtobus bugun tushdan keyin soat 2.30 da bekatga qaytishi kerak.",84.5],["James","So, should I call again later?","Unda keyinroq yana qoʻngʻiroq qilaymi?",97.5],["Receptionist","Yes. Try us after 3. If we find the bag, you can collect it from the lost property office next to the ticket desk.","Ha. Soat 3 dan keyin qoʻngʻiroq qiling. Sumkani topsak, uni chipta kassasi yonidagi yoʻqolgan buyumlar boʻlimidan olib ketishingiz mumkin.",100.5],["James","OK. What time do you close?","Xop. Soat nechada yopasizlar?",108.5],["Receptionist","At six today. If you can't come before then, we can keep the bag here for you.","Bugun oltida. Undan oldin kela olmasangiz, sumkani siz uchun shu yerda saqlab turamiz.",111.5],["James","Great. Thanks. I was worried I'd lost it completely.","Zoʻr. Rahmat. Butunlay yoʻqotib qoʻydim deb xavotirda edim.",117.5],["Receptionist","Hopefully it will turn up this afternoon.","Umid qilamizki, bugun tushdan keyin topiladi.",121.5]]},
{"id":"wb-21","u":21,"book":"Workbook","title":"Helping people and community life","dur":140,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-21.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, Eastside Community Kitchen. How can I help?","Salom, Eastside jamoat oshxonasi. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",6.1],["Matthew","Hi, my friend volunteers with you and she said you need more people to help.","Salom, doʻstim sizlar bilan ixtiyoriy ishlaydi va yordam beradigan koʻproq odam kerakligini aytdi.",10.2],["Receptionist","We do. Thanks for calling. Can I take your name first?","Ha, kerak. Qoʻngʻiroq qilganingiz uchun rahmat. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",16.2],["Matthew","Yes, I'm Matthew Ford.","Ha, men Matthew Ford.",21.4],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",24.2],["Matthew","Sure, it's F-O-R-D.","Albatta, F-O-R-D.",27.1],["Receptionist","Thank you. Have you done any volunteer work before?","Rahmat. Ilgari ixtiyoriy ish bilan shugʻullanganmisiz?",31.5],["Matthew","Yes. Last year I helped at a school event. I served drinks and helped clean up afterwards, but I've never worked in a community kitchen.","Ha. Oʻtgan yili maktab tadbirida yordam berganman. Ichimliklar tarqatdim va keyin yigʻishtirishga koʻmaklashdim, lekin jamoat oshxonasida hech ishlamaganman.",35.8],["Receptionist","That's absolutely fine. We prepare free meals for people who need them. New volunteers usually start by preparing vegetables. They wash them, cut them, and get them ready for cooking.","Bu mutlaqo muammo emas. Biz muhtojlarga bepul ovqat tayyorlaymiz. Yangi ixtiyoriylar odatda sabzavot tayyorlashdan boshlaydi. Ularni yuvishadi, toʻgʻrashadi va pishirishga tayyorlashadi.",45.7],["Matthew","Great. I cook quite a lot at home, so I'd be comfortable doing that.","Zoʻr. Uyda ancha koʻp ovqat pishiraman, shuning uchun buni qilish menga qulay boʻladi.",58.5],["Receptionist","Excellent. We prepare meals on Wednesdays and Fridays. Wednesday is already quite busy, so we especially need help on the other day.","Ajoyib. Ovqatni chorshanba va juma kunlari tayyorlaymiz. Chorshanba kuni allaqachon odam koʻp, shuning uchun ayniqsa ikkinchi kunda yordam kerak.",63.5],["Matthew","Friday works well for me.","Juma menga yaxshi mos keladi.",73.4],["Receptionist","Good. We start cooking at five, but volunteers need to arrive by four-forty-five so they can wash their hands, put their things away, and get ready.","Yaxshi. Pishirishni beshda boshlaymiz, lekin ixtiyoriylar 4.45 gacha kelishi kerak, shunda qoʻllarini yuvib, narsalarini qoʻyib, tayyorlanib olishadi.",75.5],["Matthew","No problem. How long would I stay?","Muammo yoʻq. Qancha vaqt qolaman?",85.6],["Receptionist","Usually until about eight. We start serving the meals at six-thirty.","Odatda soat sakkizgacha. Ovqat tarqatishni 6.30 da boshlaymiz.",89],["Matthew","Do I need to bring any equipment?","Biror jihoz olib kelishim kerakmi?",94.5],["Receptionist","No. We provide everything in the kitchen. Just wear comfortable clothes and closed shoes. Open shoes aren't safe when you're working around hot food.","Yoʻq. Oshxonada hamma narsani oʻzimiz beramiz. Faqat qulay kiyim va yopiq poyabzal kiying. Issiq ovqat atrofida ishlaganda ochiq poyabzal xavfsiz emas.",97],["Matthew","Okay. Is there anything else I can help with?","Mayli. Yana qanday yordam berishim mumkin?",107.5],["Receptionist","Sometimes we need people to deliver meals to older residents. Volunteers usually go in pairs and travel by car.","Goho keksa aholiga ovqat yetkazib beradigan odamlar kerak boʻladi. Ixtiyoriylar odatda ikkitadan mashinada boradi.",111.1],["Matthew","I have a car, so I could do that sometimes.","Mening mashinam bor, shuning uchun buni baʼzan qila olaman.",119.5],["Receptionist","That would be very helpful. Before you begin, there's a short training session. It lasts thirty minutes and explains the kitchen's safety rules.","Bu juda foydali boʻlardi. Boshlashingizdan oldin qisqa oʻquv mashgʻuloti bor. U oʻttiz daqiqa davom etadi va oshxonaning xavfsizlik qoidalarini tushuntiradi.",123],["Matthew","Great. When's the next one?","Zoʻr. Keyingisi qachon?",133.2],["Receptionist","This Thursday at six.","Shu payshanba soat oltida.",135.8],["Matthew","Perfect. I'll be there.","Juda yaxshi. Men oʻsha yerda boʻlaman.",138.2]]},
{"id":"wb-22","u":22,"book":"Workbook","title":"Trying something new","dur":138,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-22.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello, Creative Skills Centre. How can I help?","Salom, Creative Skills markazi. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.1],["Thomas","Hi, I'm looking for a new hobby and a friend told me about your beginner courses.","Salom, yangi hobbi qidiryapman, doʻstim sizlarning boshlangʻich kurslaringiz haqida aytdi.",9],["Receptionist","Great! We have several courses for people who want to try something different. Can I take your name first?","Zoʻr! Biz yangi narsa sinab koʻrmoqchi boʻlganlar uchun bir nechta kurs oʻtkazamiz. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",14.7],["Thomas","Yes, I'm Thomas Riley.","Ha, men Thomas Riley.",22.2],["Receptionist","Could you spell your surname, please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",25],["Thomas","Of course. It's R-I-L-E-Y.","Albatta. R-I-L-E-Y.",27.7],["Receptionist","Thank you. What sort of things are you interested in?","Rahmat. Qanday narsalarga qiziqasiz?",33],["Thomas","I work on a computer all day, so I'd like to do something with my hands. I've thought about painting, but I'm not very good at drawing.","Kun boʻyi kompyuterda ishlayman, shuning uchun qoʻllarim bilan biror narsa qilmoqchiman. Rasm chizish haqida oʻylab koʻrdim, lekin chizishni unchalik yaxshi bilmayman.",37],["Receptionist","You don't need to be. We also have cooking, photography and pottery courses.","Bilishingiz shart emas. Bizda yana pazandalik, fotografiya va kulolchilik kurslari ham bor.",46.5],["Thomas","I already cook quite a lot at home, and I use my phone for photos. Pottery sounds more unusual. I've never tried anything like that.","Uyda allaqachon ancha koʻp ovqat pishiraman, suratlarni telefonda olaman. Kulolchilik noodatiyroq eshitiladi. Bunday narsani hech sinab koʻrmaganman.",52.6],["Receptionist","Then our beginner course would be perfect. It's a four-week course, and you'll learn how to make simple bowls and cups.","Unda bizning boshlangʻich kursimiz juda mos keladi. Bu toʻrt haftalik kurs, unda oddiy kosa va piyolalar yasashni oʻrganasiz.",61.8],["Thomas","Nice! When are the classes?","Yaxshi! Darslar qachon?",69.8],["Receptionist","There's a Monday class and a Thursday class. Monday starts at 6, but Thursday is a little later.","Dushanba va payshanba kunlari dars bor. Dushanba soat 6 da boshlanadi, payshanba esa biroz kechroq.",72.5],["Thomas","Thursday would be better, because I usually work late on Mondays.","Payshanba yaxshiroq, chunki dushanba kunlari odatda kech ishlayman.",80.1],["Receptionist","Fine. The Thursday class starts at 6.45 and lasts an hour and a half.","Mayli. Payshanba darsi 6.45 da boshlanadi va bir yarim soat davom etadi.",84.6],["Thomas","Do I need to buy any equipment?","Biror jihoz sotib olishim kerakmi?",91.2],["Receptionist","No. We provide all the tools and materials. You should bring an old shirt, though, because your clothes may get dirty.","Yoʻq. Barcha asbob va materiallarni oʻzimiz beramiz. Lekin eski koʻylak olib keling, chunki kiyimingiz ifloslanishi mumkin.",93.7],["Thomas","Good idea. How many people are in each class?","Yaxshi fikr. Har bir guruhda necha kishi bor?",101.8],["Receptionist","We allow a maximum of ten, but there are usually about eight. That gives the teacher enough time to help everyone.","Eng koʻpi bilan oʻn kishiga ruxsat beramiz, lekin odatda sakkiz kishi atrofida boʻladi. Bu oʻqituvchiga hammaga yordam berishga yetarli vaqt beradi.",105.8],["Thomas","And how much is the course?","Kurs qancha turadi?",114],["Receptionist","It normally costs £50, but beginners joining this month pay £40 for all four classes.","Odatda 50 funt turadi, lekin shu oy qoʻshilgan yangi boshlovchilar toʻrt darsning hammasi uchun 40 funt toʻlaydi.",116.2],["Thomas","Great! Where is the pottery room?","Zoʻr! Kulolchilik xonasi qayerda?",124.2],["Receptionist","It's upstairs in room seven, opposite the photography room.","U yuqori qavatda, 7-xonada, fotografiya xonasining roʻparasida.",127],["Thomas","Perfect. I'd like to give it a try.","Juda yaxshi. Sinab koʻrmoqchiman.",131.8],["Receptionist","Excellent. I'll reserve a place for you.","Ajoyib. Siz uchun joy band qilib qoʻyaman.",134.7]]},
{"id":"wb-23","u":23,"book":"Workbook","title":"Interesting places and different cultures","dur":134,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-23.mp3","lines":[["Receptionist","Hello. City Exchange Club. How can I help?","Salom. City Exchange Club. Qanday yordam bera olaman?",5.9],["Ben","Hi. I saw some information about your cultural evening next week and I'd like to come.","Salom. Kelasi haftadagi madaniy kechangiz haqida maʼlumot koʻrdim va kelmoqchiman.",9.8],["Receptionist","Great. I can give you all the details. Can I take your name first?","Zoʻr. Hamma maʼlumotni aytib beraman. Avval ismingizni aytsangiz.",16],["Ben","Yes. I'm Ben Carter. Could you spell your surname, please?","Ha. Men Ben Carter. Familiyamni harflab beraymi?",21.4],["Receptionist","Of course. It's C-A-R-T-E-R.","Albatta. C-A-R-T-E-R.",26.2],["Receptionist","Thank you. This month our cultural evening is about Mexico. Last month we looked at Spain, so we wanted to choose somewhere different this time.","Rahmat. Bu oyda madaniy kechamiz Meksika haqida. Oʻtgan oy Ispaniyani koʻrib chiqqandik, shuning uchun bu safar boshqa joyni tanlamoqchi boʻldik.",32.2],["Ben","Nice. I don't know much about Mexico, so it should be interesting.","Yaxshi. Meksika haqida koʻp bilmayman, demak qiziqarli boʻlsa kerak.",42.2],["Receptionist","The evening begins with a short talk by a student who lived there for a year. She'll show photographs of different cities and talk about family life, school and food.","Kecha u yerda bir yil yashagan talabaning qisqa maʼruzasi bilan boshlanadi. U turli shaharlar suratlarini koʻrsatadi va oilaviy hayot, maktab va taomlar haqida gapiradi.",47.2],["Ben","What time does the talk start?","Maʼruza soat nechada boshlanadi?",59.2],["Receptionist","The doors open at 6, but the talk begins at 6.30. Try to arrive a little earlier because it can get busy.","Eshiklar 6 da ochiladi, maʼruza esa 6.30 da boshlanadi. Biroz barvaqtroq kelishga harakat qiling, chunki odam koʻp boʻlishi mumkin.",61.2],["Ben","I will. Is there any food to try?","Albatta. Tatib koʻradigan taom bormi?",69.2],["Receptionist","Yes. After the talk, visitors can try several dishes. One of them is a traditional soup made with vegetables and chicken.","Ha. Maʼruzadan keyin mehmonlar bir nechta taomni tatib koʻrishi mumkin. Ulardan biri sabzavot va tovuqdan tayyorlangan anʼanaviy shoʻrva.",72.2],["Ben","Great! I enjoy trying new food.","Zoʻr! Yangi taomlarni tatib koʻrishni yaxshi koʻraman.",82.9],["Receptionist","Later there'll be a short dance lesson. You don't need any experience and everyone is welcome to join.","Keyinroq qisqa raqs darsi boʻladi. Tajriba shart emas, hamma qoʻshilishi mumkin.",86.4],["Ben","That sounds fun. What should we wear?","Qiziq eshitilyapti. Nima kiyishimiz kerak?",94],["Receptionist","Anything comfortable. If you want to join the dancing, comfortable shoes are especially important.","Istalgan qulay kiyim. Raqsga qoʻshilmoqchi boʻlsangiz, qulay poyabzal ayniqsa muhim.",97.3],["Ben","Good to know. Will there be anything to buy?","Yaxshi, bilib oldim. Sotib olsa boʻladigan narsa bormi?",103.9],["Receptionist","Yes, there'll be a small market with handmade gifts, books and traditional clothes. Some of the students brought the items back from their travels.","Ha, qoʻlda yasalgan sovgʻalar, kitoblar va milliy kiyimlar sotiladigan kichik bozor boʻladi. Buyumlarni baʼzi talabalar sayohatlaridan olib kelgan.",105],["Ben","How much is the event?","Tadbir qancha turadi?",117],["Receptionist","It's £6 for adults. Children under 12 can come for free.","Kattalar uchun 6 funt. 12 yoshgacha bolalar bepul kelishi mumkin.",119],["Ben","Perfect. Where is it being held?","Juda yaxshi. U qayerda oʻtkaziladi?",125],["Receptionist","In the community hall besides Central Library.","Markaziy kutubxona yonidagi jamoat zalida.",128],["Ben","Great, thanks for the information.","Zoʻr, maʼlumot uchun rahmat.",131.4]]},
{"id":"wb-24","u":24,"book":"Workbook","title":"Life in the past and life today","dur":128,"audio":"audio/a2/workbook/unit-24.mp3","lines":[["Host","Welcome back to Life Changes. Today we're talking to people about how their daily lives are different from when they were young. Could you introduce yourself?","Life Changes dasturiga qaytganingiz bilan. Bugun odamlar bilan kundalik hayotlari yoshlik paytlaridan qanday farq qilishi haqida gaplashamiz. Oʻzingizni tanishtirib oʻtasizmi?",6],["Robert","Certainly. My name's Robert James.","Albatta. Mening ismim Robert James.",16],["Host","Could you spell your surname please?","Familiyangizni harflab bera olasizmi?",19.9],["Robert","Of course. It's J-A-M-E-S.","Albatta. J-A-M-E-S.",22.5],["Host","Thanks Robert. Where did you live as a child?","Rahmat, Robert. Bolaligingizda qayerda yashagansiz?",27.7],["Robert","I grew up on a farm about 10 kilometres from the nearest town. It was a quiet place and there weren't many other children living nearby.","Men eng yaqin shahardan taxminan 10 kilometr uzoqlikdagi fermada ulgʻayganman. U tinch joy edi va atrofda boshqa bolalar koʻp yashamasdi.",31.3],["Host","How did you get to school?","Maktabga qanday borardingiz?",40.9],["Robert","A school bus picked us up every morning. I had to leave home at 7.15 because the bus stopped at several villages before reaching the school.","Har ertalab maktab avtobusi bizni olib ketardi. Uydan 7.15 da chiqishim kerak edi, chunki avtobus maktabga yetguncha bir nechta qishloqda toʻxtardi.",43],["Host","What was school like then?","Oʻshanda maktab qanday edi?",52.6],["Robert","We didn't have computers of course. We wrote everything by hand in our notebooks. If we needed information for homework we usually looked in books.","Albatta, kompyuterlarimiz yoʻq edi. Hamma narsani daftarga qoʻlda yozardik. Uy vazifasi uchun maʼlumot kerak boʻlsa, odatda kitoblardan qidirardik.",54.5],["Host","What did you do after school?","Maktabdan keyin nima qilardingiz?",63.4],["Robert","I often helped my parents on the farm. After that I played outside with my brother. We had a television but I was only allowed to watch it for about an hour each evening.","Koʻpincha fermada ota-onamga yordam berardim. Keyin ukam bilan tashqarida oʻynardim. Televizorimiz bor edi, lekin har oqshom uni atigi bir soat atrofida koʻrishga ruxsat berilardi.",65.5],["Host","How did your family do its shopping?","Oilangiz xaridni qanday qilardi?",77.4],["Robert","We drove into town every Saturday. My mother made a long list because we needed enough food for the whole week.","Har shanba shaharga mashinada borardik. Onam uzun roʻyxat tuzardi, chunki butun hafta yetadigan oziq-ovqat kerak edi.",79],["Host","And how is your life different today?","Bugun hayotingiz qanday farq qiladi?",89],["Robert","Well I live in a city now so everything is much closer. I can walk to several shops and I sometimes order food online. Communication is much easier too.","Hozir shaharda yashayman, shuning uchun hamma narsa ancha yaqin. Bir nechta doʻkonga piyoda bora olaman va baʼzan ovqatni onlayn buyurtma qilaman. Muloqot ham ancha oson.",91.7],["Host","Do you use technology a lot?","Texnologiyadan koʻp foydalanasizmi?",103],["Robert","Yes. I use my phone every day for messages, maps, news and even paying for things. When I was young I never imagined one small thing could do all of that.","Ha. Telefonni har kuni xabarlar, xaritalar, yangiliklar va hatto toʻlovlar uchun ishlataman. Yoshligimda bitta kichik narsa bularning hammasini qila oladi deb tasavvur ham qilmagandim.",106],["Host","Is there anything you miss about the past?","Oʻtmishdan sogʻinadigan narsangiz bormi?",117],["Robert","I miss how peaceful life on the farm was but I think modern life is more convenient.","Fermadagi hayotning tinchligini sogʻinaman, lekin zamonaviy hayot qulayroq deb oʻylayman.",121.4]]}
];
